const U_DATA=[{"id":"01","title":"让大学学习有方向","en_title":"Learning with a Purpose","kind":"写作·教育与成长","en":"Initially, many students regard a diploma as their ultimate objective. Yet a qualification is only one component of an education. What matters more is whether learners can interpret a difficult paragraph, formulate a coherent argument, and apply an abstract concept to a realistic situation. A good instructor will therefore encourage a student to question an assumption, clarify a notion, and distinguish an apparent fact from a reasonable inference.\nAt our college, each participant must undertake a small research project. Students first prepare an outline, then develop a hypothesis and gather empirical evidence. They submit a draft to a tutor, who may reject a superficial explanation but will offer constructive counsel. A scholarship rewards persistence and integrity as well as achievement. The dean hopes that this systematic approach will broaden students' intellectual interests. Not only does purposeful study deepen understanding, but it also gives learners the confidence to tackle unfamiliar problems. A university should cultivate independent judgment rather than make perfection its only criterion of success.","zh":"起初，许多学生把文凭看作教育的最终目标。然而，资格证书只是教育的一部分。更重要的是，学习者能否解读难懂的段落、组织连贯的论证，并把抽象概念应用于真实情境。因此，优秀的教师会鼓励学生质疑假设、澄清概念，区分表面事实与合理推断。在我们学校，每位参与者都必须承担一个小型研究项目：先拟提纲，再提出假说并收集实证材料。学生向导师提交初稿，导师可能否定肤浅的解释，但会提供建设性建议。奖学金既奖励成绩，也奖励坚持与诚信。院长希望这种系统的方法拓宽学生的学术兴趣。有目的的学习不仅加深理解，也让学习者有信心处理陌生问题。大学应培养独立判断力，而不应把完美作为成功的唯一标准。","key":"Not only does purposeful study deepen understanding, but it also gives learners the confidence to tackle unfamiliar problems. || not only 置于句首，第一分句部分倒装，but also 后正常语序。迁移：Not only does regular practice improve accuracy, but it also builds confidence.","task":"大学应该鼓励学生质疑假设，而不是简单地接受信息。 || Universities should encourage students to question assumptions rather than simply accept information.","q":"What does the scholarship reward besides achievement? || Persistence and integrity. 文中 as well as 将三项奖励依据并列。","note":"qualification 在本文前半部分指资格；第 04 篇结尾指限制条件。dignity 是名词，原表第 1 页的形容词标注有误。","wc":165,"new":["initially","qualification","can","instructor","coherent","undertake","formulate","scholarship","paragraph","realistic","apparent","question","inference","gather","what","confidence","distinguish","develop","reject","counsel","difficult","abstract","empirical","perfection","interpret","tackle","tutor","persistence","hypothesis","deepen","ultimate","outline","notion","offer","systematic","integrity","participant","assumption","objective","superficial","criterion","diploma","should","situation","dean","broaden"]},{"id":"02","title":"从背词到主动运用","en_title":"From Vocabulary to Communication","kind":"写作·学习方法","en":"A vocabulary notebook is useful only if its owner knows how to use it. Mei used to reproduce a glossary word for word, hoping that mechanical repetition would make her proficient. Her vocabulary grew, but her proficiency in conversation remained limited. Then she began to integrate reading, writing, and oral practice into a daily routine.\nFor each entry, she would note its usage, underline a natural phrase, and compose a short message. She would also consult a handbook when an abbreviation or an obscure expression caused confusion. Instead of treating every translation as literal, she considered the context and the writer's intent. A familiar word could carry a distinctly different meaning in a novel or an editorial. She learnt to modulate her voice, check the vowel sounds, and vary her intonation. She would record a presentation, replay it, and rectify one recurring error at a time. The more actively she used a word, the easier it became to recall. Her progress was gradual, yet the method proved far more productive than an ambitious plan she could not maintain.","zh":"词汇笔记只有在主人知道如何使用时才有价值。梅过去逐字抄写词汇表，希望机械重复能让自己熟练掌握英语。她的词汇量增长了，口语熟练度却仍然有限。后来，她把阅读、写作和口头练习融入日常安排。每个词条，她都记录用法，画出自然搭配，并写一则短信息。遇到缩写或晦涩表达时，她查阅手册。她不再把所有翻译都视为逐字对应，而是考虑语境和作者意图。熟词在小说或社论中可能有明显不同的含义。她学习调节声音、检查元音并改变语调，还会录下自己的发言，重听后每次纠正一个反复出现的错误。一个词用得越主动，回忆起来就越容易。虽然进步缓慢，这种方法却比无法坚持的宏大计划更有效。","key":"The more actively she used a word, the easier it became to recall. || the + 比较级，the + 比较级，表示两个变化相互关联。迁移：The more carefully we plan, the less time we waste.","task":"只有把新词用在具体语境中，我们才能更牢固地记住它们。 || Only when we use new words in specific contexts can we remember them more securely.","q":"Why did Mei change her method? || Her growing vocabulary had not led to comparable progress in conversation. 注意词汇量与运用能力之间的转折。","note":"","wc":178,"new":["check","underline","vowel","intonation","ambitious","obscure","novel","distinctly","usage","literal","entry","modulate","proficient","proficiency","handbook","integrate","productive","editorial","context","routine","message","intent","carry","rectify","presentation","abbreviation","reproduce","glossary","vocabulary"]},{"id":"03","title":"公平不等于同一种支持","en_title":"Fair Access to Education","kind":"写作·教育公平","en":"A college may advertise itself as inclusive, yet its daily arrangements can still create a hindrance for some learners. A compulsory evening workshop, for example, may exclude a student with an unpaid caring role. A steep stairway can hamper access for someone who cannot walk easily. Such barriers are neither insignificant nor inevitable.\nOur student association submitted a petition asking the administration to review attendance rules. Its proposal was straightforward: provide an accessible room, a flexible timetable, and a digital version of each handout. Financial support should be available irrespective of family background, and a modest allowance could help cover transport. One representative argued that equal opportunity did not require identical treatment. Rather, it required an impartial assessment of individual needs. Whoever wished to enroll should receive clear guidance, not a dismissive shrug. The committee agreed to implement the proposal and monitor its outcome. By removing avoidable obstacles, a university can uphold dignity and enable more students to participate fully. Inclusion is a continuing undertaking, not merely a phrase in a public declaration.","zh":"一所大学可能宣传自己具有包容性，但日常安排仍会给部分学习者制造障碍。例如，强制性的晚间研讨课可能让承担无偿照护责任的学生无法参加，陡峭的楼梯也会妨碍行动不便者进入。这些障碍既不微小，也并非不可避免。学生协会提交请愿书，要求校方审查出勤规定，建议提供无障碍教室、灵活时间表和电子讲义。经济援助应不受家庭背景影响，适当补贴也能帮助支付交通费。一名代表指出，机会平等不要求待遇完全一致，而要求公正评估个人需求。任何想报名的人都应该得到清晰指导，而不是被轻蔑地耸肩敷衍。委员会同意实施提案并追踪结果。消除可避免的障碍能维护尊严，让更多学生充分参与。包容是一项持续的事业，不只是公开声明中的一句话。","key":"By removing avoidable obstacles, a university can uphold dignity and enable more students to participate fully. || By + 动名词交代实现目标的方法；enable sb. to do 表示使某人能够做。适合提出建议的作文结尾。","task":"公平的制度应该回应个人需求，而不是假设所有人都面临同样的困难。 || A fair system should respond to individual needs rather than assume that everyone faces the same difficulties.","q":"Why might identical treatment be unfair? || Students have different needs and face different barriers. 答案来自代表对 equal opportunity 的解释。","note":"","wc":173,"new":["dignity","workshop","hindrance","declaration","insignificant","unpaid","identical","advertise","individual","handout","undertaking","petition","compulsory","stairway","flexible","straightforward","uphold","administration","whoever","support","version","outcome","assessment","impartial","implement","hamper","enroll","attendance","representative","participate","irrespective","inclusive","shrug","allowance"]},{"id":"04","title":"一次校园调查能说明什么","en_title":"What a Survey Can Tell Us","kind":"阅读·数据与判断","en":"A popular claim on campus was that online courses would inevitably improve learning. To examine its validity, a research team designed a questionnaire and selected a random sample. The students recorded each response without changing an inconvenient datum. They distinguished quantitative measures, such as study hours, from qualitative observations about motivation.\nThe initial statistics showed a positive correlation between regular attendance and examination performance. However, a correlation did not establish a cause. A learner's prior knowledge might influence both variables. Nor was the sample homogeneous: a junior student could have different priorities from someone approaching graduation. The team therefore refused to generalize too quickly. A numerical coefficient offered useful information, but its interpretation required caution. An analytic approach, or an analytical one, involves examining how separate factors interact. The final report described the study's scope, identified a possible flaw, and acknowledged that some conclusions remained uncertain. Only by reporting limitations openly could the researchers make their recommendation credible. The exercise taught them that an honest qualification strengthens an argument instead of making it worthless.","zh":"校园里有一种流行说法：在线课程必然改善学习。为检验其有效性，一个研究团队设计问卷并随机抽样。学生如实记录每个回答，不修改不符合预期的数据。他们区分学习时长等定量指标与关于动机的定性观察。初步统计显示，规律出勤与考试成绩正相关，但相关性并不能证明因果关系，已有知识可能同时影响这两个变量。样本也不是同质的：低年级学生与即将毕业者可能有不同的优先事项。因此，团队拒绝过早概括。数值系数提供信息，但解读时需要谨慎。分析性方法意味着考察不同因素如何相互作用。最终报告交代研究范围、指出潜在缺陷，并承认某些结论仍不确定。只有公开报告局限，研究建议才可信。这让学生明白，诚实地给结论加上限制条件，反而能增强论证。","key":"Only by reporting limitations openly could the researchers make their recommendation credible. || Only + 状语置于句首，主句部分倒装；make + 宾语 + 形容词。不要把 only 修饰主语时也机械倒装。","task":"相关性可以提供线索，却不能单独证明因果关系。 || A correlation can provide a clue, but it cannot by itself establish a causal relationship.","q":"Why did the team avoid a broad generalization? || The sample was not homogeneous, and other factors could explain the correlation. 两个限制共同削弱简单的因果结论。","note":"analytic / analytical 都表示分析的。datum 是 data 的单数形式；本文作为可数单个数据使用。","wc":174,"new":["datum","qualitative","positive","validity","scope","team","coefficient","caution","correlation","interact","recommendation","statistics","homogeneous","questionnaire","random","numerical","influence","establish","claim","flaw","junior","quantitative","response","generalize","analytic","between","initial","report","inevitably","uncertain"]},{"id":"05","title":"在挫折之后继续学习","en_title":"Progress after a Setback","kind":"写作·心理与成长","en":"After a disappointing interview, Jun felt that one failure would determine his destiny. He began to brood over every awkward answer and dread the next opportunity. A friend could not remove his sorrow, but she could offer companionship and a realistic perspective. She reminded him that a momentary setback did not signify permanent incapacity.\nJun decided to confront the problem in manageable steps. He would rehearse a concise introduction, identify one strength, and ask for specific feedback. He tried not to overestimate a competitor or underestimate himself. When nervousness made him stammer, he paused instead of rushing headlong into another sentence. His tutor praised his willingness to persevere, not a faultless performance. Gradually, his bitterness gave way to cautious optimism. What helped him most was the realization that confidence could develop through action. He did not suddenly become fearless, nor did every difficulty disappear. Nevertheless, he learnt to treat uncertainty as something he could work with. A steady effort, supported by patient encouragement, was more valuable than an empty assurance of instant success.","zh":"一次不理想的面试后，俊觉得一次失败就会决定命运。他反复想着每个尴尬的回答，并害怕下一次机会。朋友无法消除他的难过，却能陪伴他，帮助他更客观地看问题：短暂挫折并不意味着永久无能。俊决定分步骤应对问题，练习简洁的自我介绍，找出一个优势，并寻求具体反馈。他既不过分高估竞争者，也不低估自己。紧张得结巴时，他会停顿，而不是一头冲进下一句话。导师称赞他的坚持意愿，而不是要求完美表现。渐渐地，苦涩变成了谨慎的乐观。最有帮助的是，他认识到信心能通过行动培养。他没有突然无所畏惧，困难也没有全部消失，但他学会了与不确定性共处。有耐心鼓励支撑的持续努力，比空洞的速成保证更有价值。","key":"What helped him most was the realization that confidence could develop through action. || what 引导主语从句；that 引导 realization 的同位语从句，解释具体认识。迁移：What matters most is the belief that effort can make a difference.","task":"一次失败并不意味着一个人缺乏取得进步的能力。 || A single failure does not mean that a person lacks the ability to make progress.","q":"How did Jun respond when he started to stammer? || He paused instead of rushing into another sentence. 留意行为变化，而不是把进步误解为紧张完全消失。","note":"","wc":173,"new":["action","way","over","through","cautious","fearless","faultless","momentary","confront","destiny","optimism","bitterness","stammer","competitor","interview","steady","persevere","overestimate","valuable","answer","underestimate","brood","awkward","strength","signify","assurance","realization","headlong"]},{"id":"06","title":"图书馆的安静不是冷漠","en_title":"A Library for Everyone","kind":"听力·校园服务","en":"Librarian: We plan to convert the old reading room into a shared study area. Before we proceed, I would like to hear your main concern.\nStudent: The current room is tranquil, which helps me concentrate. If people can chatter freely, its value will decline.\nLibrarian: We agree that silence is essential. Our proposal is to install a movable partition. The outermost section will remain a quiet zone, while the interior will house small discussion groups.\nStudent: Will there be enough stationery and power sockets? Some desks are in poor condition, and a broken fastener makes one chair unstable.\nLibrarian: Maintenance staff will mend the furniture. We also intend to update the catalogue and simplify the subscription process for electronic journals.\nStudent: That sounds sensible. Could you notify users beforehand and display an outline at the entry?\nLibrarian: Certainly. We will circulate a bulletin and invite further comments. Provided that the arrangement works satisfactorily, we will retain it next term. A library should respond to changing needs without abandoning the qualities its users cherish.","zh":"图书管理员：我们计划把旧阅览室改成共享学习区。在推进前，我想听听你最关心的问题。学生：现在的房间很安静，有助于集中注意力。如果大家随意聊天，它的价值就会下降。管理员：我们同意安静至关重要。方案是安装可移动隔断，最外侧保留为安静区，内部安排小组讨论。学生：文具和电源插座够吗？有些桌子状态不好，一把椅子的扣件坏了，坐着不稳。管理员：维修人员会修好家具。我们还打算更新目录，简化电子期刊订阅流程。学生：听起来合理。能否提前通知，并在入口展示方案概要？管理员：当然。我们会发布公告，征求进一步意见。如果安排运行良好，下学期就保留。图书馆应回应变化的需求，同时保留使用者珍视的品质。","key":"Provided that the arrangement works satisfactorily, we will retain it next term. || provided that 表示“只要／如果”，引导条件状语从句；谈将来时从句通常用一般现在时。","task":"只要提前通知用户，新安排就更容易被接受。 || Provided that users are notified beforehand, the new arrangement will be easier to accept.","q":"How will the library accommodate both silent study and discussion? || It will install a movable partition and create separate zones. 原方案并非让整间阅览室自由聊天。","note":"","wc":173,"new":["outermost","value","main","convert","cherish","further","satisfactorily","subscription","beforehand","house","decline","stationery","catalogue","notify","essential","concern","section","tranquil","interior","sensible","fastener","mend","maintenance","partition","concentrate","chatter","bulletin"]},{"id":"07","title":"让数字工具真正节省时间","en_title":"Technology That Saves Time","kind":"写作·数字生活","en":"A software developer offered to automate our volunteer registration system. Previously, an attendant had to copy each paper form, insert the information into a directory, and check for a duplicate. The process was tiresome, and a simple mistake could leave a name absent from the final list.\nThe new interface allowed users to edit an entry and receive instantaneous confirmation. A compact program would standardize the format, flag incomplete fields, and interconnect the membership records with the timetable. Its designer was careful not to overload the screen with every conceivable option. A clear heading, a visible help button, and a plain explanation of each step made the system easier to comprehend.\nYet efficiency was not the only consideration. A technical breakdown could paralyse registration, so the team kept a backup procedure. They also restricted access to confidential information and tested whether the system was compatible with older devices. Useful innovation begins with a genuine need. Unless a digital service is reliable and understandable, its sophistication may become a burden rather than an advantage.","zh":"一位软件开发者提出，把我们的志愿者登记系统自动化。过去，工作人员必须抄写纸质表格，把信息录入名录，再检查重复项。流程枯燥，一个小错误就可能让某人的名字从最终名单中消失。新界面允许用户修改条目并立即收到确认。一个小型程序能统一格式、标记不完整字段，并将会员记录与时间表连接起来。设计者避免把所有可能的选项都塞进屏幕。清晰的标题、显眼的帮助按钮和直白的步骤说明让系统更容易理解。但效率不是唯一考虑。技术故障可能使登记瘫痪，因此团队保留备用流程，也限制机密信息访问，并测试旧设备兼容性。有价值的创新始于真实需求。如果数字服务不可靠、难理解，其复杂性反而可能成为负担。","key":"Unless a digital service is reliable and understandable, its sophistication may become a burden rather than an advantage. || unless 表示“除非／如果不”；rather than 连接平行名词，突出取舍。","task":"技术应该简化日常工作，同时保护用户的个人信息。 || Technology should simplify routine work while protecting users' personal information.","q":"Why did the team keep a backup procedure? || A technical breakdown could stop registration. 备用流程对应可靠性，而非界面美观。","note":"","wc":173,"new":["volunteer","confirmation","paper","compatible","option","directory","plain","instantaneous","attendant","automate","standardize","paralyse","tiresome","interconnect","overload","confidential","comprehend","compact","duplicate","interface","simple","innovation","membership","absent","incomplete","heading","program","edit","breakdown","software","insert"]},{"id":"08","title":"网络信息与事实核查","en_title":"Before You Share a Claim","kind":"写作·媒介素养","en":"A dramatic video can spread across a network before anybody examines its origin. A shadowy account may distort an incident, attach a false caption, and provoke indignation. When a striking image confirms our existing opinion, the impulse to share it can be overwhelming. Nevertheless, popularity is not evidence of accuracy.\nOur journalism workshop taught a practical sequence. First, identify the original author and the date of publication. Next, compare the report with independent accounts. Finally, ask whether a missing detail could alter the interpretation. We learnt to distinguish a documented occurrence from gossip, an imitation from an authentic recording, and criticism from slander. A responsible editor must not fabricate testimony or disguise a sham interview as factual reporting.\nHad the first readers paused to check the source, the rumour might not have spread so widely. Verification can seem slow, particularly during a crisis, but an inaccurate message can magnify fear. The aim is neither to suppress disagreement nor to censor every unusual opinion. It is to make public discussion more informed, rational, and accountable.","zh":"一段戏剧性的视频可能在任何人核查来源之前就传遍网络。身份不明的账号可能歪曲事件、添加虚假说明，激起愤怒。当醒目图片证实我们已有观点时，分享冲动可能格外强烈。然而，流行并不是准确性的证据。新闻研讨课教了一套实用流程：先确认原作者和发布日期，再与独立报道比较，最后检查是否有遗漏细节会改变解读。我们学习区分有记录的事件与流言、仿制品与真实录音，以及批评与诽谤。负责的编辑不能编造证言，也不能把假采访包装成事实报道。如果最早的读者停下来查证，谣言可能就不会传播得如此广泛。尤其在危机期间，核实显得缓慢，但错误信息会放大恐惧。目标不是压制分歧或审查一切不同寻常的意见，而是让公共讨论更知情、理性并对言论负责。","key":"Had the first readers paused to check the source, the rumour might not have spread so widely. || 过去反事实条件句，省略 if 后将 had 提前；主句 might have + 过去分词。只用于与过去事实相反或假设的情况。","task":"一条消息越令人震惊，我们就越应该仔细核查其来源。 || The more shocking a message is, the more carefully we should verify its source.","q":"Does the workshop recommend suppressing all disagreement? || No. It recommends checking evidence so that discussion becomes better informed. 末段明确区分核实事实与压制意见。","note":"","wc":174,"new":["anybody","responsible","fabricate","suppress","shadowy","overwhelming","sequence","striking","gossip","crisis","network","distort","rational","impulse","popularity","detail","occurrence","censor","video","sham","indignation","imitation","magnify","provoke","widely","author","disagreement","inaccurate","slander"]},{"id":"09","title":"人工智能与人的责任","en_title":"Human Judgment in an Automated World","kind":"写作·科技伦理","en":"A laboratory introduced a virtual assistant to summarize research papers. It could scan a manuscript, extract a theme, and generate a brief exposition within seconds. For a busy researcher, the potential gain in productivity was substantial. The tool could also classify material by category and reveal a pattern that a reader might overlook.\nHowever, an elegant summary could still contain a blunder. The assistant might invent a reference, confuse a theory with a proven theorem, or confidently assert something unsupported. A polished tone was no guarantee of sound reasoning. Consequently, the laboratory required a human review before any generated passage entered a formal report. Researchers had to ascertain whether each citation existed and whether it supported the associated claim.\nAs useful as automation can be, responsibility remains with the people who deploy it. A sophisticated mechanism can facilitate analysis; it cannot justify careless judgment. The team's guiding principle was to preserve human oversight while using technology to lessen repetitive work. They measured success by dependable results, not by the mere rapidity of a response.","zh":"一家实验室引入虚拟助手来概括研究论文。它能扫描稿件、提取主题，并在几秒内生成简短说明。对忙碌的研究者来说，生产率提升的潜力很大。工具还能给材料分类，找出读者可能忽略的规律。但优雅的摘要仍可能包含严重错误：助手可能编造文献，把理论与已证明的定理混淆，或自信地断言没有依据的内容。成熟的语气并不保证推理可靠。因此，实验室要求生成文本进入正式报告前必须经过人工审核，研究者必须查明每条引文是否存在、是否支持相应论点。无论自动化多么有用，责任仍属于使用它的人。复杂机制能协助分析，却不能为草率判断提供理由。团队坚持保留人工监督，用技术减少重复劳动，并以结果是否可靠，而不是仅以回复速度评价成功。","key":"As useful as automation can be, responsibility remains with the people who deploy it. || As + 形容词 + as + 主语 + 谓语，表达“尽管……”，后接让步的主句；who 引导定语从句。","task":"无论工具多么先进，使用者仍然有责任核实结果。 || However advanced a tool may be, its users remain responsible for verifying the results.","q":"How did the laboratory evaluate success? || By dependable results, not merely by the speed of a response. 题目考查评价标准。","note":"","wc":174,"new":["category","formal","substantial","overlook","theme","exposition","manuscript","facilitate","virtual","productivity","tone","scan","extract","sophisticated","rapidity","theory","lessen","mechanism","reveal","summary","pattern","blunder","generate","assert","theorem","ascertain","reference","elegant"]},{"id":"10","title":"第一份工作的选择","en_title":"Choosing a First Job","kind":"听力·就业与职业规划","en":"Adviser: You have an offer from a large enterprise and another from a small design studio. Which one appeals to you?\nGraduate: The first pays more, but the second seems to suit my vocation. I could collaborate directly with an experienced architect.\nAdviser: Compare the whole arrangement. Ask about training, working hours, promotion, and the obligation you would accept. A prestigious brand does not automatically provide a supportive workplace.\nGraduate: The executive at the smaller firm was courteous. She gave an explicit description of my role and said I would initially be subordinate to a project manager.\nAdviser: That clarity is valuable. You should also check the contract before you sign. Is the promised salary fixed? Can you resign with reasonable notice? Will the employer compensate you for necessary travel?\nGraduate: I will request written confirmation. I do not want to choose purely for prestige or make a reckless commitment.\nAdviser: Exactly. Rather than seek an ideal position in every respect, identify your priority and consider the trade-off. A prudent decision balances present needs with opportunities for future development.","zh":"顾问：你收到了大企业和小设计工作室的录用通知。哪一个更吸引你？毕业生：第一份薪水更高，但第二份似乎更符合我的职业志向，我能直接与经验丰富的建筑师合作。顾问：要比较完整安排，询问培训、工时、晋升以及你要承担的义务。知名品牌不一定提供支持性的工作环境。毕业生：小公司的主管很有礼貌，明确说明了我的职责，说我起初归项目经理管理。顾问：职责清晰很重要。签约前也要核实合同：承诺的工资是否固定？能否在合理提前通知后辞职？必要差旅是否报销？毕业生：我会要求书面确认。我不想纯粹为声望选择，也不想鲁莽承诺。顾问：对。与其寻求各方面都理想的职位，不如确定优先事项并考虑取舍。审慎的决定会平衡当前需要和未来发展机会。","key":"Rather than seek an ideal position in every respect, identify your priority and consider the trade-off. || Rather than + 动词原形置前，与祈使句构成取舍建议；避免把 trade-off 误解为商业交易。","task":"选择工作时，我们不仅要考虑收入，也要考虑成长机会。 || When choosing a job, we should consider opportunities for growth as well as income.","q":"What will the graduate do before making a commitment? || Request written confirmation and check the contract. 顾问的建议引出了毕业生下一步的行动。","note":"","wc":179,"new":["trade","executive","position","vocation","second","sign","brand","courteous","obligation","collaborate","priority","subordinate","prestige","resign","suit","explicit","prudent","architect","enterprise","studio","promotion","reckless","compensate"]},{"id":"11","title":"一家修理铺的创业课","en_title":"A Repair Shop's First Year","kind":"写作·创业与社区经济","en":"When Lin decided to lease a small shop, a banker asked whether her business model was profitable. Lin did not promise unlimited growth. She planned to repair domestic appliances, sell second-hand equipment, and cater to residents who preferred maintenance to replacement. Her budget included rent, a modest wage, and a reserve for unexpected expenditure.\nThe first quarter brought little revenue. A shipment of spare parts arrived late, and one client refused to pay an invoice. Rather than conceal the problem, Lin negotiated a new delivery schedule and kept an accurate log of each transaction. She learnt to distinguish cash in the bank from actual earnings. A temporary surplus could vanish if an overlooked liability became due.\nBy the end of the year, customers began to recommend the shop. Its margin remained slim, but its reputation for fair treatment grew. Lin's experience illustrates a practical lesson: commercial survival depends not only on ingenuity but also on reliable service, careful finance, and the willingness to acknowledge a mistake promptly.","zh":"林决定租一间小店时，一位银行从业者问她的商业模式是否盈利。她没有承诺无限增长，而计划修理家用电器、出售二手设备，服务那些愿意维修而非更换物品的居民。预算包括房租、适当工资，以及应对意外支出的储备。第一季度收入不多，一批零件到货延迟，还有客户拒付发票。林没有隐瞒，而是协商新的交货安排，并准确记录每笔交易。她学会区分银行现金与真正收益：一笔被忽略的债务到期，就可能让临时盈余消失。年底，客户开始推荐这家店。利润仍薄，但公平待客的口碑逐渐增长。她的经历说明，商业生存不仅取决于巧思，也取决于可靠服务、谨慎的财务管理，以及及时承认错误的意愿。","key":"Commercial survival depends not only on ingenuity but also on reliable service, careful finance, and the willingness to acknowledge a mistake promptly. || not only ... but also ... 位于句中无需倒装；并列项在语法上保持一致。","task":"稳定的收入不能替代对成本和风险的谨慎管理。 || A steady income cannot replace careful management of costs and risks.","q":"Why could the temporary surplus disappear? || An overlooked liability might become due. 注意区分手头现金与扣除义务后的财务状况。","note":"","wc":167,"new":["lease","shipment","liability","budget","margin","profitable","cater","banker","domestic","survival","slim","unlimited","finance","revenue","late","end","promptly","fair","second-hand","reserve","ingenuity","log","surplus","replacement","client","earnings","invoice","transaction","acknowledge","bank","expenditure"]},{"id":"12","title":"理性消费的日常练习","en_title":"Buying with a Clear Purpose","kind":"写作·消费与可持续生活","en":"An advertisement offered a gorgeous jacket at a huge discount. The material resembled velvet, and the lining felt wonderfully soft. I was tempted to buy it immediately, although my wardrobe already contained several similar garments. The promise of a bargain had briefly displaced a more basic question: did I need it?\nA consumer can resist this impulse by considering use, quality, and total cost. An attractive accessory is not necessarily essential, and a fashionable novelty may soon lose its charm. Buying an item in installments does not make it cheaper; it only changes the timing of payment. Nor should a complimentary token distract us from an unreasonable price.\nI left the store and reviewed my spending. The exercise was not about becoming a miser or rejecting every pleasure. It was about ensuring that consumption reflected my priorities. I eventually bought a sturdy coat that I could mend easily. Had I followed the initial excitement, I would have purchased something less suitable. A deliberate pause can transform shopping from a reflex into a considered choice.","zh":"一则广告宣传一件漂亮夹克大幅打折。面料像天鹅绒，衬里十分柔软。尽管衣柜里已有几件相似衣服，我还是差点立刻购买。便宜的诱惑暂时挤走了更基本的问题：我需要它吗？消费者可以通过考虑用途、质量和总成本抵制冲动。好看的配饰未必必需，时尚新品也可能很快失去魅力。分期付款不会降低价格，只改变付款时间。我们也不应被免费赠品吸引，忽视不合理的价格。我离开商店并检查支出。这样做不是要变成守财奴或拒绝所有乐趣，而是确保消费符合优先事项。最后，我买了一件结实且易于修补的外套。如果跟着最初的兴奋走，我就会买到不合适的东西。刻意停顿能让购物从本能反应变成经过考虑的选择。","key":"Nor should a complimentary token distract us from an unreasonable price. || 否定副词 nor 置于句首，助动词或情态动词提前；distract sb. from sth. 为固定搭配。","task":"分期付款改变的是付款时间，而不是商品的总成本。 || Paying in installments changes the timing of payment rather than the total cost of an item.","q":"What did the narrator eventually buy? || A sturdy coat that was easy to mend. 最终选择依据实用性，不是广告中的夹克。","note":"","wc":174,"new":["discount","wardrobe","gorgeous","novelty","consumption","consumer","token","accessory","velvet","miser","deliberate","choice","charm","sturdy","distract","unreasonable","transform","lining"]},{"id":"13","title":"老街里的传统手艺","en_title":"Craft in an Old Town","kind":"翻译·传统文化","en":"In a tranquil town beside a river, a weaver still works at a wooden loom. A strip of cloth gradually becomes a decorative panel, its delicate pattern recalling the bamboo and willow along the bank. Nearby, an artisan shapes earthenware, while another adds a fine glaze to porcelain. Visitors can watch a demonstration, purchase a modest ornament, or attend a workshop on embroidery.\nThe town was formerly known principally for trade. Today, its historic quarter attracts people who wish to understand the relationship between craft and everyday life. An old warehouse has become an exhibition hall. There, a bronze utensil stands alongside a carved wooden box and an antique piece of jewellery. Each object carries evidence of practical skill as well as aesthetic judgment.\nPreserving such a place requires more than an elegant facade. Unless young people can earn a reasonable living from their work, traditional knowledge may gradually disappear. By combining training with sustainable tourism, the community hopes to keep its heritage alive. What deserves appreciation is not simply the finished product, but the patience and experience embodied in its making.","zh":"在河边一座宁静的小镇，一名织工仍使用木织机。一条布逐渐织成装饰面板，精细图案让人想到河岸的竹子和柳树。附近有人制作陶器，也有人为瓷器施上细釉。游客能观看演示、购买朴素饰品，或参加刺绣体验课。小镇从前主要以贸易闻名，如今，历史街区吸引人们了解手艺与日常生活的关系。旧仓库变成展厅，青铜器具与雕花木盒、古董珠宝并列陈列。每件物品都展示实用技能与审美判断。保护这样的地方不能只靠漂亮外观。如果年轻人无法凭手艺获得合理收入，传统知识就可能逐渐消失。社区希望通过结合培训与可持续旅游，让遗产延续。值得欣赏的不只是成品，还有制作过程中体现的耐心和经验。","key":"What deserves appreciation is not simply the finished product, but the patience and experience embodied in its making. || what 主语从句突出评价对象；embodied in ... 为过去分词短语作后置定语。","task":"这座小镇通过把传统手艺与现代生活相结合，保护了独特的文化遗产。 || By combining traditional crafts with modern life, the town has preserved its unique cultural heritage.","q":"Why is a reasonable income important for preservation? || It makes it possible for young people to continue the craft. 保护措施需要解决传承者的生计问题。","note":"","wc":182,"new":["ornament","decorative","principally","bamboo","jewellery","weaver","strip","alongside","formerly","embroidery","appreciation","earthenware","bronze","utensil","box","willow","historic","craft","antique","porcelain","warehouse","panel"]},{"id":"14","title":"一座花园的文化表达","en_title":"A Garden Built for Reflection","kind":"翻译·园林与城市文化","en":"Our guide asked us to pause beneath an arch before entering the garden. Through a circular opening, we could see a small pond, an ornamental rock, and the slender stem of a flowering shrub. The view appeared natural, yet its composition had been carefully planned. A winding footpath encouraged visitors to stroll slowly instead of heading directly towards the exit.\nOn a terrace stood a pavilion with a tiled roof. Its lattice windows framed changing views of the landscape. A vine climbed beside the doorway, while a fragrant herb grew near a patch of moss. At twilight, a faint gleam on the water made the surrounding buildings seem unusually distant. The pond could mirror the sky, but a single ripple would alter the reflection.\nRather than overwhelm visitors with grandeur, the garden invited quiet observation. Its appeal lay in the balance between enclosure and openness, detail and space. Even a miniature garden can reveal a thoughtful conception of how people might reside alongside nature. For a hurried urban resident, such a place offers a valuable opportunity to slow down and reflect.","zh":"进入花园前，导游请我们在拱门下停步。透过圆形开口，可以看到池塘、观赏石和开花灌木的细茎。景色看似自然，构图却经过精心规划。弯曲小径鼓励游客慢慢散步，而不是直奔出口。台地上的亭子盖着瓦顶，格窗框出不断变化的景观。藤蔓爬在门边，苔藓旁长着芳香草本植物。黄昏时，水上微光让周围建筑显得格外遥远。池水能映照天空，但一道涟漪就会改变倒影。花园没有用宏伟气势压倒游客，而是邀请人静静观察。其吸引力在于封闭与开阔、细节与空间之间的平衡。即使微型园林，也能展现人如何与自然相处的深思。对匆忙的城市居民而言，这样的地方提供了放慢脚步、反思生活的宝贵机会。","key":"Through a circular opening, we could see a small pond, an ornamental rock, and the slender stem of a flowering shrub. || 方位短语前置构建空间视角；三个平行名词短语组织景物描写，适合园林类翻译。","task":"蜿蜒的小路和精巧的窗户，让游客从不同角度欣赏园林。 || Winding paths and delicate windows allow visitors to appreciate the garden from different angles.","q":"What kind of experience does the garden encourage? || Slow, quiet observation and reflection. 看景物描写如何服务于慢下来的主题。","note":"","wc":181,"new":["composition","ornamental","observation","overwhelm","footpath","fragrant","towards","enclosure","gleam","even","moss","miniature","stroll","terrace","vine","ripple","twilight","winding","reside","shrub","arch","lattice","conception","landscape","mirror","stem","circular","resident","herb"]},{"id":"15","title":"节庆晚宴与文化交流","en_title":"An Evening of Shared Traditions","kind":"听力·文化交流","en":"For the anniversary of our international club, we arranged a banquet in the college hall. The hostess welcomed each guest with warmth, and volunteers set a napkin beside every plate. A small orchestra played a familiar melody as people began to dine. The meal included a mild vegetable stew, steamed fish, and a pumpkin dessert. A fragrant spice gave the food a distinctive flavour without overwhelming it.\nDuring dinner, a student described Thanksgiving as a family occasion in her community. Another explained a local harvest custom. Nobody was asked to represent an entire culture. Instead, each speaker offered a personal memory: a grandfather's proverb, a childhood song, or the sweetness of a favourite dish. Their stories revealed both difference and resemblance.\nAfter the meal, a brief concert brought everyone together. We sang the chorus of a simple song and thanked the cooks with hearty applause. Cultural exchange becomes meaningful when curiosity is joined by courtesy. By listening without making a hasty generalization, we can appreciate another person's experience while retaining the freedom to describe our own.","zh":"国际社团周年纪念时，我们在学校礼堂举办晚宴。女主人热情欢迎来宾，志愿者在每个餐盘旁放上餐巾。大家开始用餐时，小乐团演奏熟悉的旋律。食物有味道温和的蔬菜炖菜、清蒸鱼和南瓜甜点，一种芳香调料增添特色而不喧宾夺主。席间，一名学生讲述她所在社区把感恩节当作家庭团聚日，另一人介绍当地收获习俗。没有人被要求代表整种文化，每个人只是分享私人记忆：祖父的一句谚语、儿时歌曲，或喜爱食物的甜味。故事既呈现差异，也展现相似。饭后的短音乐会把大家聚到一起，我们合唱简单歌曲的副歌，用热烈掌声感谢厨师。当好奇与礼貌相伴，文化交流才有意义。倾听时不仓促概括，就能欣赏别人的经历，也保有讲述自身经历的自由。","key":"Cultural exchange becomes meaningful when curiosity is joined by courtesy. || when 从句说明产生结果的条件；抽象名词作主语使文化类作文简洁自然。","task":"尊重文化差异并不意味着一个人必须放弃自己的传统。 || Respecting cultural differences does not mean that a person must abandon their own traditions.","q":"Were students expected to speak for an entire culture? || No. Each speaker shared a personal memory. 这是晚宴交流方式的核心区别。","note":"","wc":176,"new":["anniversary","hearty","concert","generalization","banquet","proverb","melody","spice","resemblance","sweetness","dessert","hostess","pumpkin","courtesy","set","applause","custom","orchestra","flavour","Thanksgiving","stew","dine","napkin","mild","chorus"]},{"id":"16","title":"博物馆如何讲述历史","en_title":"Reading Objects in a Museum","kind":"阅读·历史与证据","en":"A museum display showed an Egyptian sculpture beside a Roman coin. Nearby stood a model of a medieval fortress, complete with a tower, a gate, and a defensive trench. The labels described the reign of a monarch, the privileges of a duke and a baron, and the daily work of an ordinary tradesman. A historian explained that a grand monument might glorify a conqueror while revealing little about those who built it.\nThe next section examined colonial expansion. It distinguished the account of a colonist from the memory preserved by a descendant of a displaced community. A military victory, the guide observed, could be followed by exile, loss, and a profound change in social life. An exhibit should not erase that complexity.\nSeen in context, an object can illuminate more than its maker's skill. It can also reveal who possessed authority and whose labour remained largely invisible. The museum invited visitors to compare sources, question a triumphant narration, and consider the people missing from it. History becomes more informative when admiration is accompanied by careful inquiry.","zh":"博物馆把埃及雕塑与罗马硬币并列展示。附近是中世纪堡垒模型，包括塔楼、大门和防御壕沟。说明牌介绍君主统治、公爵与男爵的特权，以及普通工匠的日常工作。历史学者解释，宏伟纪念碑可能歌颂征服者，却很少呈现建造者的生活。下一区域讨论殖民扩张，区分殖民者的叙述与被迫迁移社区后裔保存的记忆。导游指出，军事胜利之后可能出现流放、损失和社会生活的深刻变化，展览不应抹去这些复杂性。把物品置于语境中，看到的不仅是制作者的技艺，也能看出谁掌握权力、谁的劳动长期被忽略。博物馆邀请游客比较资料、质疑胜利者的叙述，并考虑其中缺席的人。当欣赏伴随认真探究时，历史才更能提供启发。","key":"Seen in context, an object can illuminate more than its maker's skill. || 过去分词短语作状语，逻辑主语应与主句的 an object 一致；相当于 When it is seen in context。","task":"博物馆不仅展示珍贵物品，也帮助公众理解普通人的生活。 || Museums not only display valuable objects but also help the public understand ordinary people's lives.","q":"Why should visitors compare different historical sources? || One account may glorify powerful people and omit the experiences of others. 答案由征服者与建造者、殖民者与后裔两组对照支撑。","note":"","wc":176,"new":["descendant","coin","colonial","conqueror","illuminate","glorify","colonist","narration","profound","trench","tradesman","admiration","baron","Roman","exile","historian","monarch","duke","tower","complexity","sculpture","triumphant","largely","reign","fortress","Egyptian"]},{"id":"17","title":"音乐让社区相遇","en_title":"Music in a Shared Space","kind":"听力·艺术与公益","en":"The community theatre had been empty for years when a retired composer offered to revive it. He proposed a weekly rehearsal open to both an amateur and a trained musician. Someone donated a second-hand piano; another lent a harp and a guitar. An old gramophone in the lobby reminded visitors how people had listened to music before digital recording.\nAt first, the performers struggled to coordinate. A singer would miss an entry, a player would strike the wrong chord, and the group would lose the rhythm. The conductor resisted the urge to rebuke them harshly. Instead, she asked them to listen to one another and repeat a short sequence. The improvement was gradual but appreciable.\nOn opening night, a solo performance was followed by a short symphony. The audience began to applaud before the final note had faded. It was not technical superiority that made the evening memorable, but the devotion shared by people of different ages. The project demonstrated how participation in the arts can foster fellowship and give an overlooked public space a new purpose.","zh":"社区剧院空置多年后，一位退休作曲家提出让它重新活跃起来，每周组织排练，向业余爱好者与专业乐手开放。有人捐赠二手钢琴，有人借出竖琴和吉他。大厅里的老式留声机让游客想起数字录音之前的听乐方式。起初，表演者难以协调：歌手错过进入时机，乐手弹错和弦，大家失去节奏。指挥克制住严厉责备的冲动，而是请大家彼此倾听，反复练习一小段。进步虽然缓慢，却很明显。首演夜，独奏之后是一首短交响曲，最后一个音还没消失，观众就开始鼓掌。使夜晚难忘的不是技艺高人一等，而是不同年龄者共享的投入。这个项目说明，参与艺术能够促进情谊，赋予被忽略的公共空间新的用途。","key":"It was not technical superiority that made the evening memorable, but the devotion shared by people of different ages. || It was ... that ... 强调句突出原因；not ... but ... 形成平行对比。可迁移为强调合作而非个人天赋。","task":"艺术活动能把不同年龄的人聚在一起，并增强社区归属感。 || Artistic activities can bring together people of different ages and strengthen their sense of belonging to the community.","q":"How did the conductor respond to early mistakes? || She encouraged listening and repeated practice instead of harsh criticism. 留意实际指导方式。","note":"","wc":177,"new":["composer","rebuke","audience","superiority","amateur","foster","devotion","theatre","coordinate","harp","lobby","gramophone","appreciable","symphony","guitar","fellowship","applaud","solo","chord","urge","revive"]},{"id":"18","title":"城市更新应当保留什么","en_title":"Renewal without Erasure","kind":"写作·城市发展","en":"A metropolitan district planned to replace an old market with a skyscraper. The developer praised the scheme as a way to increase retail space and municipal revenue. Residents, however, feared that the new complex would displace small traders and weaken the neighbourhood's character. Their objection was not simply an attachment to the past.\nThe market provided inexpensive food, informal employment, and a place where elderly residents could meet. Its narrow lanes were shabby, but they supported a lively network of relationships. An architect suggested a more flexible option: reinforce the structure, improve drainage, and convert the upper floor into a spacious community centre. The plan would preserve the street's scale while improving its safety.\nAfter a public forum, the council agreed to assess both proposals. It asked for a transparent account of cost, environmental impact, and the likelihood of disruption. Urban renewal should not be judged solely by the height of a building. To be sustainable, it must reconcile economic development with the practical needs of the people who already dwell there.","zh":"一个大城市街区计划用摩天楼替换老市场。开发商称方案能增加零售空间和市政收入，但居民担心新综合体挤走小商贩、削弱街区特色。他们的反对并非只是怀旧。市场提供便宜食物、非正式就业，以及老年居民见面的场所。狭窄街巷虽然破旧，却维系活跃的人际网络。建筑师提出更灵活的选项：加固结构、改善排水，把上层改为宽敞的社区中心。这样既能保留街道尺度，也能改善安全。公开论坛后，市议会同意评估两个方案，并要求透明说明成本、环境影响和受扰动的可能性。城市更新不能只用楼高评价。要实现可持续发展，就必须协调经济发展与现有居民的实际需要。","key":"To be sustainable, it must reconcile economic development with the practical needs of the people who already dwell there. || 不定式作目的／条件意味的状语；reconcile A with B 表示协调两种需求。","task":"城市更新应该改善居民的生活，而不是只追求更高的建筑。 || Urban renewal should improve residents' lives rather than merely pursue taller buildings.","q":"What alternative did the architect suggest? || Repair and adapt the existing market while improving drainage and safety. 原建筑保留并改造，而非完全推倒。","note":"","wc":172,"new":["metropolitan","displace","replace","municipal","reconcile","drainage","skyscraper","forum","retail","attachment","shabby","likelihood","dwell","scheme","environmental","spacious","market"]},{"id":"19","title":"湿地并不是闲置土地","en_title":"A Marsh Worth Protecting","kind":"翻译·生态保护","en":"A marsh on the outskirts of town was once dismissed as useless land. A developer wanted to drain it and construct a warehouse. Local volunteers, however, argued that the apparent emptiness concealed a complex habitat. A reed bed sheltered small animals, while the shallow water offered a feeding ground for birds.\nDuring an excursion, we watched a woodpecker near a willow grove and a dove resting on a branch. A snail moved across a damp leaf, and a grasshopper clung to a stalk. Our guide asked us not to trample the vegetation or disturb a nest. Even an organism that seemed trivial could contribute to the area's ecology.\nThe group prepared a proposal to reclaim a damaged section and restrict construction near the water. It did not claim that preservation would solve every environmental problem. Rather, it showed how one practical intervention could protect a valuable locality. Once a habitat is destroyed, its restoration may demand far more time and money than its protection would have required. Treating nature as an integral part of a city can therefore be both responsible and economical.","zh":"镇郊一片湿地曾被视为无用土地，开发商想排干水建仓库。当地志愿者却指出，看似空旷的地方隐藏着复杂栖息地：芦苇地庇护小动物，浅水为鸟类提供觅食场所。一次考察中，我们看见柳林附近的啄木鸟、枝头的鸽子、湿叶上的蜗牛，以及紧抓植物茎秆的蚱蜢。导游要求大家不要踩踏植被或干扰鸟巢。即使看似微小的生物，也可能对当地生态作出贡献。团队建议修复受损地段，并限制水边建设。他们没有声称保护湿地能解决所有环境问题，而是展示一次实际行动如何保护重要地点。一旦栖息地遭破坏，恢复所需时间和资金可能远超原本保护的投入。因此，把自然视为城市不可分割的一部分，既负责，也可能经济合算。","key":"Once a habitat is destroyed, its restoration may demand far more time and money than its protection would have required. || once 引导时间／条件从句；比较结构中 would have required 表示对未采取保护措施的假设成本。","task":"湿地为许多物种提供栖息地，因此不应该被当作无用的土地。 || Wetlands provide habitats for many species and should therefore not be regarded as useless land.","q":"Why did volunteers oppose draining the marsh? || It supported a complex habitat and valuable ecological relationships. 不是单纯因为不喜欢仓库。","note":"","wc":183,"new":["integral","woodpecker","nest","stalk","marsh","grasshopper","snail","locality","trivial","ecology","reed","grove","excursion","reclaim","construction","bed","dove","preservation","drain","trample"]},{"id":"20","title":"在动物保护区学习观察","en_title":"Watching Wildlife Responsibly","kind":"听力·自然科普","en":"At the reserve, an instructor explained the difference between a mammal and a reptile before leading us past the observation enclosure. A peacock displayed its feathers, a turtle rested near the pond, and a beetle crawled beneath a stone. In the distance, a herd moved slowly across the pasture. We were told to observe quietly and let each creature follow its normal pattern.\nThe afternoon talk concerned endangered animals. A gorilla, a leopard, and a whale require very different habitats, yet each can suffer when human activity destroys its surroundings. A panther in a photograph was not a pet or a spectacle; it was a wild animal whose needs deserved respect. The guide also discussed how an extinct species differs from one merely absent from a particular locality.\nWhat impressed us most was the restraint required of a responsible observer. We must not use bait to attract wildlife, allow a puppy to chase birds, or toss food into an enclosure. Curiosity should lead to understanding rather than interference. The privilege of seeing an animal does not entitle us to control its behaviour.","zh":"保护区里，指导员先讲解哺乳动物与爬行动物的区别，再带我们经过观察围栏。孔雀展示羽毛，乌龟在池边休息，甲虫爬到石下，远处兽群缓缓穿过草地。我们被要求安静观察，让动物按正常方式活动。下午的讲座讨论濒危动物：大猩猩、豹和鲸需要不同栖息地，但都可能因人类破坏环境而受苦。照片里的黑豹不是宠物或表演对象，而是需求应受尊重的野生动物。导游还解释物种灭绝与仅在某地消失的区别。最让我们印象深刻的是，负责的观察者必须克制：不能用诱饵引来野生动物，不能让小狗追鸟，也不能把食物扔进围栏。好奇应带来理解，而非干扰。能够看见动物，并不意味着有权控制它的行为。","key":"The privilege of seeing an animal does not entitle us to control its behaviour. || entitle sb. to do 表示给予某人做某事的权利；适合讨论权利与责任。","task":"观察野生动物时，人们应该保持距离，避免干扰它们的正常行为。 || When observing wildlife, people should keep their distance and avoid disturbing the animals' normal behaviour.","q":"Which actions does the guide discourage? || Using bait, allowing dogs to chase birds, and throwing food into enclosures. 三个并列动作都是人为干扰。","note":"","wc":182,"new":["species","puppy","observe","reptile","pasture","peacock","particular","extinct","whale","beetle","turtle","stone","herd","toss","bait","gorilla","follow","spectacle","mammal","panther","leopard","entitle"]},{"id":"21","title":"把废弃物重新变成资源","en_title":"Repair, Reuse, and Recover","kind":"写作·循环利用","en":"At a recycling workshop, each volunteer received a glove and a sorting guide. We separated metal scrap from plastic, detached a cable from a damaged appliance, and removed a worn tile from a reusable wooden frame. The supervisor asked us to handle a sharp edge with caution and leave electrical dismantling to trained personnel.\nThe display explained why materials need different treatment. A polymer may require a specialized process, while a composite product can be difficult to separate. A coating that protects an object from corrosion may complicate its recovery. Even a seemingly minor impurity can reduce the value of a recycled batch. These details made the promise of effortless recycling appear less convincing.\nWe then repaired a chair with a loose joint. A clamp held the parts together until the glue could solidify. Repair could prolong the object's useful life and reduce the need for replacement. The lesson was clear: a circular economy begins before something becomes waste. If manufacturers design products that people can maintain, reuse, and dismantle, fewer valuable resources will end up as litter.","zh":"回收工作坊给每名志愿者发了手套和分类指南。我们把金属废料与塑料分开，从坏电器上拆下电缆，再从可重复使用的木框上取下一块旧瓷砖。主管提醒大家小心锋利边缘，把电器拆解留给受训人员。展览说明材料为何需要不同处理：聚合物可能需要专门工艺，复合产品则难以分离。防腐涂层可能让回收更复杂，看似微小的杂质也可能降低整批回收材料的价值。这些细节让“轻松回收”的承诺显得不够可信。之后，我们修理了一把接头松动的椅子，用夹具固定部件，等胶水凝固。维修能延长使用寿命、减少替换需求。循环经济在物品成为垃圾前就已开始。如果厂家设计便于维护、再用和拆解的产品，最终变成垃圾的宝贵资源就会减少。","key":"If manufacturers design products that people can maintain, reuse, and dismantle, fewer valuable resources will end up as litter. || if 条件句搭配含定语从句的宾语；三个动词并列描述可持续设计。","task":"延长产品寿命，是减少资源浪费的一种切实可行的方法。 || Extending the useful life of products is a practicable way to reduce the waste of resources.","q":"Why can composite products be hard to recycle? || Their different materials can be difficult to separate. 文中通过材料构成解释回收困难。","note":"","wc":178,"new":["glue","prolong","tile","scrap","plastic","personnel","polymer","clamp","composite","cable","corrosion","litter","impurity","seemingly","solidify"]},{"id":"22","title":"节能改造从细节开始","en_title":"An Energy Audit on Campus","kind":"听力·能源与工程","en":"Our college invited an engineer to assess energy consumption in the oldest building. She examined the boiler, the radiator, and the pipe network before checking the insulation. A small leakage near a junction had gone unnoticed, and an inefficient heater was consuming more power than necessary. The proposed replacement would require an initial investment, but might reduce long-term costs.\nDuring her presentation, the engineer explained that a watt describes power, while energy use depends on both power and duration. A kilowatt is a thousand watts. She then showed how a sensor could regulate indoor lighting according to brightness and whether a room was occupied. A solar panel might supply part of the building's electricity, but its contribution would vary with conditions.\nThe students wanted a single spectacular solution. The engineer instead recommended a sequence of measurable improvements: insulate exposed pipes, repair faulty controls, ventilate rooms appropriately, and monitor the outcome. Not every impressive technology produces the optimum result in every setting. A careful assessment of actual needs is indispensable to an effective transition towards more efficient energy utilization.","zh":"学校邀请工程师评估最老建筑的能耗。她先检查锅炉、暖气片和管道网络，再查看保温情况。接头附近有一处小泄漏未被发现，一台低效取暖器耗电超出需要。更换设备需要初始投资，却可能减少长期成本。报告中，她说明瓦特描述功率，而能耗取决于功率和持续时间；一千瓦等于一千瓦特。她还展示传感器如何根据亮度及房间是否有人来调节室内灯光。太阳能板也许能供给部分电力，但贡献会随条件变化。学生希望找到一个惊人的单一方案，工程师却建议进行一系列可测量改进：给裸露管道保温、修理失灵控制器、适当通风并监测结果。并非每种先进技术在所有场景下都最优。认真评估实际需求，是有效转向高效能源利用不可缺少的步骤。","key":"Not every impressive technology produces the optimum result in every setting. || not every 是部分否定，意为“并非每一个”，不要误译为“所有都不”。","task":"节能政策应该建立在实际需求和可衡量的结果之上。 || Energy-saving policies should be based on actual needs and measurable results.","q":"What approach did the engineer recommend? || A sequence of measurable improvements rather than a single spectacular solution. 听清转折词 instead 后的建议。","note":"","wc":178,"new":["optimum","transition","watt","regulate","indoor","ventilate","insulate","kilowatt","radiator","brightness","leakage","junction","solar","utilization","heater","boiler","pipe","sensor","indispensable"]},{"id":"23","title":"从果园到餐桌","en_title":"A Farm's Changing Seasons","kind":"翻译·乡村生活","en":"At dawn, the farmer led us through a fertile valley. An orchard occupied the gentle slope, while barley and another cereal grew on the level ground. Beyond a grassy track, cattle began to graze in a pasture. A rooster called near the poultry shed, where a hen guarded her offspring. The farm also kept a small flock of domestic fowl.\nOur task was to help in the vegetable garden. We used a hoe to loosen the soil, planted a young shoot, and checked the irrigation channels. A toad rested near a water basin, and a bee moved between flowers. The farmer explained that a pest could damage a crop, but careless treatment might also harm useful creatures. Watching a locust did not mean that every insect was an enemy.\nAfter work, we carried a bushel of apples to the storehouse. Some would be sold fresh; others would become juice. Fallen leaves would decompose and return material to the soil. The visit showed us that agricultural productivity rests on patient observation, suitable tools, and an understanding of the relationships that sustain growth.","zh":"黎明，农民带我们穿过肥沃山谷。果园位于缓坡，大麦和另一种谷物长在平地上。草径外，牛开始在牧场吃草。家禽棚附近公鸡啼叫，母鸡守着幼崽，农场还养着一群其他家禽。我们的任务是在菜园帮忙：用锄头松土、种下幼苗，并检查灌溉沟渠。一只蟾蜍停在水盆附近，蜜蜂在花间移动。农民解释，害虫会伤害作物，但不慎处理也可能伤害有益生物。看到一只蝗虫，不等于所有昆虫都是敌人。劳动后，我们把一蒲式耳苹果搬入库房，有的鲜卖，有的榨汁。落叶会分解，让物质回到土壤。参观让我们看到，农业生产力依赖耐心观察、合适工具，以及对维系生长的相互关系的理解。","key":"The visit showed us that agricultural productivity rests on patient observation, suitable tools, and an understanding of the relationships that sustain growth. || show sb. that ... 引出认识；rest on 表示依赖；并列三个名词短语组织总结。","task":"现代农业既需要合适的技术，也需要对自然规律的理解。 || Modern agriculture requires both suitable technology and an understanding of natural patterns.","q":"Why should farmers avoid treating every insect as an enemy? || Some creatures are useful, and careless treatment may harm them. 文章强调生态关系而非一概消灭昆虫。","note":"","wc":181,"new":["graze","flock","bushel","basin","track","fowl","poultry","locust","pest","orchard","irrigation","cereal","rooster","offspring","barley","visit","toad","grassy","loosen","fertile","hoe","decompose"]},{"id":"24","title":"海岸清洁行动","en_title":"A Morning by the Sea","kind":"听力·海洋与志愿服务","en":"Before the seaside cleanup began, the organizer gave us a safety briefing. We were to remain on the beach, avoid a slippery rock, and report anything sharp. Nobody should wade into a rough inlet or attempt to retrieve waste from a reef. A changing tide could create peril even when the water looked calm.\nOur group found a length of fishing line, a torn net, and a plastic crate near the pier. A crab hid beneath a shell, while a gull hovered over the wharf. Farther out, a ferry crossed the strait towards the seaport. Its wake sent a small splash onto the shore. The contrast between everyday activity and discarded rubbish was striking.\nAt the end, we recorded the number and type of objects collected. The data would support a local campaign for better waste management. We did not pretend that one morning could purify an entire coast. Nevertheless, repeated action could reduce harm, deepen awareness, and encourage cooperation. Protecting the sea requires both individual effort and the infrastructure that makes responsible behaviour possible.","zh":"海边清洁开始前，组织者做安全说明：留在沙滩，避开湿滑岩石，发现尖锐物就报告；不要涉入风浪大的小海湾，也不要尝试从礁石上捡垃圾。即使水面平静，潮汐变化也可能带来危险。我们在码头附近找到一段鱼线、破渔网和塑料箱。螃蟹藏在贝壳下，海鸥在码头上盘旋。远处渡船穿过海峡驶向海港，尾流把小片水花推上岸。日常活动与随意丢弃的垃圾形成鲜明对照。结束时，我们记录垃圾数量和种类，用数据支持当地改进废物管理的行动。我们没有假装一上午能净化整片海岸，但重复行动能减少伤害、加深认识并鼓励合作。海洋保护既需要个人努力，也需要使负责行为成为可能的基础设施。","key":"Protecting the sea requires both individual effort and the infrastructure that makes responsible behaviour possible. || 动名词短语作主语，谓语用单数 requires；both ... and ... 连接两个必要条件。","task":"个人行动能够带来改变，但也需要公共设施和长期政策的支持。 || Individual action can make a difference, but it also needs support from public facilities and long-term policies.","q":"What would the recorded data be used for? || To support a local campaign for better waste management. 留意活动结束后数据的用途。","note":"","wc":175,"new":["net","crab","peril","purify","wade","contrast","shell","wharf","inlet","reef","splash","line","strait","seaport","seaside","number","ferry","length","pier"]},{"id":"25","title":"自行车维修室里的力学","en_title":"Mechanics at the Repair Bench","kind":"阅读·工程科普","en":"At the repair bench, the instructor asked us to mount a bicycle securely before examining the rear wheel. We checked the axle, the bearing, and the alignment of the frame. A bent shaft could make a rotating part move unevenly, while excessive friction could waste energy. The instructor used a wrench to tighten a nut and a lever to lift a heavy component.\nNext came a demonstration of torque. A force applied farther from the axis could produce a greater turning effect, provided its direction was appropriate. We turned a crank slowly and watched the pedal rotate. A small model showed how a gear could change the relationship between speed and turning force. Another displayed a piston moving inside a cylinder.\nThe lesson connected theory with visible motion. We learnt to distinguish axial movement from sideways displacement and to notice a loose hinge before it caused damage. No one was permitted to operate unfamiliar equipment without supervision. Understanding mechanics meant more than memorizing a formula: it required noticing how parts interact and recognizing when an apparently minor defect could endanger the whole operation.","zh":"维修台前，指导员让我们先固定自行车，再检查后轮。我们查看车轴、轴承和车架对齐情况。弯曲转轴可能使旋转部件运动不均，过大摩擦则会浪费能量。指导员用扳手拧紧螺母，用杠杆抬起重部件。随后演示扭矩：方向合适时，力作用点离轴越远，转动效果可能越强。我们慢慢转曲柄，观察踏板旋转；小模型展示齿轮如何改变转速与转动力之间的关系，另一模型展示活塞在气缸内运动。课程把理论与可见运动联系起来。我们学习区分轴向运动与侧向位移，并在铰链松动造成损坏前发现问题。没人能在无人监督时操作陌生设备。理解力学不只是背公式，还要观察部件相互作用，认识到小缺陷可能危及整个运行。","key":"Understanding mechanics meant more than memorizing a formula: it required noticing how parts interact. || 动名词作主语；more than + 动名词表示“不只是”；冒号后解释更深层要求。","task":"即使是一个小缺陷，也可能影响整台设备的可靠性。 || Even a minor defect can affect the reliability of an entire machine.","q":"What did the lesson connect? || Mechanical theory with directly observable motion and practical inspection. 学习重点是把概念用于观察。","note":"科技术语用于阅读识别，不必把 torque、axial 等生硬放入普通议论文。","wc":183,"new":["mount","torque","axial","axis","bearing","operation","cylinder","displacement","sideways","endanger","lever","pedal","rear","crank","wrench","nut","mechanics","piston","hinge","move","alignment","gear","friction","axle","shaft","tighten","rotate"]},{"id":"26","title":"一间材料实验室","en_title":"Inside a Materials Laboratory","kind":"阅读·材料与实验","en":"The laboratory compared a metal strip with a sample of polymer. Students measured tensile strength, watched a specimen bend, and recorded the point at which a fracture appeared. A wedge helped hold one sample in place, while a protective screen separated the observers from the apparatus. Safety took precedence over speed.\nA second experiment examined deformation under pressure. A soft material could flatten or stretch, whereas a brittle one might crack. The instructor warned that surface appearance alone could not predict capability. A shiny coating might hide an internal flaw, and a thick workpiece was not necessarily stronger in every direction. The sample's composition and manufacturing process also mattered.\nThe team used calibration records to check its instruments. A small deviation in measurement could become significant when results were compared. Rather than discard an unexpected reading, students repeated the procedure and described the discrepancy. Experimentation requires an honest account of uncertainty. The purpose was to assess a material's behaviour under specified conditions, not to declare one substance universally superior to every alternative.","zh":"实验室比较一条金属与一块聚合物样品。学生测量抗拉强度，观察试件弯曲，并记录何时出现断裂。楔块帮助固定样品，防护屏把观察者与设备隔开，安全优先于速度。第二个实验研究受压变形：柔软材料可能变扁或拉伸，脆性材料则可能开裂。指导员提醒，单看表面不能预测性能，光亮涂层可能掩盖内部缺陷，厚工件也并非各方向都更强，组成与制造工艺同样重要。团队用校准记录检查仪器。比较结果时，小测量偏差也可能很重要。学生没有丢弃意外读数，而是重复程序并说明差异。实验需要诚实交代不确定性，目的是评估材料在指定条件下的行为，而非宣布一种物质普遍优于所有替代物。","key":"A soft material could flatten or stretch, whereas a brittle one might crack. || whereas 连接对照；could / might 保留条件性，避免把实验结果写成无条件规律。","task":"可靠的实验报告应该记录异常结果，而不是把它们隐藏起来。 || A reliable experimental report should record unexpected results rather than hide them.","q":"Why did students repeat an unexpected measurement? || To investigate the discrepancy rather than simply discard inconvenient evidence. 与科研诚信主题呼应。","note":"","wc":172,"new":["tensile","significant","wedge","calibration","deformation","bend","experimentation","hide","universally","fracture","capability","workpiece","whereas","pressure","specimen","substance","deviation","flatten","measurement","crack"]},{"id":"27","title":"看懂一块简单电路板","en_title":"Understanding a Simple Circuit","kind":"阅读·电子与信息","en":"An electrician brought a demonstration board to our electronics class. It contained a battery, a switch, a small lamp, and a capacitor. A diagram showed the connection between each component. The instructor explained that resistance is measured in ohms, with ohm as the singular form, and capacitance in farads. She reminded us that a circuit diagram simplifies a physical arrangement.\nWe examined a silicon chip under a camera connected to a projector. Its tiny scale contrasted with the old radio receiver beside it. A microprocessor could perform operations far more quickly than the mechanical devices in the display, but it still required a suitable power supply. An insulator prevented an unintended electrical connection, while a loose contact could interrupt transmission.\nThe class then discussed a photoelectric detector and an optical sensor. Both examples helped us link an invisible process to a visible response. The demonstration used enclosed educational equipment; students did not handle live household wiring. The most useful insight was that a complex device becomes easier to understand when its function is divided into a sequence of manageable parts.","zh":"电工给电子课带来演示板，上面有电池、开关、小灯和电容器，图示说明各部件的连接。指导员解释，电阻的单位是欧姆，ohm 是单数形式；电容的单位是法拉。她提醒，电路图是对实际布局的简化。我们通过连接投影仪的摄像头观察硅芯片。其微小尺寸与旁边旧收音机形成对比。微处理器运算远快于展出的机械设备，但仍需要合适电源。绝缘体防止意外电连接，接点松动则会中断传输。随后，课堂讨论光电探测器和光学传感器，帮助我们把不可见过程与可见反应联系起来。演示采用封闭教学设备，学生不接触家用带电线路。最实用的认识是：把复杂设备的功能分解为可理解的小步骤，就更容易看懂它。","key":"A complex device becomes easier to understand when its function is divided into a sequence of manageable parts. || when 从句说明理解条件；被动语态突出被分析的功能而非执行者。","task":"把复杂问题分成较小的部分，能够帮助学习者逐步建立理解。 || Dividing a complex problem into smaller parts can help learners develop understanding step by step.","q":"Why was the old radio displayed beside the chip? || To contrast its physical scale with modern electronic technology. 对比用于帮助理解技术变化。","note":"ohm 的单数被明确写出以对应词表。复数 ohms 常用于实际数量表达。","wc":180,"new":["singular","transmission","microprocessor","projector","battery","ohm","receiver","silicon","photoelectric","optical","insulator","detector","insight","capacitance","electronics","capacitor","electrician","chip","switch","board"]},{"id":"28","title":"化学课不只是在记符号","en_title":"Chemistry beyond Symbols","kind":"阅读·化学与材料","en":"In the chemistry gallery, labels introduced zinc, nickel, sodium, and mercury. Another case displayed graphite, quartz, limestone, and a piece of granite. The guide stressed that naming a substance was only the start of understanding it. Its properties depended on its structure and the conditions under which it was examined.\nA model represented an atom with a central nucleus and surrounding electrons. A proton carried positive charge, while a neutron was electrically neutral. An ion differed from a neutral atom or group of atoms because it had gained or lost electrons. The class then compared an inorganic compound with a hydrocarbon and considered what a molecular diagram could show.\nIn a recorded demonstration, a metal could oxidize and form an oxide. Elsewhere, a display illustrated an electrode and an anode in a particular cell. The guide did not invite us to mix unfamiliar chemicals. Instead, she asked us to read each label carefully and distinguish an observation from an explanation. Scientific literacy begins when technical terminology helps us reason about evidence rather than merely impress an audience.","zh":"化学展厅的标签介绍锌、镍、钠和汞，另一个展柜展示石墨、石英、石灰岩和花岗岩。导游强调，叫出物质名称只是理解的开始，其性质取决于结构和观察条件。一个模型以中心原子核及周围电子表示原子：质子带正电，中子不带电。离子与中性原子或原子团的区别，在于获得或失去了电子。课堂又比较无机化合物与烃，思考分子图能展示什么。录播演示中，金属可以氧化并形成氧化物，另一展项说明特定电池中的电极和阳极。导游没有邀请大家混合陌生化学品，而要求认真阅读标签、区分观察与解释。术语帮助我们依据证据推理，而不只是用来显得高深时，科学素养才开始形成。","key":"The guide stressed that naming a substance was only the start of understanding it. || stressed that 引述强调内容；两个动名词短语 naming / understanding 构成“命名—理解”的逻辑递进。","task":"掌握科学术语很重要，但更重要的是理解它们所描述的现象。 || Knowing scientific terminology is important, but understanding the phenomena it describes matters more.","q":"What distinction did the guide ask students to make? || The distinction between an observation and an explanation. 不把看到的现象与对原因的解释混同。","note":"","wc":177,"new":["neutron","proton","nucleus","oxide","oxidize","anode","zinc","inorganic","atom","hydrocarbon","terminology","quartz","limestone","graphite","nickel","sodium","ion","start","granite","mercury","impress","charge","molecular","electrode","reason"]},{"id":"29","title":"从风到运动","en_title":"How Machines Transfer Energy","kind":"阅读·动力与工程","en":"At an engineering exhibition, a small windmill stood beside a model turbine. A moving stream of air could turn a rotor and drive a dynamo. Another display used a transparent hose to illustrate a hydraulic system, while a sealed model demonstrated pneumatic motion. The guide compared these mechanisms without suggesting that they were interchangeable.\nA pulley helped raise a weight, and a spring stored energy when compressed. Visitors could observe the kinetic energy of a moving trolley and the friction that slowed it. A rotating propeller produced thrust in an enclosed demonstration, helping explain one form of propulsion. The shape of the blade and the rate of rotation affected the result.\nThe instructor asked us to consider both useful output and unwanted losses. Vibration, heat, and sound could dissipate energy that might otherwise perform work. A smooth motion did not imply a perfect machine. By identifying where losses occurred, a designer could modify a component, streamline a process, or choose a more suitable mechanism. Engineering progress often comes from a series of careful improvements rather than a single dramatic invention.","zh":"工程展上，小风车立在涡轮模型旁。流动空气能带动转子并驱动发电机。另一展项用透明软管说明液压系统，封闭模型则演示气动运动。导游比较这些机构，并未说它们可以互换。滑轮帮助提升重物，弹簧受压时储存能量。参观者观察移动小车的动能，以及让它减速的摩擦。封闭演示中，旋转螺旋桨产生推力，帮助解释一种推进方式；叶片形状和转速会影响结果。指导员让我们同时考虑有用输出与非预期损耗。振动、热和声音可能使原本可用于做功的能量耗散。运动平稳不等于机器完美。查明损耗位置后，设计者能修改部件、简化流程或选择更合适的机构。工程进步常来自一连串认真改进，而不是单一惊人发明。","key":"By identifying where losses occurred, a designer could modify a component, streamline a process, or choose a more suitable mechanism. || by + 动名词说明方法；where 引导宾语从句；三个动词并列列出可采取的措施。","task":"发现能量损失发生在哪里，是提高设备效率的重要一步。 || Identifying where energy losses occur is an important step towards improving a device's efficiency.","q":"Does smooth motion prove that a machine is perfect? || No. Energy may still be lost through heat, sound, or vibration. 平稳运动并不等于没有损耗。","note":"","wc":180,"new":["hose","propulsion","raise","hydraulic","trolley","perfect","dissipate","propeller","streamline","otherwise","pneumatic","rate","pulley","windmill","dynamo","kinetic"]},{"id":"30","title":"飞行展厅的一堂课","en_title":"Learning How Aircraft Fly","kind":"听力·航空科普","en":"The aviation gallery displayed a glider, a propeller aircraft, and a model supersonic jet. A guide explained that aerospace research examines flight both within and beyond the atmosphere, although each environment creates different problems. A diagram showed the four forces commonly discussed in aircraft flight: lift, weight, thrust, and drag.\nWe watched a video in which air moved around a wing. A model could tilt, ascend, or descend while its controls changed the airflow. Another exhibit demonstrated why a pilot must coordinate movement rather than make a sudden jerk. The guide pointed to the aircraft's nose and explained how the shape of its body could influence drag.\nThe final section concerned emergency equipment. A parachute was displayed beside a training harness, and a notice described why routine inspection mattered. Visitors could manipulate a simulator, but only after an instructor explained its limitations. No model could reproduce every real condition. What the gallery offered was an orientation: a way to connect familiar motion with the principles that make controlled flight possible.","zh":"航空展厅展示滑翔机、螺旋桨飞机和超声速喷气机模型。导游解释，航空航天研究涉及大气层内外的飞行，但不同环境带来不同问题。图示介绍飞机飞行常讨论的四种力：升力、重力、推力和阻力。视频展示气流绕过机翼，模型能倾斜、上升或下降，控制装置会改变气流。另一展项解释为何飞行员要协调动作，避免突然猛动。导游指着机头，说明机身形状如何影响阻力。最后一区域展示应急设备，降落伞放在训练安全带旁，告示说明日常检查的重要性。参观者只有在指导员解释局限后才能操作模拟器，因为模型无法重现所有真实条件。展厅提供的是入门方向：把熟悉运动与可控飞行背后的原理联系起来。","key":"No model could reproduce every real condition. || no + 名词与 every 的组合表达模型无法覆盖所有条件；科学说明文中应主动说明适用范围。","task":"模拟器可以帮助学生理解原理，但无法重现所有真实情况。 || A simulator can help students understand principles, but it cannot reproduce every real situation.","q":"What had to happen before visitors used the simulator? || An instructor had to explain its limitations. 时间顺序由 only after 引出。","note":"","wc":170,"new":["orientation","body","nose","ascend","jerk","flight","parachute","glider","aerospace","aviation","supersonic","manipulate","tilt"]},{"id":"31","title":"星空下的科学提问","en_title":"Questions under the Dome","kind":"阅读·天文学","en":"Inside the observatory dome, our astronomy tutor projected an image of Venus, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn. Each planet could revolve around the Sun along an elliptical orbit. A separate animation explained a lunar eclipse. The tutor warned us not to confuse a cosmic event with a prophecy: a prediction should rest on evidence, not the authority of a prophet.\nWe then discussed exploration beyond Earth. A satellite could carry a probe, but a picture of the cosmos could not answer every question about it. An apparently spherical object might conceal a complicated structure. The quest for knowledge therefore remained open. Rather than speculate without limits, we should define a question and identify the observation needed to examine it. The most memorable sight was not a spectacular photograph, but a student discovering that uncertainty could inspire further inquiry.","zh":"天文台圆顶内，导师投映金星、火星、木星和土星的图像，展示行星沿椭圆轨道绕太阳运行，并用另一动画解释月食。她提醒，不要把宇宙事件与预言混淆：预测应依靠证据，而不是先知权威。随后大家讨论地外探索。卫星可以搭载探测器，但宇宙照片不能回答所有问题，看似球形的物体也可能藏着复杂结构。求知仍有广阔空间。我们应提出明确问题并寻找所需观测，而不是无限猜测。最难忘的景象，是学生发现不确定性也能激发进一步探究。","key":"Rather than speculate without limits, we should define a question. || rather than + 动词原形，提出研究方法上的选择。","task":"科学预测应该建立在可检验的证据之上。 || Scientific predictions should rest on evidence that can be tested.","q":"How does the tutor distinguish a prediction from a prophecy? || A prediction rests on evidence rather than a prophet's authority. 关注论断的依据。","note":"","wc":137,"new":["lunar","dome","prophet","prophecy","prediction","cosmic","cosmos","quest","Venus","elliptical","astronomy","probe","speculate","spherical","Jupiter","sight","Saturn","exploration","Mars","define","satellite","eclipse","revolve"]},{"id":"32","title":"用图形理解数学","en_title":"Mathematics Made Visible","kind":"阅读·数学思维","en":"Our teacher used a rectangle, a triangular frame, and an oval mirror to introduce geometrical thinking. A radius linked a circle's centre to its edge; a perpendicular line met another at a right angle. We compared radial and transverse directions before drawing a spiral and an arc.\nThe algebra lesson began with a simple equation. We expressed a fraction as a decimal, practised multiplication, and used a subscript to distinguish related quantities. A linear relation appeared as a straight line on our graph. Its gradient helped describe change. Later, calculus would extend that idea. The teacher distinguished a finite interval from infinity and explained why an infinite process could require careful reasoning. Saying that something grows infinitely does not replace a proof. Even when a diagram appears symmetrical, its symmetry must be examined, not merely presumed.","zh":"老师用长方形、三角框和椭圆镜引入几何思维。半径连接圆心与边缘，垂直线以直角相交；我们比较径向与横向，再画螺线和圆弧。代数课从简单方程开始，把分数写成小数，练习乘法，并用下标区分相关量。线性关系在图中呈直线，斜率描述变化，微积分会进一步发展这一思想。老师区分有限区间与无穷，指出无穷过程需要严谨推理，说某物无限增长不能代替证明。即使图形看似对称，也要检验而非臆断。","key":"Even when a diagram appears symmetrical, its symmetry must be examined. || even when 表示让步；must be + 过去分词强调必要步骤。","task":"直观的图形可以辅助理解，却不能代替严格的证明。 || An intuitive diagram can aid understanding, but it cannot replace a rigorous proof.","q":"What does the gradient help describe? || Change in the graphed relationship. 图形术语应与实际功能联系。","note":"","wc":136,"new":["multiplication","finite","gradient","subscript","decimal","linear","infinitely","infinite","calculus","introduce","triangular","equation","spiral","oval","rectangle","geometrical","arc","transverse","radial","fraction","symmetry","symmetrical","algebra","infinity","perpendicular","radius"]},{"id":"33","title":"光与声音的实验展","en_title":"Signals We Can Observe","kind":"阅读·物理科普","en":"A prism separated a beam of white light into a spectrum. Nearby, a display compared visible light with ultraviolet radiation and a microwave signal. Visitors adjusted a model wave's amplitude and frequency, then observed how the resulting pattern changed. An antenna and a receiving aerial illustrated the transmission of information.\nIn the sound gallery, a low hum became a loud buzz. The instructor explained why an intense sound could deafen rather than merely irritate. An ultrasonic device was shown in a sealed demonstration. We compared stereo recordings with an older analogue system and listened for distortion. The ambient noise made a subtle difference difficult to discern. Only when the room became quiet could we hear it clearly. The exhibition turned unfamiliar terms into questions about perception, measurement, and the limits of our senses.","zh":"棱镜把白光束分成光谱，旁边展项比较可见光、紫外辐射和微波信号。参观者调节波形模型的振幅与频率，观察图案变化，天线展示信息传输。声音展区里，低沉嗡鸣变成响亮蜂鸣。老师解释，强烈声音可能损害听觉，而不只是烦人。超声设备采用封闭演示。我们比较立体声录音与旧模拟系统，倾听失真。环境噪声让细微差异难以辨别，只有安静后才听得清楚。展览把陌生术语转化为关于感知、测量与感官局限的问题。","key":"Only when the room became quiet could we hear it clearly. || only + when 从句前置，主句部分倒装。","task":"环境噪声可能使细微的差别难以辨别。 || Ambient noise may make subtle differences difficult to discern.","q":"Why was the difference initially hard to hear? || Ambient noise concealed it. 注意实验条件对观察的影响。","note":"","wc":133,"new":["ultraviolet","ambient","spectrum","hum","subtle","microwave","deafen","frequency","distortion","stereo","prism","analogue","aerial","discern","irritate","amplitude","perception","beam","antenna","ultrasonic","white","buzz"]},{"id":"34","title":"谈能源先弄清概念","en_title":"Discussing Energy Carefully","kind":"阅读·能源与政策","en":"At a symposium, a speaker explained nuclear fission using a model reactor. A uranium nucleus could split, releasing energy. The audience then compared this process with combustion in a fossil-fuel plant. A refinery, the speaker added, served a different purpose from an electricity generator. Mixing these concepts would produce a misleading debate.\nStudents asked about thermal efficiency, carbon dioxide emission, and the management of residual material. No single number could express every consequence. The speaker recommended a framework that considered cost, reliability, and environmental effects together. A by-product that appeared negligible in one experiment might matter at a larger scale. Before proposing a drastic change, decision-makers should quantify the expected benefits and identify the assumptions behind them. A balanced discussion requires neither blind enthusiasm nor blanket rejection, but a clear account of the relevant evidence.","zh":"研讨会上，发言者用反应堆模型解释核裂变：铀原子核可以分裂并释放能量。听众把它与化石燃料电厂的燃烧比较。发言者补充，炼油厂与发电机承担不同任务，混淆概念会误导讨论。学生询问热效率、二氧化碳排放及残余物管理。单一数字不能表达所有后果，应同时考虑成本、可靠性与环境影响。某次实验中似乎微不足道的副产物，规模扩大后可能很重要。提出剧烈变革前，决策者应量化预期收益并说明假设。平衡的讨论需要清晰证据，而非盲目热情或全盘否定。","key":"A by-product that appeared negligible in one experiment might matter at a larger scale. || 定语从句限定对象；might 保持审慎推断。","task":"评估能源政策时，应同时考虑成本、可靠性和环境影响。 || When assessing energy policy, we should consider cost, reliability, and environmental effects together.","q":"Why is a single number insufficient? || It cannot represent every consequence of an energy choice. 综合评估需要多个维度。","note":"","wc":135,"new":["consequence","uranium","negligible","residual","emission","thermal","combustion","quantify","fission","symposium","refinery","drastic","framework","fossil","by-product","split","reactor","dioxide","blind"]},{"id":"35","title":"地图上的方向与实地判断","en_title":"Finding Our Way","kind":"听力·地理与旅行","en":"Before our expedition, the scout explained latitude, longitude, and the equator on a globe. We located each hemisphere, traced a continental coastline, and distinguished an arctic route from an antarctic one. The polar regions were far from our actual destination: a mountainous district in our own province.\nWe would travel eastward, turn northward at a junction (northwards on the route card), and then proceed southwards around a steep incline. A barometer, a map, and a compass belonged in our kit. The guide warned that mist could hide the horizon and make a familiar location seem strange. If a storm developed, we would not press onward. Onwards was our general direction, not an obligation to ignore danger. A geographical description was useful, but real navigation also required attention to current conditions and the capability of the group.","zh":"考察前，向导在地球仪上解释纬度、经度和赤道，定位南北半球，描出大陆海岸，区分北极与南极路线。极地离我们的实际目的地很远：我们只去本省山区。路线先向东，在岔口向北，再向南绕过陡坡。装备包括气压计、地图和指南针。导游提醒，雾可能遮住地平线，让熟悉地点显得陌生。若有暴风雨，就不硬向前走；继续前行是总体方向，不是忽视危险的义务。地理描述有用，但实际导航也需关注当前条件与团队能力。","key":"If a storm developed, we would not press onward. || 过去叙述中的条件与未来行动，用 would 表示当时预定的应对。","task":"良好的计划应该允许人们根据实际条件调整路线。 || A good plan should allow people to adjust their route according to actual conditions.","q":"Where was the expedition actually going? || To a mountainous district in the group's own province. 极地只是地图教学内容。","note":"onward/onwards、northward/northwards 为原表括号变体，此处均保留。地图描述是虚构训练场景。","wc":136,"new":["press","onward","southwards","northward","latitude","strange","expedition","scout","barometer","incline","antarctic","polar","province","longitude","mountainous","location","geographical","continental","equator","kit","horizon","arctic","storm","mist","hemisphere","eastward"]},{"id":"36","title":"港口如何协同运作","en_title":"A Working Harbour","kind":"听力·交通与物流","en":"At the harbour, a tug helped a tanker approach the dock while a barge waited outside. A passenger liner would depart after a freight vessel. From the terminal, we could also see a yacht prepared for a coastal cruise. The port's headquarters had to coordinate these movements carefully.\nAn inspector checked a ship's hull and storage compartments. Workers would hoist a container, secure it, and record its destination before loading another. A damaged load required a different procedure; nobody could simply haul it aboard and hope for the best. A notice explained how the railway locomotive linked the port to inland distribution centres.\nThe guide said that shipbuilding and transport depended on countless modest operations performed correctly. A delay ashore could affect a schedule overseas. What looked like a chaotic gathering of machines was, in fact, an intricate arrangement of people, equipment, and information.","zh":"港口里，拖船协助油轮靠码头，驳船在外等待。客轮将在货船后离港，航站楼外还能看到准备沿海巡游的游艇。港口总部必须仔细协调。检查员查看船体和储藏舱，工人吊起集装箱、固定并记录目的地后，再装下一只。受损货物要另按流程处理，不能随便拖上船再碰运气。告示说明铁路机车如何连接港口与内陆配送中心。导游说，造船和运输依赖无数小步骤的正确执行，岸上一处延误可能影响海外时刻表。看似混乱的机器集合，实际是人员、设备与信息的精密安排。","key":"What looked like a chaotic gathering of machines was, in fact, an intricate arrangement. || what 引导主语从句，对照表面印象与实际情况。","task":"一次局部延误可能影响整个运输网络。 || A local delay can affect an entire transport network.","q":"How were inland centres connected to the port? || By railway. 听清不同交通方式之间的衔接。","note":"","wc":144,"new":["headquarters","storage","correctly","shipbuilding","overseas","ashore","outside","freight","locomotive","yacht","tanker","tug","harbour","cruise","hull","haul","hoist","inspector","terminal","gathering","inland","barge","liner","dock"]},{"id":"37","title":"在厨房里学习协作","en_title":"Cooking Together","kind":"听力·日常生活","en":"Our cooking club planned a wholesome luncheon. One group would chop garlic and ginger, while another prepared mustard, soy sauce, and olive oil. We had tuna, salmon, sardine, shrimp, and oyster on a display card, but chose only one fish for the meal. A separate team prepared a sandwich with ham and a small bowl of vegetable soup.\nThe instructor showed us how to peel a pineapple, squeeze fruit, and finely chop a walnut for decoration. A raisin and a chestnut could provide different textures. We learnt to thicken soup gradually, sweeten a sauce moderately, and avoid turning it watery. Before using a mixer, we checked that the jug was correctly fitted. The meal taught us that a recipe is also an exercise in coordination: each ingredient has a role, and good timing helps separate efforts become a shared result.","zh":"烹饪社计划做一顿健康午餐。一组切蒜和姜，另一组准备芥末、酱油与橄榄油。展示卡列出金枪鱼、鲑鱼、沙丁鱼、虾和牡蛎，但这顿饭只选一种鱼；另一组做火腿三明治和蔬菜汤。老师演示削菠萝、榨水果汁并把核桃切碎装饰，葡萄干与栗子带来不同口感。我们学习逐步把汤调浓、适度给酱汁增甜，避免过稀。使用搅拌机前先确认容器安装正确。菜谱也是协调练习：每种食材有作用，恰当时机让分头劳动成为共同成果。","key":"Good timing helps separate efforts become a shared result. || help + 宾语 + 动词原形，适用于团队协作主题。","task":"分工明确和及时沟通可以提高团队效率。 || Clear responsibilities and timely communication can improve a team's efficiency.","q":"Did the club cook all the seafood on the card? || No. It selected one fish. 展示词卡与实际菜单不同。","note":"","wc":140,"new":["chop","squeeze","luncheon","garlic","watery","wholesome","moderately","sweeten","thicken","sardine","raisin","ingredient","oyster","chestnut","finely","tuna","mustard","soy","ginger","sandwich","ham","mixer","walnut","peel","salmon","olive","pineapple","jug","recipe","shrimp"]},{"id":"38","title":"在诊所把症状说清楚","en_title":"Describing a Problem Clearly","kind":"听力·就医沟通","en":"At the clinic, a patient explained that he felt dizzy and had developed a persistent cough. He could describe a symptom, but he did not try to diagnose himself. The nurse asked when the problem began and whether he had taken anything before the visit. Accurate information would help the clinician assess the situation.\nA poster explained the distinction between a bacterium and the broader everyday word germ. Another described the clinic's work to vaccinate eligible patients and reduce the spread of infectious disease. A pamphlet mentioned tuberculosis, while a diagram illustrated a kidney and a vein. These displays offered vocabulary, not a prescription for every visitor.\nThe patient asked what the next step involved and requested clarification of an unfamiliar term. Good communication did not require specialized knowledge. It required an honest description, careful listening, and the confidence to ask when an explanation remained unclear.","zh":"诊所里，一位患者说自己头晕并持续咳嗽。他描述症状，却不自行诊断。护士询问何时开始、来之前是否服用过什么，以帮助临床人员评估。海报区分细菌与日常更宽泛的“病菌”，介绍为符合条件者接种以及减少传染病传播的工作。宣传册提到结核病，图示展示肾脏与静脉。这些展示提供知识与词汇，不是给所有人的统一处方。患者询问下一步安排，并请求解释陌生术语。良好沟通不要求专业知识，而需要诚实描述、认真倾听，以及不懂时敢于提问。","key":"He could describe a symptom, but he did not try to diagnose himself. || but 连接职责不同的行为；symptom 是症状，diagnose 是诊断。","task":"清楚描述问题，比使用自己不理解的专业术语更有帮助。 || Describing a problem clearly is more helpful than using technical terms one does not understand.","q":"What information did the nurse request? || When the problem began and what the patient had taken before the visit. 时间与此前行为是具体信息。","note":"","wc":146,"new":["symptom","clinic","diagnose","prescription","pamphlet","bacterium","germ","dizzy","kidney","vein","tuberculosis","vaccinate","infectious"]},{"id":"39","title":"运动中的节奏与坚持","en_title":"Fitness without Comparison","kind":"写作·健康生活","en":"Our coach encouraged us to regard fitness as a gradual undertaking. A muscular appearance did not prove endurance, and a vigorous start did not guarantee a sustainable routine. Each person needed an adjustable plan that reflected experience and current ability.\nAt the first session, we would jog, practise balance, and learn a controlled movement involving the hip and thigh. Some participants could barely complete the sequence, while others wanted an extra challenge. The coach asked us not to mock a slower learner or mistake discomfort for achievement. A competitive atmosphere could energize a group, but excessive comparison could also frustrate it.\nAfter several weeks, the participants noticed steadier progress. The aim was to feel physically capable and remain engaged. Regular recreation offered a break from work and an opportunity to build supportive relationships. A modest routine we could sustain was more useful than an extreme programme abandoned after a few days.","zh":"教练鼓励我们把体能看作逐步培养的结果。肌肉外观不证明耐力，猛烈开头也不保证能坚持，每人需要符合经验与当前能力的可调计划。第一次训练包含慢跑、平衡及涉及髋部和大腿的受控动作。有人勉强完成，有人希望增加挑战。教练要求不嘲笑慢一些的学习者，也不把不适误当成绩。竞争气氛可以激励团队，过度比较却可能使人受挫。几周后，大家的进步更稳定，目标是身体能胜任活动并保持参与。规律休闲让人暂离工作、建立支持关系。能坚持的适量安排，比几天后放弃的极端计划更有用。","key":"A muscular appearance did not prove endurance, and a vigorous start did not guarantee a sustainable routine. || 两个平行否定句区分表象与长期能力。","task":"可持续的进步需要适合个人能力的计划。 || Sustainable progress requires a plan suited to individual ability.","q":"What was the coach's attitude towards comparison? || Competition could help, but excessive comparison could frustrate learners. 答案保留两面性。","note":"","wc":151,"new":["recreation","physically","hip","fitness","jog","endurance","feel","adjustable","competitive","vigorous","barely","challenge","extreme","muscular","thigh","energize","extra","coach","frustrate","mock"]},{"id":"40","title":"合租生活里的协商","en_title":"Sharing a Home","kind":"听力·住宿沟通","en":"When we moved into our lodging, the sitting-room contained a sofa, a couch cover, and a small table. A closet held spare bedding, while the pantry was almost empty. The landlord showed us the basement, the laundry area, and the balcony before handing over the key.\nSharing the space required more than dividing the rent. We agreed to rinse dishes, scrub the sink, and mop up a spill promptly. Nobody should leave underwear or pyjamas in the common lounge. One flatmate preferred an early breakfast; another came home late and needed a quiet place to unwind. These habits were not necessarily incompatible.\nWe held a short meeting whenever a complaint arose. An explicit agreement helped prevent a minor annoyance from becoming lasting resentment. The flat was neither luxurious nor spacious, but considerate behaviour made it homely. A comfortable home depends as much on cooperation as on furniture.","zh":"搬入住处时，起居室有沙发、沙发罩和小桌。壁橱存放备用寝具，食品储藏间几乎空着。房东展示地下室、洗衣区和阳台后交钥匙。合租不只是分房租。大家同意冲净碗碟、刷洗水槽并及时拖净泼洒物，不把内衣睡衣留在公共休息室。一人喜欢早吃早饭，另一人晚归需要安静放松，这些习惯未必不能兼容。出现抱怨就开短会，明确约定能防止小烦恼变成长期怨恨。房子既不豪华也不宽大，但体谅让它温馨。舒适的家既依赖家具，也依赖合作。","key":"A comfortable home depends as much on cooperation as on furniture. || as much on A as on B 表示两方面同样重要。","task":"明确的约定有助于防止小分歧演变成严重冲突。 || Clear agreements help prevent minor disagreements from developing into serious conflicts.","q":"How did the flatmates deal with complaints? || They held a short meeting and clarified agreements. 解决方式是及时协商。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["sofa","balcony","closet","laundry","couch","rinse","pantry","underwear","sitting-room","homely","lodging","complaint","mop","basement","breakfast","incompatible","luxurious","spill","lounge","pyjamas","sink","scrub"]},{"id":"41","title":"学生社团的公开决策","en_title":"Rules for a Student Association","kind":"写作·治理与责任","en":"Our association asked a volunteer to preside over its annual meeting. The treasurer presented the accounts, and a delegate proposed an alteration to the constitution. The new provision would require public notice before a major expenditure. Members could second a motion, debate its merit, and vote in a poll.\nOne faction wanted to abolish every procedural constraint, arguing that bureaucracy wasted time. Others feared that a powerful chair might dominate decisions. We eventually reached an accord: retain a brief review, but shorten unnecessary paperwork. The committee would designate a deputy to supervise implementation and publish a quarterly summary.\nThe unanimous decision did not remove every disagreement about politics. It established a procedure whereby disagreement could be expressed fairly. A charter is valuable when people abide by its principles and hold each other accountable. Good administration should make participation possible while preventing authority from becoming a personal privilege.","zh":"社团请志愿者主持年会，财务负责人汇报账目，一位代表提议修改章程：大笔开支前必须公开通知。成员可附议、讨论价值并投票。一个派别主张废除一切程序限制，认为官僚手续浪费时间；其他人担心强势主席控制决策。最终大家达成一致：保留简短审查，减少多余文书，指定副手监督执行并发布季度摘要。一致通过不代表政治分歧消失，而是建立公平表达分歧的程序。章程的价值在于遵守原则并相互问责。良好管理应让参与成为可能，防止权力变成个人特权。","key":"It established a procedure whereby disagreement could be expressed fairly. || whereby 表示“借助该程序”，引导定语从句，正式语体中可用。","task":"透明的程序有助于防止权力被滥用。 || Transparent procedures help prevent the abuse of power.","q":"What compromise did members reach? || Keep a short review while reducing unnecessary paperwork. 兼顾监督与效率。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["abide","charter","preside","designate","merit","politics","poll","dominate","accord","treasurer","constraint","faction","shorten","whereby","quarterly","provision","bureaucracy","abolish","deputy","delegate","alteration","unanimous","constitution","supervise"]},{"id":"42","title":"诚实比掩饰更重要","en_title":"Integrity under Pressure","kind":"写作·职业道德","en":"A supplier offered an employee a bribe to overlook a defective batch. Accepting it would violate the company's rules and betray its clients. Yet the employee feared that reporting the incident might endanger his promotion. A colleague urged him to document what had happened and use the firm's reporting process.\nThe subsequent investigation found an irregularity in several transactions. Managers had tried to whitewash the matter with an ambiguous statement, but the evidence contradicted their denial. The board decided to dismiss the responsible manager and commission an independent review. It also promised to compensate affected customers.\nA scandal can damage more than immediate earnings. It can undermine the confidence on which long-term cooperation rests. No organization can claim moral superiority merely because it has a code of conduct. Its integrity becomes manifest when it is willing to acknowledge wrongdoing, impose appropriate consequences, and protect people who raise a legitimate concern.","zh":"供应商向员工行贿，希望他忽略一批缺陷产品。接受贿赂既违背公司规定，也背叛客户，但员工担心举报影响晋升。同事建议记录事实并使用公司报告流程。后续调查发现多笔交易异常。管理人员曾用模糊声明粉饰问题，但证据否定其说法。董事会决定解雇负责人、委托独立审查并补偿客户。丑闻损害的不只是眼前收益，还会削弱长期合作的信任。组织不能仅凭行为准则就宣称道德优越；愿意承认错误、落实适当后果并保护正当反映问题者时，诚信才真正显现。","key":"Its integrity becomes manifest when it is willing to acknowledge wrongdoing. || when 从句给出抽象品质得以体现的具体条件。","task":"公众信任取决于组织如何回应错误。 || Public trust depends on how an organization responds to its mistakes.","q":"Why was the employee initially hesitant? || He feared that reporting the incident might harm his promotion. 留意心理动因。","note":"","wc":150,"new":["commission","violate","dismiss","whitewash","ambiguous","impose","bribe","denial","subsequent","scandal","irregularity","manifest"]},{"id":"43","title":"一场模拟法庭","en_title":"Evidence in a Mock Court","kind":"阅读·公共规则","en":"In a mock court, a student played a detective investigating a theft. Another acted as an attorney, while a third took the role of a magistrate. The alleged offence involved a stolen bicycle. The class had to distinguish suspicion from proof before discussing guilt.\nA witness would testify about what she had seen, not what gossip suggested. The defence could challenge a claim, question identification, and make a plea for careful consideration. A confession in the script was not automatically conclusive: its circumstances also mattered. The teacher asked us not to presume that a suspicious appearance established wrongdoing.\nThe exercise ended without a real conviction or penalty. Its purpose was to acquaint us with disciplined reasoning. It is easy to demand certainty when a story provokes anger; it is harder to examine competing explanations fairly. An impartial process protects both the person making a complaint and the person accused.","zh":"模拟法庭上，学生分别扮演侦探、律师和法官，案件是一辆自行车失窃。讨论有罪与否前，要区分怀疑与证据。证人只能陈述所见，不依赖流言；辩方可质疑主张与身份辨认，并请求慎重考虑。剧本中的供认也并非自动成为定论，还要看发生背景。老师要求不要凭外表可疑就认定犯错。活动没有真实定罪或处罚，而是让大家熟悉严谨推理。故事激起愤怒时要求确定答案很容易，公正审视不同解释更难。公正程序同时保护申诉者与被指控者。","key":"It is easy to demand certainty; it is harder to examine competing explanations fairly. || it 作形式主语，不定式为真正主语，平行比较增强论证。","task":"我们不应该把怀疑当作已经得到证明的事实。 || We should not treat suspicion as an established fact.","q":"What was the purpose of the exercise? || To practise disciplined reasoning rather than impose a real punishment. 模拟场景的学习目的。","note":"","wc":149,"new":["testify","detective","guilt","acquaint","identification","conviction","certainty","plea","suspicious","presume","offence","magistrate","theft","attorney","penalty"]},{"id":"44","title":"冲突之后的重建","en_title":"Rebuilding after Conflict","kind":"阅读·历史与人道关怀","en":"The documentary followed a civilian family returning to a desolate town. Warfare had damaged a bridge, emptied a nursery, and left the market in ruins. A former refugee described the grief of losing a neighbour and the difficulty of beginning again. No triumphant slogan could erase that experience.\nAn aid worker explained how humanitarian support could help restore ordinary life. Teams repaired water facilities, reunited relatives, and made a damaged school usable. A memorial recorded a massacre and warned against treating cruelty as an inevitable feature of history. The narrator rejected both the glorification of slaughter and a call for vengeance.\nReconstruction demanded solidarity, patience, and practical resources. A political settlement might end a battle, but it would not instantly remove fear or deprivation. Lasting peace requires institutions that safeguard dignity and opportunities for people to rebuild trust. Humanity is tested most clearly when the needs of vulnerable people remain visible after public attention has moved elsewhere.","zh":"纪录片跟随一个平民家庭返回荒凉城镇。战争毁坏桥梁、使托儿所空置、让市场成为废墟。曾为难民的人讲述失去邻居的悲痛与重新开始的困难，胜利口号无法抹去经历。援助人员解释，人道支持通过修复供水、帮助亲人团聚、恢复学校来重建日常生活。纪念碑记录屠杀，提醒人们不要把残酷当作历史必然。旁白拒绝歌颂杀戮或呼吁复仇。重建需要团结、耐心与资源，政治和解能结束战斗，却不会立刻消除恐惧与匮乏。长久和平还需维护尊严的制度和重建信任的机会。公众目光转移后仍看见脆弱者的需要，尤其考验人性。","key":"A political settlement might end a battle, but it would not instantly remove fear. || might / would 保持条件性，区分短期结果与长期问题。","task":"重建不仅包括修复建筑，也包括恢复人们之间的信任。 || Reconstruction involves restoring trust between people as well as repairing buildings.","q":"Why is rebuilding more than repairing structures? || People also need security, relationships, and trust restored. 关注物质与社会层面。","note":"","wc":157,"new":["warfare","battle","solidarity","settlement","humanity","civilian","refugee","nursery","bridge","documentary","desolate","massacre","cruelty","humanitarian","grief","vengeance","safeguard","slaughter"]},{"id":"45","title":"博物馆中的权力故事","en_title":"When Power Goes Unchecked","kind":"阅读·历史词汇","en":"An exhibit described a fictional sovereign who became a tyrant. His regime used propaganda to glorify obedience, while a dictator in a neighbouring state claimed that dissent was a menace. The curator asked visitors to examine how tyranny could turn a disagreement into an excuse to persecute people.\nThe story included a siege, a captive soldier, and a regiment ordered to defend a fort. A bugle signalled the advance of a troop. Later, a mob tried to overthrow the ruler, and a bandit exploited the disorder to plunder abandoned houses. The display did not present every opponent as a hero.\nIts closing panel described efforts to govern through accountable institutions. A society cannot escape abuse simply by replacing one ruler with another. What matters is whether public authority is constrained and whether ordinary people can challenge injustice without being treated as enemies. Historical language becomes useful when it helps us ask precise questions about power.","zh":"展览讲述虚构君主变成暴君的故事。他的政权用宣传歌颂服从，邻国独裁者则称异议是威胁。策展人请游客思考，暴政如何把分歧当作迫害借口。故事包含围城、被俘士兵和奉命守堡的团，军号发出部队前进信号。后来暴民试图推翻统治者，匪徒趁乱劫掠空屋。展览没有把所有反对者都描绘成英雄。最后介绍通过可问责制度治理的努力：只换统治者不足以摆脱滥权，关键在于公共权力是否受约束，普通人能否挑战不公而不被视为敌人。历史词汇能帮助我们准确追问权力问题。","key":"What matters is whether public authority is constrained. || what 主语从句搭配 whether 表语从句，适合提出判断标准。","task":"真正重要的是，权力是否受到有效监督。 || What truly matters is whether power is subject to effective oversight.","q":"Did the exhibition portray every opponent as heroic? || No. It also showed bandits exploiting disorder. 避免把复杂叙述简化为单一对立。","note":"","wc":155,"new":["regime","excuse","troop","fort","propaganda","overthrow","regiment","bandit","persecute","neighbouring","sovereign","mob","bugle","govern","disorder","obedience","dictator","captive","tyrant","tyranny","siege","menace","plunder"]},{"id":"46","title":"宗教词汇与尊重差异","en_title":"Reading about Belief","kind":"阅读·文化与宗教","en":"In a comparative religion class, we read about Islam, Buddhism, and Christian traditions. One text described a mosque and a pilgrim; another introduced a monk, a nun, and a Catholic bishop. References to Jesus Christ, the pope, and scripture required attention to each passage's context.\nThe teacher distinguished description from personal endorsement. To explain why someone might worship, pray, or burn incense was not to demand that classmates share a doctrine. A pious person might cherish a shrine, while another reader approached the same object historically. Older texts sometimes used Moslem where contemporary texts often use Muslim.\nWe discussed words such as divine, Heaven, and eternal without presenting supernatural claims as scientific findings. A respectful reader should neither ridicule belief nor assume that every member of a community thinks alike. Understanding cultural language requires sensitivity to difference, including differences within a tradition.","zh":"比较宗教课阅读伊斯兰教、佛教与基督教传统。文章提到清真寺、朝圣者、僧侣、修女和天主教主教；耶稣基督、教皇与经文等词需要结合语境。老师区分描述与个人赞同：解释礼拜、祈祷或焚香，不是要求同学接受某种教义。虔诚信徒可能珍爱圣祠，其他读者则从历史角度看它。旧文有时用 Moslem，当代文本常用 Muslim。我们讨论神圣、天堂和永恒等词，却不把超自然主张当作科学发现。尊重的读者既不嘲笑信仰，也不假设群体成员思想一致；文化理解要注意传统内部的差异。","key":"To explain why someone might worship was not to demand that classmates share a doctrine. || 不定式作主语，区分解释某种行为与要求认同。","task":"理解一种文化，不意味着必须接受其中的每一种信念。 || Understanding a culture does not mean accepting every belief within it.","q":"What distinction did the teacher emphasize? || Description versus personal endorsement. 解释并不等于赞同。","note":"Moslem 是旧拼写；主动写作优先使用 Muslim。宗教名词需结合语境理解。","wc":142,"new":["eternal","Islam","Jesus","nun","religion","pilgrim","incense","Catholic","shrine","divine","Heaven","mosque","pious","sensitivity","Christ","doctrine","Christian","monk","Buddhism","worship","scripture","pope","bishop","ridicule","Moslem"]},{"id":"47","title":"舞台背后的合作","en_title":"Behind the Curtain","kind":"听力·戏剧与表演","en":"The amateur drama group prepared a comedy about a magician who could not perform a simple trick. A clown would interrupt him, a dancer would attempt a ballet step, and a witty servant would reveal the illusion. The final episode ended with a surprising gesture rather than a long speech.\nBackstage, someone repaired a scarlet cloak, stitched a seam in a frock, and attached a lace collar to a blouse. A makeup artist adjusted a blond wig and added a wrinkle to make a young actor appear older. The actress playing a goddess practised a graceful movement, while the stage manager checked every cue.\nOpening night brought nervous excitement. The audience began to clap at the climax, and the actors exchanged a grateful hug afterwards. The performance seemed effortless only because innumerable small tasks had been completed with care. Entertainment is often built on cooperation that the spectator never sees.","zh":"业余剧团排演一出喜剧：魔术师连简单戏法都做不好，小丑打断他，舞者尝试芭蕾动作，机智仆人揭露幻象。最后一幕以意外动作而非长演说收尾。后台有人修补猩红披风、缝连衣裙接缝，把蕾丝领安到女衬衫上；化妆师调整金色假发、画上皱纹让年轻演员显老。饰女神的演员练习优雅动作，舞台监督逐一核对提示。首演令人紧张兴奋，高潮时观众鼓掌，结束后演员感激相拥。表演之所以看似轻松，是因为无数小任务已被细心完成。娱乐往往建立在观众看不见的合作上。","key":"The performance seemed effortless only because innumerable small tasks had been completed with care. || 过去完成时被动表示演出之前已完成的准备。","task":"看似轻松的表演往往需要大量看不见的准备。 || A seemingly effortless performance often requires extensive preparation that the audience never sees.","q":"Why did the performance appear effortless? || Numerous backstage tasks had been completed carefully. 外在效果来自幕后劳动。","note":"","wc":150,"new":["makeup","wrinkle","entertainment","episode","cloak","scarlet","lace","drama","comedy","innumerable","clap","blouse","goddess","magician","hug","grateful","witty","illusion","seam","spectator","blond","ballet","climax","frock","clown","gesture"]},{"id":"48","title":"一场风暴中的社区","en_title":"A Community Facing a Storm","kind":"听力·应急协作","en":"A sudden gust shook the shutters as the weather bulletin announced a severe storm. Clouds gathered, hail struck the pavement, and water began to overflow a gutter. The council asked residents to remain alert and follow the local warning. A hurricane mentioned in the broadcast was affecting a distant coast; our town faced heavy rain.\nVolunteers helped move supplies from a damp basement. They used a portable lamp, carried a watertight box, and kept the exit clear. When a branch threatened to block the road, trained staff arranged a safe diversion. No one was encouraged to scramble onto a roof or cross a flooded street.\nAfterwards, neighbours checked on a frail resident and helped clear debris. The damage was serious, but timely cooperation reduced confusion. Preparedness means more than owning equipment: it means knowing who will do what and how information will reach those who need it.","zh":"突起阵风摇动百叶窗，天气公告宣布强风暴来临。云聚集，冰雹打向路面，雨水溢出排水沟。市政部门要求居民警觉并遵循当地预警。广播提到的飓风在遥远海岸，本镇面对的是大雨。志愿者把物资移出潮湿地下室，使用便携灯、搬防水箱并保持出口畅通。树枝可能堵路时，受训人员安排安全绕行。没人被鼓励爬屋顶或穿过积水街道。事后，邻居查看体弱居民并清理杂物。损害严重，但及时合作减少混乱。准备不只是拥有设备，还包括明确分工和信息如何送到需要的人手中。","key":"Preparedness means more than owning equipment: it means knowing who will do what. || means + 动名词，冒号后把抽象准备落实为具体分工。","task":"明确的沟通能够在紧急情况下减少混乱。 || Clear communication can reduce confusion in an emergency.","q":"Was a hurricane directly affecting the town? || No. The hurricane was distant; the town faced heavy rain. 识别不同地点的信息。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["block","diversion","gust","cross","hail","portable","hurricane","alert","warning","timely","severe","gutter","frail","overflow","watertight","scramble"]},{"id":"49","title":"山路上的一次改道","en_title":"A Hike That Changed Course","kind":"听力·户外活动","en":"Our hike began on a winding trail beside a barren slope. We passed a rocky overhang, a shallow cave with a hollow echo, and a clearing where a lily grew in the shade. The guide asked us to tread carefully on loose gravel and avoid the fragile edge of the path.\nAt noon, a fallen tree made the intended route inaccessible. We could not bypass it safely. Some walkers wanted to cling to the original plan, but the guide chose a longer descent. We would traverse the lower ridge, turn at a fence, and return through a neighbouring village.\nThe change caused disappointment, yet nobody had to prove courage by taking a needless risk. We ate a snack, tightened a bootlace, and resumed at a comfortable pace. A successful journey does not always reach the planned summit. Sometimes its achievement lies in recognizing when a sensible alteration is necessary.","zh":"徒步从贫瘠山坡旁的曲径开始，经过悬岩、带空洞回声的浅洞，以及阴影中长着百合的空地。导游要求小心踩碎石，避开脆弱路边。中午倒树使原路无法进入，也无法安全绕过。有人执意原计划，导游却选了更长的下山路：横穿较低山脊，在围栏处转弯，经邻村返回。变化令人失望，但没人需要以无谓冒险证明勇气。大家吃零食、紧鞋带，按舒适速度继续。成功旅程不一定到达计划中的山顶，有时成就在于认出何时必须合理调整。","key":"Sometimes its achievement lies in recognizing when a sensible alteration is necessary. || lie in + 动名词表示关键所在；when 引导宾语从句。","task":"坚持目标并不意味着拒绝调整方法。 || Commitment to a goal does not mean refusing to adjust one's approach.","q":"Why did the guide change the route? || A fallen tree blocked the path, and it could not be bypassed safely. 决定基于现场条件。","note":"","wc":149,"new":["hike","cling","hollow","overhang","descent","gravel","barren","bypass","snack","fence","traverse","echo","summit","inaccessible","fragile","lily","clearing","shade","pace","tread"]},{"id":"50","title":"退休后的新角色","en_title":"A Different Kind of Contribution","kind":"写作·老龄社会","en":"After retirement, a former engineer feared that his experience would become irrelevant. He did not yearn for a grand title, but he missed the satisfaction of solving a practical problem. A community centre invited him to mentor a small repair team.\nAt first, he expected unquestioning obedience. A younger volunteer found his manner stern and his instructions overly conservative. Rather than dismiss the disagreement, they discussed it openly. He learnt to explain the reason behind a procedure; she learnt to value knowledge acquired through years of practice. Their reciprocal respect became the project's greatest strength.\nThe engineer's contribution was not charity received but expertise shared. An ageing society benefits when it creates opportunities for meaningful involvement. Experience can complement youthful energy, provided neither group assumes automatic superiority. Respect grows through genuine collaboration, not a sentimental compliment offered once a year.","zh":"退休后，一位工程师担心经验失去意义。他不渴望头衔，却怀念解决实际问题的满足感。社区中心邀请他指导维修队。起初他希望大家绝对服从，年轻志愿者觉得他严厉、指令过分保守。双方公开讨论：他学着解释程序的原因，她学着重视多年实践积累的知识。相互尊重成为项目最大优势。工程师的参与不是接受施舍，而是分享专长。老龄社会能从有意义的参与机会中受益；只要彼此不自认天然优越，经验就能与年轻活力互补。尊重来自实际合作，而非一年一次的感伤赞美。","key":"Experience can complement youthful energy, provided neither group assumes automatic superiority. || complement 作动词意为互补；provided 引导条件从句。","task":"社会应该为老年人提供继续发挥专长的机会。 || Society should provide older people with opportunities to continue using their expertise.","q":"What changed after the disagreement was discussed? || Both participants learnt to explain or appreciate the other's perspective. 变化是双向的。","note":"","wc":140,"new":["conservative","yearn","reciprocal","compliment","stern","retirement","satisfaction","complement"]},{"id":"51","title":"移居之前的信息准备","en_title":"Preparing to Move Abroad","kind":"听力·出国与手续","en":"Before deciding to emigrate, Lan attended an information session about life in a foreign country. She learnt that immigrate describes entering a country to settle, while emigrate emphasizes leaving one. Her personal motive was to join an overseas research team, not to escape an immediate problem.\nShe checked her passport, visa, and the availability of accommodation. A consul at an embassy information event explained where to find official guidance. An ambassador's speech about diplomatic cooperation was interesting, but it could not answer her individual paperwork questions. Lan made a reservation, packed a suitcase, and kept a copy of her correspondence.\nShe also checked when her documents would expire and whether a dependant needed separate arrangements. No tempting shortcut could replace proper preparation. Moving abroad might be advantageous, but it would involve adaptation, expense, and uncertainty. A realistic decision required both hope and a clear understanding of the commitment.","zh":"兰决定移居前，参加国外生活说明会。她了解到 immigrate 强调迁入定居，emigrate 强调迁出；自己的动机是加入海外研究团队。她核查护照、签证与住宿供应。使馆活动中的领事介绍官方信息渠道，大使关于外交合作的讲话虽有趣，却不能回答个人手续问题。她预订住宿、装好行李并保存通信副本，也核查证件到期时间及受抚养人是否需单独安排。捷径不能取代准备。出国可能有利，但涉及适应、费用与不确定性，现实决定既需要希望，也需要理解承诺。","key":"Moving abroad might be advantageous, but it would involve adaptation, expense, and uncertainty. || might / would 表示审慎预期，三个名词并列呈现成本。","task":"作出重大决定之前，人们应该核实相关信息。 || People should verify relevant information before making a major decision.","q":"Why was the ambassador's speech insufficient for Lan? || It did not answer her individual paperwork questions. 区分宏观讲话与具体服务。","note":"","wc":148,"new":["availability","advantageous","emigrate","suitcase","foreign","diplomatic","correspondence","dependant","visa","expire","consul","shortcut","proper","motive","embassy","ambassador","passport","reservation","immigrate"]},{"id":"52","title":"小店为何会资金紧张","en_title":"Understanding a Cash Shortage","kind":"阅读·经济与经营","en":"A trader sold imported merchandise through a small outlet. Inflation raised his costs, and a fluctuation in currency values made the next order more expensive. Although demand remained steady, the business faced a shortage of cash. A dealer offered to finance a purchase, but the first installment would be due almost immediately.\nThe owner asked whether he could repay the debt if sales fell. A deposit was already tied up in an estate lease, and his mortgage still required payment. One failed assumption could push him towards default or leave the firm bankrupt. He chose to negotiate a smaller order and reduce excess stock.\nAn economics student used this example to explain why profit and liquidity differ. Prices can fluctuate, a commodity can lose value, and a seemingly profitable business can still struggle to meet immediate obligations. Thrifty management means planning ahead, not merely refusing every expenditure.","zh":"商贩通过小门店出售进口商品。通胀推高成本，汇率波动让下批货更贵。需求稳定，现金却短缺。经销商提出融资，但首期很快到期。店主考虑销售若下降能否还债：一笔押金占在物业租约中，按揭仍要支付。错误假设可能导致违约甚至破产。他决定协商减少订单、降低过量库存。经济学学生用此例解释利润与流动性的区别：价格会波动，商品会贬值，看似盈利的企业仍可能无法履行眼前义务。节俭管理是提前规划，不是一概拒绝支出。","key":"A seemingly profitable business can still struggle to meet immediate obligations. || seemingly 表示表象；meet obligations 为履行义务的搭配。","task":"销售稳定并不一定意味着企业有足够的现金。 || Steady sales do not necessarily mean that a business has sufficient cash.","q":"What did the owner choose to do? || Negotiate a smaller order and reduce excess stock. 根据现金压力调整规模。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["deposit","currency","inflation","negotiate","trader","dealer","merchandise","commodity","bankrupt","fell","economics","thrifty","excess","installment","estate","outlet","shortage","mortgage","fluctuation","fluctuate","repay","default"]},{"id":"53","title":"展会上如何提出好问题","en_title":"Asking Questions at a Trade Fair","kind":"听力·商务交流","en":"At a fair, a producer displayed a prototype with a patent application pending. Its spokesman praised an ingenious modification that could halve processing time. I asked for the specification, the conditions of the comparison, and a demonstration using an ordinary workpiece.\nThe machine had a modular design: one module could detach from another, and a handy fitting allowed adjustment. A cutter moved along a preset track while a roller guided the material. The output looked first-rate, but the representative admitted that a delicate garment required different settings. A promotional claim needed qualification.\nWe discussed a possible deal without making an immediate bid. A clear quotation would identify what the price included, what support was available, and who would be liable if delivery failed. Commercial courtesy does not require unquestioning acceptance. A buyer can remain gracious while asking firm, pertinent questions about a product's actual performance.","zh":"展会上，厂家展示一台专利申请中的原型机。发言人称巧妙改进能把加工时间减半，我询问规格、比较条件，并要求用普通工件演示。设备采用模块结构，模块可拆，便利配件能调节；切刀沿预设轨道走，滚轮引导材料。成品看似一流，但代表承认精细衣物需要不同设置，宣传必须有适用限制。双方讨论交易，却没立即报价。清楚的报价单要说明包含内容、售后支持和交货失败责任。商业礼貌不等于全盘接受，买方完全可以礼貌而坚定地询问实际性能。","key":"A buyer can remain gracious while asking firm, pertinent questions. || while + 动名词表示两种行为同时成立。","task":"评价一项宣传时，应该先了解比较是在什么条件下进行的。 || When evaluating a promotional claim, we should first understand the conditions under which the comparison was made.","q":"Why did the performance claim need qualification? || Different materials required different settings. 宣称不能脱离适用条件。","note":"","wc":145,"new":["deal","patent","specification","prototype","preset","liable","cutter","garment","fitting","producer","gracious","pertinent","module","bid","ingenious","modification","roller","detach","handy","spokesman","halve","first-rate"]},{"id":"54","title":"一场简朴的婚礼","en_title":"A Wedding within Our Means","kind":"听力·家庭与消费","en":"The bridegroom wanted a small wedding, although a cousin insisted that a grand engagement party was customary. The couple rejected an extravagant mansion and chose a community hall. A friend would take the photography, and relatives would prepare a light refreshment for each guest.\nThe bride wore a simple dress with a bead decoration and carried a tulip. Her partner looked radiant but nervous. A child tried to tickle his ear, making him grin and blush. During the ceremony, the couple made a vow to support one another. Nobody needed to dazzle the guests with expensive jewellery.\nAfterwards, we added pictures to an album and exchanged a small souvenir. The atmosphere was romantic because people showed sincere affection, not because a millionaire had paid the bill. A meaningful celebration can embody commitment and hospitality without becoming an unreasonable financial burden.","zh":"新郎想办小婚礼，尽管表亲坚持盛大订婚派对是惯例。两人放弃奢华宅邸，选择社区礼堂。朋友摄影，亲戚给每位宾客准备茶点。新娘穿珠饰简裙、拿郁金香，伴侣容光焕发却紧张。孩子挠他耳朵，让他咧嘴笑又脸红。仪式中两人誓言相互支持，无需用昂贵珠宝炫目。后来大家把照片放进相册，交换小纪念品。浪漫来自真诚情意，而非百万富翁买单。有意义的庆祝能体现承诺和好客，又不成为不合理负担。","key":"A meaningful celebration can embody commitment and hospitality without becoming an unreasonable financial burden. || without + 动名词表示避免伴随结果。","task":"庆祝活动的意义并不取决于花费的多少。 || The meaning of a celebration does not depend on how much is spent.","q":"Why did the couple choose a community hall? || They wanted a modest wedding within their means. 场地选择体现消费观。","note":"","wc":140,"new":["album","tulip","bead","radiant","bridegroom","customary","embody","vow","photography","extravagant","tickle","grin","blush","souvenir","engagement","romantic","hospitality","mansion","millionaire","refreshment","ear","dazzle"]},{"id":"55","title":"烘焙课上的耐心","en_title":"Patience in a Baking Class","kind":"听力·生活技能","en":"We began by separating an egg yolk from the white and measuring the flour. The teacher added yeast to one mixture and explained the need for time. Another group prepared a crisp biscuit, a fruit jelly, and a small pickle to accompany a savoury dish. Bacon and steak belonged to the next lesson, not today's menu.\nI tried to hurry and left a lump in the batter. The teacher asked me to stir evenly, scrape the rim, and let the mixture settle. A little extra liquid could soften it; too much would spoil the intended texture. We would bake one batch and compare it with another.\nAfterwards, we cleaned a stainless tray, removed grease from the counter, and checked the burner was off. The class reminded me that skill grows through attention. An ordinary task can teach restraint when impatience tempts us to skip a necessary step.","zh":"大家先分开蛋黄蛋清、称面粉。老师给一份混合物加酵母，解释等待的必要；另一组准备脆饼、果冻和配咸食的小腌菜。培根与牛排属于下次课，非本日菜单。我急躁，面糊留下一团块。老师让均匀搅拌、刮净容器边缘并静置。少量液体能使其变软，过多则破坏口感；我们烤两批比较。事后清洗不锈钢盘、擦去台面油脂并确认炉头关闭。技能通过留心成长，日常任务也能教人克制，避免因急躁跳过必要步骤。","key":"An ordinary task can teach restraint when impatience tempts us to skip a necessary step. || tempt sb. to do 表示诱使；when 从句给出具体情境。","task":"耐心完成每一个步骤，通常比一味求快更有效。 || Completing each step patiently is often more effective than simply trying to work faster.","q":"What mistake did the narrator make? || Hurrying left a lump in the batter. 原因与结果直接对应。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["evenly","pickle","bacon","skip","soften","yeast","jelly","grease","burner","yolk","steak","crisp","stainless","rim","lump","counter"]},{"id":"56","title":"牙科候诊室的阅读练习","en_title":"Reading in a Waiting Room","kind":"阅读·健康信息素养","en":"While waiting for a dentist, I read a leaflet about a cavity and another about the absorption of nutrients. A diagram showed how food could nourish the body, but it did not recommend the same intake for everyone. A vitamin supplement, the text cautioned, should not be confused with a complete diet.\nNearby material discussed deficiency, nourishment, and the interpretation of research. A study of a microscopic process might offer insight, yet its finding could not automatically justify a general claim. A headline about regenerative treatment required more context than the poster supplied.\nI wrote down a question rather than infer a personal diagnosis from the display. Public information is useful when it helps people ask better questions and locate reliable guidance. It becomes misleading when a limited observation is presented as a universal solution. Understanding the boundary between information and individual advice is itself a valuable reading skill.","zh":"等牙医时，我阅读龋洞和营养吸收传单。图示解释食物如何滋养身体，却没有给所有人建议同样摄入量。文中提醒，维生素补充剂不等于完整饮食。附近资料讨论营养缺乏及研究解读：微观过程研究可以提供启发，但不能自动证明一般主张。再生治疗标题所需语境比海报提供的更多。我记下问题，没有从展示推断个人诊断。公共信息若帮助人提出好问题、找到可靠指导就有用，把有限观察包装成万能方案则会误导。区分一般信息与个体建议，本身就是阅读能力。","key":"It becomes misleading when a limited observation is presented as a universal solution. || 被动语态突出信息被如何呈现，适合批判性阅读讨论。","task":"有限的研究结果不应该被描述成适用于所有人的解决方案。 || Limited research findings should not be presented as solutions that apply to everyone.","q":"What did the reader do instead of self-diagnosing? || Wrote down a question for clarification. 信息阅读后采取的行动。","note":"","wc":149,"new":["dentist","regenerative","microscopic","absorption","intake","vitamin","nourish","nourishment","deficiency","cavity","leaflet","supplement","infer"]},{"id":"57","title":"农场工具与劳动分工","en_title":"Tools and Work on a Farm","kind":"阅读·乡村与技术","en":"At the ranch, a farmer showed us an old waggon beside a diesel tractor. A bridle hung near the stable, and a wooden yoke recalled an earlier way of working. A bull stood apart from a buffalo, while a donkey, called an ass in an older account, waited quietly.\nWe watched workers thresh grain, inspect a seed's kernel, and prepare a bed for transplant work. A shovel helped move soil; a machine could perform the same task on a larger scale. Neither tool was ideal for every job. A hardy plant might survive where a delicate one would wither.\nThe farmer explained why care mattered during breeding. To breed animals responsibly required attention to their needs rather than merely increasing numbers. A child watched a chick hatch and later peck at food. The visit made visible the labour behind products that urban shoppers often treat as commonplace.","zh":"牧场里，农民展示柴油拖拉机旁的旧货车。马厩挂着笼头，木轭让人想起旧劳动方式。公牛与水牛分开站，一头旧文称 ass 的驴安静等待。工人脱粒、查看种仁、准备移栽苗床，铲子移土，机器则能扩大处理规模，但没有工具适合一切任务。耐寒健壮的植物可能在娇弱植物枯萎的地方生存。农民解释，负责任地繁育动物需要关注需求，而不只是增加数量。孩子看小鸡孵化，之后啄食。参观让城市消费者常视为平常的商品背后劳动显现出来。","key":"Neither tool was ideal for every job. || neither 否定两者；for every job 限定适用范围。","task":"技术的价值取决于它是否适合具体任务。 || The value of technology depends on whether it suits the particular task.","q":"What did the visit reveal to urban shoppers? || The labour behind everyday products. 细节最后汇成主题。","note":"ass 在此指驴，现代日常表达也可能有其他含义；写作中 donkey 更明确。waggon 为拼写变体，常见拼写 wagon。","wc":147,"new":["buffalo","hardy","commonplace","bull","ass","bridle","wither","yoke","thresh","waggon","shovel","diesel","hatch","kernel","breed","ranch","transplant","peck"]},{"id":"58","title":"铁匠铺与工业展厅","en_title":"From a Forge to a Factory","kind":"阅读·工业史","en":"A blacksmith heated metal in a forge and used a hammer to shape it. The museum placed this scene beside a display on metallurgy. Labels distinguished ferrous material from other metals and explained how coke and charcoal appeared in historical processes. We observed the tools without attempting the work ourselves.\nIn the modern section, a lathe cut a groove into a demonstration piece. A guide described how workers lubricate machinery, inspect a valve, and remove dust before it causes trouble. A steel frame could brace a structure; cement could help form a foundation. A blast furnace model illustrated a very different scale of production.\nIndustrial progress involved more than larger machines. Standard procedures, training, and maintenance were instrumental in improving reliability. A small workplace could still excel by selecting suitable equipment and checking each stage carefully. Technical change matters when it improves the quality of work as well as the quantity of output.","zh":"铁匠在炉中加热金属，用锤成形。博物馆将此场景放在冶金展旁，标签区分含铁材料与其他金属，说明焦炭、木炭在历史工艺中的用途。大家只观察工具，不亲自操作。现代区的车床在演示件上切槽，导游解释润滑设备、检查阀门、清除积尘的重要性。钢架能支撑结构，水泥帮助形成地基，高炉模型则展示另一生产规模。工业进步不只是机器变大，标准程序、培训和维护都帮助提高可靠性。小作坊也能通过选对设备、细查各环节表现出色。技术变化若同时改善工作质量与产量，才有意义。","key":"Technical change matters when it improves the quality of work as well as the quantity of output. || as well as 连接两个评价维度。","task":"可靠的生产既需要设备，也需要培训和维护。 || Reliable production requires training and maintenance as well as equipment.","q":"What helped improve reliability besides machinery? || Standard procedures, training, and maintenance. 考查并列信息。","note":"","wc":153,"new":["brace","cement","instrumental","metallurgy","blacksmith","ferrous","charcoal","lubricate","excel","dust","coke","blast","valve","forge","lathe","groove"]},{"id":"59","title":"小说中的人物不能只看标签","en_title":"Reading a Character Closely","kind":"阅读·文学与判断","en":"Our literary seminar examined a novel about a lonely bachelor and his wealthy patron. At first, the narrator presented the patron as a haughty snob whose bourgeois tastes were beyond criticism. Yet a later chapter revealed generosity that the earlier description had concealed.\nThe teacher asked us to separate a character's voice from the author's position. A maid, a mistress of a household, and a travelling missionary each saw the same incident differently. Their discourse reflected personality, prejudice, and experience. A hostile remark might characterize its speaker more accurately than its target.\nWe compared the novel's prose with a short verse about longing. Neither text offered a simple lesson in morality. Both encouraged us to ponder how perception shapes judgment. Close reading requires more than choosing a sympathetic character: it asks us to notice whose account dominates and which details complicate it.","zh":"文学讨论班研究一部关于孤独单身男子和富有资助者的小说。起初，叙述者把资助者写成傲慢势利者，其资产阶级趣味不容批评；后文却揭露先前未写出的慷慨。老师要求区分人物声音与作者立场。女佣、女主人和旅行传教士对同一事件看法不同，话语反映个性、偏见与经历。敌意评论可能更能说明说话者，而非评论对象。大家将小说散文与表达渴望的诗比较：两者都不提供简单道德教训，而让人思考感知如何塑造判断。细读不只是选同情的人物，还要注意谁主导叙述、哪些细节使其复杂。","key":"A hostile remark might characterize its speaker more accurately than its target. || might 表示文本推断；比较级呈现反向解读。","task":"理解小说人物时，我们需要考虑叙述者的立场。 || When interpreting a fictional character, we need to consider the narrator's perspective.","q":"Why did the later chapter matter? || It revealed generosity that complicated the earlier portrayal. 后文修正初始印象。","note":"","wc":142,"new":["bourgeois","bachelor","snob","verse","maid","prose","personality","mistress","prejudice","longing","ponder","generosity","literary","discourse","hostile","morality","missionary","characterize","patron","haughty"]},{"id":"60","title":"旧文献里的词义变化","en_title":"Words across Time","kind":"阅读·语体与旧义","en":"An archive displayed a telex message, a postal notice, and a typed report produced before a modern printer became commonplace. A visitor asked whether xerox could be used as a verb. The librarian explained its association with photocopying and recommended neutral wording in formal work.\nLanguage also changes in social contexts. An older text might use intercourse to describe communication, while contemporary readers often associate it with sexual activity. A historical author might call someone a dwarf or an idiot, terms that can be inappropriate when applied to people today. Quoting such language requires context, not casual imitation.\nThe class compared a dictionary's older sense with current usage. An entry's presence did not mean every meaning was equally suitable for an essay. The lesson was to read generously but write selectively. A strong vocabulary includes knowing when a word will convey the intended meaning and when it may create an unintended impression.","zh":"档案馆展示电传信息、邮政通知及现代打印机普及前的打字报告。有人问 xerox 能否作动词，管理员解释其与复印的联系，并建议正式写作选中性表达。社会语境也会改变词义：旧文 intercourse 可指交往，如今读者常联想到性行为；历史作者可能用 dwarf 或 idiot 称人，今天这样称呼可能不妥。引用需交代语境，不宜随手模仿。大家比较词典旧义与当前用法，词条存在不等于所有义项都适合作文。阅读应广泛理解，写作则有选择。词汇能力也包括知道何时能准确传意、何时会引发意外印象。","key":"An entry's presence did not mean every meaning was equally suitable for an essay. || not ... every 是部分否定，强调词义与语域选择。","task":"掌握一个词也包括了解它适合什么语境。 || Knowing a word also involves understanding the contexts in which it is appropriate.","q":"What does “write selectively” mean here? || Choose meanings and registers appropriate to the intended context. 不是故意少写信息。","note":"此篇专门辨析旧义与语体，文中的词不宜全部当作作文推荐表达。xerox 涉及品牌衍生用法，正式表达可用 photocopy。","wc":152,"new":["postal","printer","intercourse","telex","convey","idiot","dwarf","xerox"]},{"id":"61","title":"面对愤怒时如何回应","en_title":"Choosing a Response","kind":"写作·人际沟通","en":"After a harsh remark, my first impulse was to retort. I felt furious, and my fury made a minor dispute seem monstrous. I wanted to denounce the speaker, ridicule his conceit, and embarrass him in front of everyone. Fortunately, a friend asked me to pause.\nShe did not dismiss my hurt. Instead, she helped me distinguish a thoughtless comment from deliberate malice. To sneer, scoff, or hurl an insult would merely heighten the conflict. It would not explain why the remark was offensive. I decided to state my objection with firmness and ask for a proper response.\nThe conversation remained awkward, but the other person eventually apologized. I could accept that without pretending the incident had been nice. Tact does not require passive resignation. It requires enough restraint to address a problem without allowing wrath, jealousy, or spite to govern the exchange. A measured response can be courageous precisely because it resists an easy outburst.","zh":"听到严厉评论，我最初想反驳。愤怒让小争执显得可怕，我想公开谴责、嘲笑对方自负，让他难堪。朋友请我停一停。她没有否定我的受伤，而帮助区分轻率言论与蓄意恶意。冷笑、讥讽或辱骂只会加剧冲突，不能解释言论为何冒犯。我决定坚定表达异议并要求适当回应。谈话仍尴尬，对方最终道歉，我接受但不假装经历愉快。得体不等于消极顺从，而是克制地解决问题，不让暴怒、嫉妒和怨恨支配交流。平静回应正因抵制轻易爆发而可能勇敢。","key":"Tact does not require passive resignation. || 简短否定句澄清概念，可接 It requires ... 给出正面定义。","task":"坚定地表达异议，并不意味着必须侮辱对方。 || Expressing disagreement firmly does not mean having to insult the other person.","q":"Why would insults have been unhelpful? || They would heighten conflict without explaining the objection. 关注行为能否解决问题。","note":"","wc":155,"new":["conceit","courageous","nice","resignation","hurt","embarrass","denounce","thoughtless","hurl","offensive","furious","fury","monstrous","firmness","heighten","tact","malice","spite","jealousy","harsh","wrath","scoff","retort","sneer"]},{"id":"62","title":"悬疑故事中的线索","en_title":"Clues in a Radio Drama","kind":"听力·故事与推断","en":"In a radio drama, a sheriff received a report that a burglar had tried to steal an antique. A watchful guard heard a clatter, saw a figure flee, and called a patrol. The suspected outlaw left a badge behind, but it might have been fake.\nA second scene introduced a notorious gangster and a rumour that he planned to kidnap a dealer. The police could not detain someone merely because a frightening story sounded plausible. They had to examine evidence and follow the required procedure. The narrator mentioned a warrant without explaining its legal details.\nAt the climax, the apparent villain turned out to be a witness. The real motive involved greed and a failed attempt to smuggle stolen ware. The story taught listeners to separate a clue from an assumption. A dramatic voice can make a questionable explanation sound persuasive, but suspense is not proof.","zh":"广播剧里，警长接报窃贼企图盗古董。警觉守卫听到碰撞声、看见身影逃跑并叫巡逻人员。疑犯遗下徽章，却可能是假货。第二幕引出臭名昭著的歹徒，以及他计划绑架商人的传言。不能仅凭吓人故事似乎可信就拘留某人，必须查证并遵循程序。旁白提到令状，但未讲法律细节。高潮时，看似反派的人其实是证人，真实动机涉及贪婪和走私赃物未遂。故事提醒听众区分线索与假设。戏剧化声音会让可疑解释听着有说服力，但悬念不是证明。","key":"A dramatic voice can make a questionable explanation sound persuasive. || make + 宾语 + 动词原形；区分表达效果与证据质量。","task":"一个听起来可信的故事仍然需要证据支持。 || A plausible story still needs supporting evidence.","q":"Why was the abandoned badge not decisive proof? || It might have been fake. 线索存在其他解释。","note":"","wc":146,"new":["watchful","kidnap","burglar","patrol","warrant","steal","flee","outlaw","greed","smuggle","ware","questionable","sheriff","fake","badge","gangster","clatter","detain","notorious"]},{"id":"63","title":"球场上的规则与尊重","en_title":"Fair Play on the Field","kind":"听力·运动与规则","en":"At a baseball match, a spectator shouted when the referee made an unpopular call. A player wanted to argue, but the captain urged everyone to resume play. Being a champion, she said, did not entitle a team to disregard a rule or treat an opponent as inferior.\nLater, a runner slipped and began to limp. The game paused while staff checked the situation. Another player tried to shove past a rival; the coach immediately challenged that foul behaviour. To cheat, threaten, or deliberately hurt someone was a violation of the spirit of the match.\nOur team lost by a narrow margin. A disappointed supporter muttered, “Damn,” then joined the applause. The word expressed informal frustration, not language to imitate in an academic essay. The captain chose to credit the winners and commend her own team for its effort. Respect matters most when the result is unwelcome.","zh":"棒球赛中，裁判作出不受欢迎判罚，观众大喊。一名球员想争辩，队长劝继续比赛：冠军身份不允许无视规则或轻视对手。后来跑者滑倒跛行，比赛暂停让工作人员查看。另一球员推搡对手，教练立即指出犯规。作弊、威胁或蓄意伤害违背体育精神。球队惜败，一名球迷低声说“该死”，随后鼓掌。damn 表示非正式沮丧，不适合照搬到学术作文。队长肯定胜者，也称赞自己队伍的努力。结果不如意时，尊重尤其重要。","key":"Respect matters most when the result is unwelcome. || when 从句把抽象价值落实到困难情境。","task":"真正的体育精神也体现在如何面对失败。 || True sportsmanship is also reflected in how people respond to defeat.","q":"How did the captain react to losing? || She credited the winners and praised her team's effort. 不把失败转化为对他人的攻击。","note":"damn 是非正式感叹语，此处用于听力识别，不推荐写进正式作文。","wc":146,"new":["damn","inferior","violation","shove","deliberately","cheat","limp","champion","commend","rule","disregard","baseball","foul","referee","resume","credit"]},{"id":"64","title":"车站里的一次延误","en_title":"A Delay at the Station","kind":"听力·出行信息","en":"At the platform, an announcement said our train would not depart on time. A shuttle would take passengers to a nearby station. We needed to keep our ticket and board at the marked point. An attendant asked the crowd not to shove and helped a passenger carrying a cane.\nOutside, traffic approached a roundabout. A horn sounded as a driver tried to overtake a slow vehicle near a pedestrian crossing. Farther along the motorway, a crash had caused the original delay. Staff would divert the replacement bus past a garage and a motel before returning to the main road.\nI wanted to cancel the journey, but a clear explanation reduced my annoyance. We could claim the stated compensation through the operator's process, though the attendant did not promise an immediate payment. Travel disruption becomes less distressing when accurate information replaces speculation and passengers know what to do next.","zh":"站台公告说列车不能准时出发，接驳车将送乘客去附近车站，需保留车票并在标记处上车。工作人员请人群别推挤，帮助拄手杖乘客。外面车流驶近环岛，司机在人行横道附近试图超慢车，喇叭响起。高速公路更远处的碰撞造成原延误，替代巴士将绕经车库与汽车旅馆再回主路。我想取消行程，但清晰解释缓解烦躁。乘客可按运营方流程申领所述补偿，工作人员并没保证立刻付款。准确信息替代猜测、下一步明确时，出行中断就没那么令人困扰。","key":"Travel disruption becomes less distressing when accurate information replaces speculation. || become + 比较级形容词，说明服务改善的条件。","task":"及时提供准确的信息能够减轻乘客的焦虑。 || Providing accurate information promptly can reduce passengers' anxiety.","q":"Did the attendant promise immediate compensation? || No. Passengers had to use the operator's stated process. 避免把可申请误听为已支付。","note":"","wc":148,"new":["crash","platform","roundabout","overtake","divert","cancel","garage","motel","motorway","horn","pedestrian","compensation","shuttle","cane","ticket"]},{"id":"65","title":"小狗不懂人的标签","en_title":"Learning to Observe Behaviour","kind":"阅读·动物与观察","en":"My little pal called our puppy a rascal because it would gnaw a slipper, grab a mitten, and make a mess. It might wag its tail at a visitor, then growl at an unfamiliar noise. Once, a wasp made it leap sideways and howl; a moment later it began to sniff the grass again.\nAn animal-care volunteer asked us not to ascribe every action to a human motive. A hound might follow a scent, a cat might twitch a whisker, and a bird might flutter before settling on a perch. These behaviours required observation rather than a story about good or evil intentions.\nWe learnt to avoid teasing the puppy or encouraging it to snap. A youngster should not poke an animal simply to make it react. Understanding grew when we noticed patterns, respected space, and asked knowledgeable people for guidance. Affection is more useful when it is accompanied by attention to another creature's needs.","zh":"小伙伴称小狗淘气鬼，因为它啃拖鞋、抢手套、弄乱屋子。它向访客摇尾，对陌生声音低吼；一次被黄蜂吓得侧跳嚎叫，片刻又嗅草。动物照护志愿者要求别把一切动作都归因于人的动机：猎犬循气味，猫动胡须，鸟扑翅后停枝，都需要观察，而非编善恶意图故事。我们学着不逗弄小狗、不鼓励咬人，孩子不该只为看反应而戳动物。留意规律、尊重空间、向懂行者求助，理解才会增长。感情伴随对需求的关注才更有帮助。","key":"Affection is more useful when it is accompanied by attention to another creature's needs. || 被动结构 be accompanied by 表示相伴条件。","task":"喜爱动物也意味着尊重它们的行为和空间。 || Caring about animals also means respecting their behaviour and space.","q":"What did the volunteer discourage? || Assigning human motives to every animal action. 避免过度拟人化推断。","note":"","wc":155,"new":["sniff","wag","evil","whisker","mess","snap","rascal","mitten","gnaw","wasp","pal","howl","hound","youngster","poke","ascribe","perch","flutter","growl","grab"]},{"id":"66","title":"关于情绪的课堂讨论","en_title":"Understanding Difficult Feelings","kind":"写作·心理与支持","en":"In a psychology class, students discussed anxiety, melancholy, and depression as terms requiring care. A sorrowful day did not automatically establish a disorder, and a cheerful appearance did not prove that someone was free from distress. A person's inner experience could remain largely hidden.\nThe class examined a fictional student whose nightmare and persistent worry began to haunt his daily life. He feared being called pathetic, incapable, or unfit for study. Such labels could intensify his misery and make him reluctant to seek support. A friend chose to listen without ridicule and helped him contact the campus service.\nThe lecturer also discussed responsible reporting of suicide: language should avoid sensationalism and respect those affected. No dramatic story could substitute for appropriate professional assessment. The lesson emphasized compassion and the limits of casual judgment. We need not solve every problem ourselves to offer patient, humane support.","zh":"心理学课讨论焦虑、忧郁和抑郁等需谨慎使用的术语。一天难过不自动构成障碍，外表开心也不能证明没有困扰，内在经历可能隐而不见。案例中的虚构学生被噩梦与持续担忧影响生活，害怕被说可悲、无能或不适合学习。这些标签会加重痛苦，使他不敢求助。朋友选择不嘲笑地倾听，帮助联系校园支持服务。讲师也讨论负责任的自杀报道：避免煽情，尊重受影响者。戏剧化故事不能取代适当专业评估。课程强调同情与随意判断的局限。提供耐心、人性化支持，不要求我们独自解决一切。","key":"A cheerful appearance did not prove that someone was free from distress. || prove that 后接判断内容，强调外表不足以证明内在状态。","task":"耐心倾听可以帮助一个人更愿意寻求支持。 || Patient listening can help a person feel more willing to seek support.","q":"How did the friend respond? || Listened without ridicule and helped the student contact campus support. 具体支持行为。","note":"","wc":145,"new":["psychology","depression","incapable","misery","sorrowful","nightmare","haunt","unfit","pathetic","suicide","melancholy"]},{"id":"67","title":"山谷中的地质记录","en_title":"Reading a Landscape","kind":"阅读·地质与环境","en":"Our geology class visited a plateau above a river. Layers of rock recorded deposition, while a steep bank showed signs of erosion. A guide explained that a landscape could change through processes too slow to notice in a single afternoon. Its apparent stillness did not imply permanence.\nWe compared a dry channel with one carrying cloudy water. A small flake of stone rested beside a larger fragment. Above us, a massive cliff rose to a striking elevation, and a stream disappeared beneath an opaque pool. The teacher asked us to describe what we could observe before discussing its origin.\nNo one was permitted to collect material indiscriminately. The purpose was to connect evidence with an explanation, not to fill a bag with souvenirs. A dramatic view could fascinate us, but scientific understanding required attention to scale, time, and alternative accounts of how the feature had formed.","zh":"地质课前往河流上方高原，岩层记录沉积，陡岸显示侵蚀。导游解释，景观变化可能慢到一下午察觉不到，看似静止不等于永恒。我们比较干河道与流着浑水的河道，小石片靠着大碎块。上方巨大崖壁高耸，溪流隐入不透明水潭。老师要求先描述观察，再讨论成因。不得随意采集材料，目的是联系证据与解释，而非装满纪念品。壮观景色能使人着迷，但科学理解还需关注尺度、时间和不同成因解释。","key":"Its apparent stillness did not imply permanence. || apparent 与 imply 区分表象和推论，适合科学说明。","task":"理解自然景观需要同时考虑空间尺度和时间。 || Understanding a natural landscape requires considering both spatial scale and time.","q":"What were students asked to do before explaining origins? || Describe what they could observe. 观察先于成因解释。","note":"","wc":146,"new":["flake","deposition","fascinate","stillness","cloudy","plateau","elevation","dry","erosion","geology","fill","massive","opaque"]},{"id":"68","title":"微小变化的实验","en_title":"Measuring Small Changes","kind":"阅读·实验设计","en":"We used a pendulum to examine periodic motion. Its regularity looked impressive, but the teacher asked us to measure rather than assume. A small change in length could affect the result. We recorded a vector's direction in one exercise and a scalar magnitude in another, taking care not to confuse them.\nNext, a magnet helped demonstrate attraction and repulsion. We observed polarity and discussed magnetism before considering induction in a separate apparatus. A nearby display showed how a filament could glow and how a narrow opening formed a slit in an optical experiment.\nEach group had to tabulate observations, compare the resultant values, and explain a possible source of error. A parameter was held constant while another changed. Where a relation appeared inversely proportional, we checked several points. Scientific confidence increased through repeated examination, not because the first result looked elegant.","zh":"我们用摆研究周期运动。规律看似明显，老师仍要求测量，长度小变化也可能影响结果。练习分别记录矢量方向与标量大小，避免混淆。随后用磁铁演示吸引与排斥，观察极性、讨论磁性，再用另一装置考虑感应。旁边展示灯丝发光及光学实验狭缝。各组必须列表记录、比较所得数值并解释误差来源，一个参数固定，另一个变化。关系似乎成反比时，还要检验多个点。科学信心通过重复检查增强，而不是因为首个结果漂亮。","key":"A parameter was held constant while another changed. || while 对照控制变量和变化变量；被动语态适合描述实验。","task":"我们应该通过重复测量来检验最初的判断。 || We should test our initial judgment through repeated measurements.","q":"Why were several points checked? || To examine whether the apparent proportional relationship held. 不以单点代替规律。","note":"","wc":141,"new":["resultant","magnet","periodic","inversely","filament","vector","slit","induction","polarity","regularity","magnitude","magnetism","parameter","tabulate","pendulum"]},{"id":"69","title":"从毕业论文到研究表达","en_title":"Turning Evidence into a Thesis","kind":"写作·学术表达","en":"My thesis examined the adoption of a new teaching method. I had to formulate a proposition, explain its derivation, and identify what would count as supporting evidence. The first draft was deficient in detail and relied on an analogy that did not fit the data.\nMy supervisor asked me to distinguish a constituent of the model from an assumption about the whole. I should not postulate a mechanism merely to explain away an inconvenient result. Nor could I claim that two trends must correlate simply because their timing happened to coincide.\nI revised the formulation, placed extra tables in an appendix, and prepared a synthesis of the findings. The conclusion acknowledged a marginal effect and a substantial limitation. The process was demanding, but it helped me appreciate why rigorous expression matters. A sound argument remains open to revision when new evidence challenges its premises.","zh":"毕业论文研究新教学法的采用。我需提出命题、解释推导，并明确何种证据能支持。初稿细节不足，类比也不符数据。导师要求区分模型组成部分与对整体的假设，不能只为搪塞不利结果而假定机制，也不能因两个趋势恰好同时出现，就断言相关。我修改表述，把额外表格放附录，综合研究发现，结论承认效果很小且局限明显。过程费力，却让我理解严谨表达的重要。新证据挑战前提时，可靠论证仍应允许修改。","key":"Nor could I claim that two trends must correlate simply because their timing happened to coincide. || nor 句首部分倒装；simply because 指出理由不足。","task":"一篇有说服力的论文也应该承认自身的局限。 || A persuasive thesis should also acknowledge its own limitations.","q":"What was wrong with the first draft? || It lacked detail and used an analogy that did not fit the data. 两个问题并列。","note":"","wc":144,"new":["derivation","postulate","constituent","analogy","coincide","adoption","deficient","count","proposition","formulation","thesis","marginal","correlate","synthesis","appendix","rigorous"]},{"id":"70","title":"面试中的表达与倾听","en_title":"Speaking without Performing Confidence","kind":"听力·面试技巧","en":"Before the interview, I was tempted to memorize an elaborate speech. My adviser warned that eloquence could not conceal an absence of relevant experience. A clear example would be more useful than a lofty declaration about being exceptional.\nWe practised answering without rambling. I would state the situation, describe my action, and explain the outcome. When I began to ramble, she asked me to return to the question. I learnt not to flatter an interviewer or claim expertise I did not possess. Modesty did not require hiding an achievement; sincerity required describing it accurately.\nOn the day, one question seemed designed to baffle me. I paused, admitted the uncertainty, and explained how I would investigate. The panel appeared interested. I left without knowing the result, but with a better understanding of communication: a thoughtful response can reveal more intellect than a quick display of confidence.","zh":"面试前，我想背精致长演说。顾问提醒，口才掩盖不了相关经验缺失，清楚案例比宣称自己非凡的高调表态有用。练习中，我依次交代情境、行动和结果，一跑题她就让我回到问题。我学着不奉承面试官，也不冒称专长。谦逊不要求隐藏成绩，真诚则要求准确描述。当天一个问题似乎故意难倒我，我停顿、承认不确定，并解释会怎样调查。评委似乎有兴趣。离开时虽不知结果，却更理解沟通：深思熟虑的回答比急着表现自信更能展现智慧。","key":"Modesty did not require hiding an achievement; sincerity required describing it accurately. || 两个平行分句辨析谦逊与真诚。","task":"承认不知道某件事，并不意味着缺乏学习能力。 || Admitting that one does not know something does not imply a lack of ability to learn.","q":"How did the narrator handle the difficult question? || Admitted uncertainty and explained how to investigate. 不是编造确定答案。","note":"","wc":145,"new":["sincerity","eloquence","ramble","baffle","modesty","exceptional","intellect","lofty","flatter"]},{"id":"71","title":"公共会议上的意见与行动","en_title":"From a Petition to a Decision","kind":"写作·公共参与","en":"At a public convention, a senator invited residents to discuss proposed legislation. One advocate wanted to repeal an outdated prohibition; another urged the council to retain a regulation that protected a vulnerable group. The controversy concerned both fairness and the possibility of unintended effects.\nThe chair asked speakers to cite evidence, refrain from personal attacks, and acknowledge a reasonable concession. A coalition offered an allied campaign, but members would not accept an ally who encouraged a riot. They preferred to mobilize support through a peaceful rally and a clearly stated pledge.\nAfter debate, the council agreed to initiate a review and announce its findings annually. A proposed veto was withdrawn, and a subsidiary committee would handle technical questions. The mayor would inaugurate the consultation rather than dictate its outcome. Public participation can counter inertia when citizens turn dissatisfaction into a practicable proposal. Strong conviction matters, but persuasion also requires listening to people whose priorities differ from our own.","zh":"公共会议上，参议员邀请居民讨论立法。一位倡导者要求废除旧禁令，另一位主张保留保护弱势群体的规定，争议关乎公平及意外影响。主席要求引用证据、克制人身攻击并接受合理让步。联盟愿意联合行动，却不接受鼓励骚乱的盟友，倾向和平集会与明确承诺。议会同意启动审查、每年公布结果，拟议否决被撤回，附属委员会处理技术问题；市长负责开启咨询而非决定结论。公民将不满化为可行建议，就能克服惰性。信念重要，但说服也需要倾听不同优先事项。","key":"Public participation can counter inertia when citizens turn dissatisfaction into a practicable proposal. || turn A into B 描述将情绪转化为可行动方案。","task":"建设性的参与需要把不满转化为具体建议。 || Constructive participation requires turning dissatisfaction into concrete proposals.","q":"What kind of campaign did the coalition prefer? || A peaceful rally with a clearly stated pledge. 与骚乱明确区分。","note":"","wc":158,"new":["controversy","cite","refrain","pledge","concession","persuasion","annually","practicable","ally","allied","legislation","possibility","inaugurate","initiate","prohibition","regulation","inertia","convention","veto","subsidiary","mobilize","repeal","senator","dissatisfaction","advocate","announce","rally","riot"]},{"id":"72","title":"报道应该如何措辞","en_title":"Editing a Sensitive Report","kind":"阅读·新闻与表达","en":"Our editor received a draft describing an assault, a hostage incident, and a suspected terrorist threat. The writer had used the same dramatic language for all three. The editor asked whether each label was supported and whether the reader could distinguish confirmed information from an allegation.\nShe would not let an adjective substitute for evidence. A headline might trigger panic, and a careless phrase could propagate an unverified claim. The newsroom had to relay accurate information, correct a misleading passage, and avoid turning a person's suffering into a sensation.\nWe revised the text to denote the known facts precisely. A direct quotation remained a quotation; it did not become the publication's own conclusion. The exercise helped us understand that word choice can either enlighten or bewilder. Responsible reporting should inform the public without exploiting fear, and it should remain open to correction when subsequent evidence changes the account.","zh":"编辑收到一份同时描述袭击、人质事件与疑似恐怖威胁的稿子，作者全用同样戏剧化语言。编辑问，每个标签是否有依据，读者能否区分已证实信息与指控。形容词不能代替证据，标题可能引发恐慌，草率措辞会传播未核实主张。编辑部须传递准确信息、纠正误导段落，避免把痛苦变成轰动。我们修改文字来准确表示已知事实，直接引语仍是引语，不变成刊物自己的结论。选词能启发也能迷惑。负责报道应告知公众而不利用恐惧，后续证据改变叙述时要允许纠正。","key":"A direct quotation remained a quotation; it did not become the publication's own conclusion. || 平行分句区分转述与认定，适合媒介素养讨论。","task":"新闻报道应清楚区分已证实的事实与未经证实的指控。 || News reports should clearly distinguish confirmed facts from unverified allegations.","q":"Why did the editor question the labels? || They might not all be supported by confirmed evidence. 用词强度需要证据匹配。","note":"","wc":148,"new":["denote","assault","hostage","enlighten","bewilder","panic","terrorist","sensation","relay","propagate","trigger"]},{"id":"73","title":"修理工作中的小动作","en_title":"Small Actions at a Workbench","kind":"听力·动作与顺序","en":"The instructor asked me to unfold a cloth and place the broken frame on it. I would first untie a cord, loosen a clip, and straighten a crooked strip. Then I could use tape to hold the pieces temporarily. A narrow tack would secure the final covering, but I should not pierce the wrong layer.\nBeside me, a student tried to twist a wire too sharply. It began to deform. Another tugged at a loose thread and made the fabric rip. We stopped, examined the damage, and learnt to apply less force. A stitch could mend the tear; a clamp would keep the joint tightly aligned.\nThe demonstration was a lesson in restraint. We must not fling tools onto the bench, squash a delicate part, or scratch the surface through haste. To repair something well is to understand what each small action will change. Patience prevents damage that greater strength cannot undo.","zh":"老师让我展开布、放上破框。先解绳、松夹子、拉直歪条，再用胶带临时固定。小钉固定最后覆盖层，但别刺错层。旁边学生把金属丝扭得太急，开始变形；另一人拉松线使布撕裂。我们停下检查，学着减力。针脚能补破口，夹具保持接头紧密对齐。这是克制训练：不能甩工具、压坏精细部件，或因着急划伤表面。修好物品意味着理解每个小动作带来的改变。耐心能预防力量无法挽回的损坏。","key":"To repair something well is to understand what each small action will change. || 不定式作主语与表语，形成行为与能力的对应。","task":"修理物品之前，应先理解每个部件的作用。 || Before repairing an object, we should understand the function of each component.","q":"What caused the wire to deform? || It was twisted too sharply. 留意程度副词。","note":"","wc":152,"new":["unfold","stitch","sharply","squash","tape","crooked","twist","deform","rip","scratch","tack","tightly","untie","clip","pierce","straighten","fling"]},{"id":"74","title":"液体实验中的观察","en_title":"Watching a Liquid Change","kind":"阅读·物理化学","en":"In a recorded experiment, a scientist poured a viscous liquid into a flask. A filter removed visible particles before the solution entered a second vessel. We watched a solid dissolve, a bubble rise, and a thin layer of foam appear. The instructor asked us to record these changes without inventing a cause.\nAnother demonstration compared evaporation under different humidity conditions. To evaporate was not to vanish without a trace; matter had moved into another form. A sample reached saturation, while an adjacent container held a weaker mixture. We discussed concentration, compression, and the need to keep measurements comparable.\nThe teacher used an animation to show how one process might induce another. A catalyst appeared in a separate example, and the class considered the distinction between speeding a process and changing its final result. The lesson's purpose was observational discipline: a striking transformation should prompt a careful question, not an immediate, unsupported explanation.","zh":"录播实验中，科学家把黏稠液体倒入烧瓶，过滤器除去可见颗粒，液体进入第二容器。大家看固体溶解、气泡上升、薄泡沫出现。老师要求记录变化，不凭空编原因。另一演示比较不同湿度下的蒸发。蒸发不是无踪消失，而是物质转为另一形态。一份样品达到饱和，相邻容器是更稀混合物。大家讨论浓度、压缩与测量可比性。动画展示一个过程可能诱发另一个，另例出现催化剂，并区分加快过程与改变最终结果。课程目的在于规范观察：明显变化应引出认真问题，而非立刻给出无依据解释。","key":"A striking transformation should prompt a careful question, not an immediate, unsupported explanation. || should 表示建议；平行名词短语区分提问与臆断。","task":"观察到变化并不意味着我们已经理解了它的原因。 || Observing a change does not mean that we already understand its cause.","q":"What did the instructor ask students to avoid? || Inventing a cause before examining evidence. 观察与解释不能跳步。","note":"","wc":152,"new":["viscous","compression","evaporate","humidity","induce","flask","adjacent","foam","filter","comparable","dissolve","catalyst","saturation"]},{"id":"75","title":"在不同生境之间比较","en_title":"Comparing Habitats","kind":"阅读·自然与比较","en":"A school display compared a tropical jungle, an open prairie, and a wooded valley. One map marked the Tropic of Cancer, while another showed where birds migrate. The children noticed an abundance of life in every scene, but the dominant forms differed.\nIn a short film, a cuckoo called near a maple, a snake described as a serpent moved through leaves, and a predator pursued its prey. The teacher warned against calling an unfamiliar creature an alien monster. Its appearance might seem peculiar to us, yet it belonged to its own environment.\nWe examined how a web could trap an insect and how a plant's growth might be limited by scarcity of water. No habitat contained perpetual plenty. Ecological understanding grows when we compare relationships rather than rank landscapes by beauty. Even a place that appears empty can sustain life adapted to conditions that would challenge other organisms.","zh":"学校展览比较热带丛林、开阔草原和林木山谷。一幅图标北回归线，另一幅展示候鸟迁移地。每处生命丰富，但优势类型不同。短片里，布谷鸟在枫树旁叫，被称为 serpent 的蛇穿叶而行，捕食者追猎物。老师提醒别把陌生生物叫外来怪物：外观对我们奇特，却属于自身环境。大家考察蛛网捕虫及缺水限制植物生长，没有栖息地永远丰裕。比较关系而不是按美景排名，才能理解生态。看似空旷之地也可维系适应特定条件的生命。","key":"Its appearance might seem peculiar to us, yet it belonged to its own environment. || yet 引导转折，提示避免以观察者熟悉程度评价对象。","task":"不同物种能够适应不同的环境条件。 || Different species can adapt to different environmental conditions.","q":"What did the teacher recommend comparing? || Ecological relationships rather than scenic beauty. 比较标准是核心。","note":"","wc":148,"new":["perpetual","web","alien","dominant","serpent","tropic","tropical","scarcity","migrate","maple","prey","monster","abundance","cuckoo","prairie","jungle"]},{"id":"76","title":"航海故事中的动作与位置","en_title":"A Boat in Changing Weather","kind":"听力·位置与动作","en":"In a training story, a crew prepared to moor a small boat beside a sheltered cape. One person held an oar while another checked the mast and the line at the stern. A windy afternoon had made the return slower than expected.\nWhen a rope began to tangle, the captain told the crew to pause. They must not let a loose loop catch a foot or allow impatience to propel the boat into a rock. A nearby vessel offered to tow them the final distance. Once secure, they could step ashore and examine the problem.\nThe instructor contrasted this practical account with a romance about a pirate and a tragic shipwreck. Adventure writing could thrill a reader, but it often concealed the ordinary preparation behind safe travel. The class learnt the difference between enjoying a story and treating its dramatic actions as a guide to real behaviour.","zh":"训练故事中，船员准备把小船系在避风海角旁。一人持桨，另一人查看桅杆与船尾绳。下午风大，返程比预计慢。绳子缠绕时，船长要求停下，避免绳圈套脚，也不能因急躁把船推向岩石。附近船只愿拖完最后一段。固定后，大家才能上岸查看。老师把实际叙述与海盗及悲剧海难的传奇对比：冒险写作能使人激动，却常省略安全出行背后的日常准备。课堂学习区分享受故事与把戏剧动作当现实行为指南。","key":"Adventure writing could thrill a reader, but it often concealed the ordinary preparation behind safe travel. || but 对比故事效果与被省略的信息。","task":"精彩的故事不一定能作为现实行动的指南。 || An exciting story does not necessarily provide a guide to real action.","q":"How did the nearby vessel help? || It offered to tow the boat the final distance. tow 指拖曳。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["mast","propel","moor","tangle","cape","oar","pirate","windy","shipwreck","romance","tragic","thrill","tow"]},{"id":"77","title":"历史展品上的称号","en_title":"Titles, Memory, and Interpretation","kind":"阅读·历史文化","en":"The archive displayed an oath taken by a knight, a tribute to a martyr, and a portrait labelled “His Majesty.” Another panel described a patriot remembered for defending a town. The curator asked how a patriotic account could differ from a later historical interpretation.\nA document mentioned a plan to assassinate a ruler, followed by an execution and a public burial. Nearby stood a coffin from a theatrical reconstruction, clearly identified as a reproduction. These objects were intended to illustrate a narrative, not to prove every statement in it.\nThe final section examined royalty and public memory. A hero's likeness could appear on a coin, and an official decree could bestow a title. Yet neither honour made a person immortal or removed the need for inquiry. To salute a historical contribution is compatible with examining its limitations. Careful remembrance permits both appreciation and critical thought.","zh":"档案展示骑士誓言、烈士纪念文及标“陛下”的肖像，另一面板介绍守城而被纪念的爱国者。策展人问，爱国叙述与后来历史解释可能怎样不同。文献提到刺杀统治者的计划，以及随后的处决和公开安葬；附近剧场复原用棺木明确标注为复制品。物品用于说明叙事，不证明所有陈述。最后讨论王室与公共记忆：英雄肖像可上硬币，官方法令可授头衔，但荣誉不让人永生，也不能免于探究。致敬历史贡献与审视局限并不矛盾。认真纪念允许欣赏与批判思考共存。","key":"To salute a historical contribution is compatible with examining its limitations. || be compatible with + 动名词表示两种态度可并存。","task":"尊重历史人物并不意味着忽视他们的局限。 || Respecting historical figures does not mean ignoring their limitations.","q":"Why was the coffin labelled as a reproduction? || So visitors would not mistake a reconstruction for an original object. 说明证据性质。","note":"","wc":145,"new":["reproduction","salute","majesty","likeness","oath","execution","knight","martyr","royalty","coffin","tribute","decree","immortal","bestow","assassinate","burial","patriot","patriotic"]},{"id":"78","title":"一份拒信之后","en_title":"After a Rejection","kind":"写作·挫折与成长","en":"The rejection filled me with dismay. I had expected recognition and imagined a superb result. Instead, I felt blue, then sullen, and finally tempted to grumble that the whole process was absurd. An email from my tutor helped console me without offering false praise.\nShe suggested that I examine the feedback before deciding it was unfair. A grim mood could make every criticism seem dreadful. It could also tempt me to forsake the project or regard one misfortune as permanent doom. Neither response would help me improve.\nI took a day to rest, then returned to the draft. Some comments were hard to accept, but several revealed a genuine gap. The experience did not suddenly enchant me or produce rapture. It did, however, teach me to separate disappointment from judgment. Growth often begins with the willingness to remain engaged when the first outcome is unwelcome.","zh":"拒信使我沮丧。我期待认可与极佳结果，却先忧郁、再闷闷不乐，最后想抱怨整个流程荒谬。导师邮件安慰我，却没虚假夸奖。她建议先看反馈，再判是否不公。阴郁情绪会让批评都显可怕，也会诱使人放弃项目，把一次不幸当永久厄运，两者都无助改进。我休息一天再回稿件，有些意见难接受，但一些揭示真实缺口。经历没有突然令我欣喜若狂，却教会区分失望与判断。成长常始于首次结果不如意时，仍愿继续投入。","key":"It did, however, teach me to separate disappointment from judgment. || did + 动词原形表示强调；separate A from B 区分两者。","task":"失望不应该阻止我们认真考虑有价值的反馈。 || Disappointment should not prevent us from considering useful feedback carefully.","q":"What did the tutor suggest first? || Examine the feedback before judging the process unfair. 先证据后评价。","note":"","wc":145,"new":["superb","tempt","forsake","console","blue","gap","recognition","doom","enchant","grim","rapture","dreadful","dismay","misfortune","absurd","sullen","grumble","hard"]},{"id":"79","title":"初入职场的第一周","en_title":"An Induction Week","kind":"听力·职场学习","en":"During induction, the manager explained how our team would specialize in customer support. We should comply with the service procedure, but not conform blindly when an unusual case required judgment. A script was a starting point, not an excuse to ignore a person.\nI learnt to classify a complaint, ask for relevant input, and dispatch a request to the right department. A colleague taught me shorthand for private notes, although a formal record needed full wording. We would alternate between calls and written work to maintain attention.\nThe manager encouraged initiative while setting a clear threshold for escalation. If a problem exceeded our authority, we should seek help rather than improvise a promise. A thorough handover could minimize repetition and improve the overall experience. The week showed me that professionalism combines consistent methods with the sensitivity to recognize when a case is different.","zh":"入职培训时，经理解释团队专做客服：应遵守流程，但特殊案例需要判断时不能盲从。脚本是起点，不是忽视人的借口。我学习分类投诉、询问相关信息、把请求转至正确部门。同事教私人笔记速记，正式记录则需完整措辞。我们轮换电话与书面工作来保持注意。经理鼓励主动性，也明确何时升级处理：问题超权限应求助，不随意承诺。完整交接能减少重复、改善整体体验。专业能力结合一致方法与识别特殊情况的敏感度。","key":"A script was a starting point, not an excuse to ignore a person. || 两个名词短语界定工具的作用和边界。","task":"遇到超出权限的问题时，员工应该及时寻求帮助。 || Employees should seek help promptly when a problem exceeds their authority.","q":"When should staff seek help? || When the issue exceeds their authority. 权限是判断标准。","note":"","wc":143,"new":["overall","comply","shorthand","input","conform","specialize","alternate","minimize","consistent","dispatch","threshold","thorough","initiative"]},{"id":"80","title":"一个社区项目的启动","en_title":"Starting a Shared Project","kind":"写作·公益与执行","en":"Our neighbourhood decided to dedicate an unused room to adult learning. Volunteers would furnish it, establish a small lending shelf, and recruit people willing to impart practical skills. A retired teacher offered to teach adults who had previously remained illiterate.\nThe project needed more than idealism. We had to secure a grant, nominate a coordinator, and agree on a timetable. The first meeting would commence once the room was ready, while the completion of minor repairs could follow. A local business offered to endow a small fund for materials.\nSome residents doubted the idea, but the organizers did not promise a miracle. They proposed a modest trial and invited suggestions. The resulting cooperation could enrich community life and give overlooked abilities recognition. A shared vision becomes credible when people translate it into specific responsibilities and are willing to review what actually happens.","zh":"社区决定把闲屋用于成人学习，志愿者布置家具、设借阅书架、招募愿传授实用技能的人。退休教师愿教此前不识字的成人。项目不能只靠理想主义，还需资助、协调人和时间表。房间准备好即可开首次会议，小修随后完成。当地企业愿捐设材料基金。有人怀疑，组织者没许诺奇迹，而提出小规模试行并征求建议。合作能丰富社区生活，让被忽视的能力获得认可。把共同愿景落实为具体职责，并愿评估真实结果，愿景才可信。","key":"A shared vision becomes credible when people translate it into specific responsibilities. || translate ... into ... 也可表示将想法落实为行动。","task":"共同愿景需要明确分工才能变成现实。 || A shared vision needs clear responsibilities if it is to become reality.","q":"What made the project more than idealism? || Funding, coordination, a timetable, and a modest trial. 实际执行要素。","note":"","wc":142,"new":["endow","illiterate","idealism","completion","nominate","grant","vision","enrich","commence","impart","dedicate"]},{"id":"81","title":"社会调查中的解释边界","en_title":"Explaining Social Change","kind":"阅读·社会科学","en":"In sociology, a dynamic account must do more than label one practice a norm and another a peculiarity. Our class studied a district where unemployment was prevalent. The predominant explanation blamed idleness, but interviews revealed inadequate transport. We had to contend with several interpretations. One finding seemed to contradict another, partly because of selection. An intermediate category helped distinguish temporary difficulty from persistent exclusion. A pattern was indicative of a problem, not proof of its origin. The teacher asked us to orient the analysis towards evidence and incorporate competing explanations. Normalization of a harmful condition can conceal its causes. Research should illuminate those causes without treating every case as equivalent.","zh":"社会学中的动态解释不能只把一种做法叫常态、另一种叫怪异。班级研究失业普遍的地区。主流解释责怪懒惰，访谈却显示交通不足。不同发现似乎冲突，部分源于样本选择；中间类别帮助区分暂时困难与持续排斥。规律提示问题，却不证明起因。老师要求以证据为导向，纳入其他解释。有害条件常态化会掩盖原因，研究应揭示成因，又不把所有案例等同。","key":"A pattern was indicative of a problem, not proof of its origin. || be indicative of 表示提示，区分迹象与证明。","task":"社会问题不能仅归因于个人选择。 || Social problems cannot be attributed solely to individual choices.","q":"Why did the findings partly differ? || The selection of cases differed. 样本选择影响结论。","note":"","wc":110,"new":["intermediate","indicative","normalization","predominant","peculiarity","unemployment","sociology","prevalent","idleness","contend","selection","incorporate","dynamic","contradict","orient","equivalent","inadequate","norm"]},{"id":"82","title":"改革为什么需要试行","en_title":"Testing a Reform","kind":"写作·公共政策","en":"The college wanted to enhance teaching and diminish paperwork. A radical proposal promised a decisive improvement, but critics feared instability and the consequent confusion. Its inherent drawback was the time required for training. The committee chose to subdivide the project and test one stage experimentally. This would not constitute a perfect comparison, but it could reveal a complication early. A clear procedure would precede each change. Staff would consolidate initial gains and offset extra work with additional support. The question was whether the reform could operate economically. A resolute commitment to improvement can coexist with a willingness to reverse a decision when its effects prove undesirable.","zh":"学校想改善教学、减少文书。激进方案承诺决定性提升，批评者担心不稳定与随之混乱，其固有弊端是培训耗时。委员会决定分阶段试行，虽非完美对比，却能早发现麻烦。每次改变前明确程序，巩固初步成果，以支持抵消额外工作，并考察是否经济高效。坚定改进与不良结果出现时撤回决定并不矛盾。","key":"A resolute commitment to improvement can coexist with a willingness to reverse a decision. || coexist with 表示两种态度可以并存。","task":"小规模试行能够揭示潜在问题。 || A small-scale trial can reveal potential problems.","q":"Why was the project divided into stages? || To reveal complications before wider implementation. 分阶段有助于检验。","note":"","wc":106,"new":["consequent","precede","drawback","enhance","experimentally","decisive","economically","diminish","resolute","radical","inherent","constitute","consolidate","complication","offset","instability","undesirable","reverse","subdivide"]},{"id":"83","title":"从灵感到设计","en_title":"Making an Idea Work","kind":"写作·创新","en":"A student tried to conceive a device to help users with limited hand movement unlock a door. Her inspiration came from a relative's struggle with a stiff handle. The aim was to reduce a practical handicap. A versatile design needed careful testing. A loosely connected part could stall, and a sharp edge could prick a finger. Latent problems forced her to restrain her enthusiasm. The team would exert a small force and compare responses systematically. The prototype did not surpass every existing product. Nevertheless, it revealed a neglected need. The essence of useful design lies in testing ideas against reality; a modest invention can exemplify this principle.","zh":"学生构想帮助行动受限者开门的装置，灵感来自亲属转不动僵硬把手，目标是减少实际障碍。通用设计需测试：连接松会卡住，锐边会扎手。潜在问题让她暂缓热情，团队施加小力并系统比较。原型没超过一切产品，却揭示被忽略的需要。有用设计本质在于让想法接受现实检验，小发明也能体现原则。","key":"The essence of useful design lies in testing ideas against reality. || lie in + 动名词，指出关键所在。","task":"实用创新应该回应真实需求。 || Practical innovation should respond to real needs.","q":"What inspired the device? || A relative's difficulty with a stiff handle. 具体问题激发创新。","note":"","wc":107,"new":["restrain","systematically","loosely","stiff","conceive","inspiration","unlock","exemplify","stall","handicap","exert","versatile","latent","prick","surpass","essence"]},{"id":"84","title":"接替前任的管理者","en_title":"Taking Over a Team","kind":"听力·职场","en":"My predecessor left a detailed handover. A successor, he warned, should sift useful routines from wasteful ones. The forthcoming project required us to marshal resources, lengthen testing, and terminate an outdated arrangement. I asked colleagues to affirm what worked. A senior employee was insistent that nothing change, but we examined evidence. I learnt to shoulder responsibility without claiming exclusive wisdom. A mature manager should engage with criticism rather than expect obedient agreement. Leadership involves succession as well as personal performance. A clear handover helps the next person understand a decision and revise it thoughtfully when conditions diverge from earlier expectations.","zh":"前任留下详细交接，提醒继任者筛选有用与浪费的惯例。新项目需统筹资源、延长测试并终止旧安排。我请同事肯定有效部分，老员工坚持不变，但大家检验证据。我学着承担责任而不自称独有智慧。成熟管理者应回应批评，不只期待服从。领导涉及传承，交接帮助后来者理解决定并在条件偏离预期时修订。","key":"A mature manager should engage with criticism rather than expect obedient agreement. || rather than 连接动词短语，表达管理原则。","task":"承担责任不意味着必须独自决定一切。 || Taking responsibility does not mean deciding everything alone.","q":"What did the handover help explain? || The reasoning behind decisions. 交接不仅是任务清单。","note":"","wc":100,"new":["marshal","lengthen","mature","engage","sift","predecessor","expect","wasteful","insistent","succession","successor","forthcoming","obedient","diverge","affirm","exclusive","shoulder","wisdom","terminate"]},{"id":"85","title":"市集上的下午","en_title":"At the Bazaar","kind":"听力·生活","en":"The bazaar was situated near houses that adjoin the square. A pedlar displayed an array of objects, including a ruby imitation and an ivory-coloured plastic comb. A waitress carried tea past a mint-sweet stall. People stopped to mingle. A plump child with curly hair tried to clasp a balloon while a stout man retrieved a coin. Nearby, a woman applied lipstick using a mirror. Someone in a jean jacket played a tune. Conversation and music seemed to overlap without creating a disturbance. The market offered amusement, but its agreeable atmosphere also depended on clear paths and cleanliness. Public comfort often rests on small, almost invisible arrangements.","zh":"市集在与广场相接的房屋旁，小贩摆出仿红宝石和象牙色塑料梳等物件。女服务员端茶经过薄荷糖摊，人们停留交流。卷发胖孩子抱气球，壮实男人捡硬币，女人照镜涂口红，穿牛仔布夹克者奏曲。声音交叠却不扰人。市集有娱乐，宜人气氛也依靠道路畅通与清洁。公共舒适往往来自细小安排。","key":"Public comfort often rests on small, almost invisible arrangements. || rest on 表示依赖，用于解释服务质量。","task":"良好服务能够增强一个地方的吸引力。 || Good services can enhance a place's appeal.","q":"What supported the pleasant atmosphere? || Clear paths and cleanliness as well as entertainment. 条件不只有娱乐。","note":"jean 在 jean jacket 中作定语指牛仔布；denim jacket 也是常用表达。","wc":106,"new":["array","mint","overlap","amusement","jean","ivory","situated","adjoin","mingle","cleanliness","agreeable","waitress","clasp","curly","bazaar","ruby","plump","disturbance","lipstick","stout","pedlar"]},{"id":"86","title":"旅店的一夜","en_title":"A Night at the Inn","kind":"听力·住宿","en":"The inn stood in the vicinity of a villa. A fireplace warmed the entrance, and a kettle rested by the hearth. The host gave me a flannel blanket and showed me how to close the shutter without making it rattle. A repaired fixture held the lamp. Tired but awake, I could overhear a murmur and an occasional snore. Outside, a luminous sign seemed to float in darkness. I chose not to fret. I folded my pants, left my coat to dry, and read until the day's agitation subsided. A shower began. By morning, ventilation had helped freshen the stuffy room. Comfort depended on details, not a grand description.","zh":"旅店在别墅附近，壁炉温暖门厅，炉边有水壶。主人给绒布毯，演示安静关窗，修好的固定件支撑灯。我累却清醒，听见低语与偶尔鼾声。夜中发光招牌仿佛漂浮。我不再焦虑，折裤、晾外套、阅读到烦躁平息。阵雨开始，次晨通风使闷房清新。舒适来自细节，不是夸大描述。","key":"Comfort depended on details, not a grand description. || 简洁对照强调评价应基于实际体验。","task":"住宿质量也取决于细节。 || The quality of accommodation also depends on attention to detail.","q":"What helped freshen the room? || Ventilation. 辨认具体改善措施。","note":"","wc":108,"new":["shower","freshen","awake","float","overhear","vicinity","pants","fixture","agitation","flannel","luminous","rattle","murmur","snore","stuffy","villa","hearth","fireplace","shutter","fret"]},{"id":"87","title":"一场安全演练","en_title":"A Safety Drill","kind":"听力·公共安全","en":"A siren sounded during the drill. The scenario involved a blaze near storage, where trained staff would assess the flame. We were not asked to improvise a way to extinguish it. Pictures explained how a spark could ignite material or scorch a surface. A lighter, a cigar butt, and a faulty fuse appeared in separate examples. A firework belonged in another discussion, not in the room. The purpose was prevention. We kept the perimeter clear and followed an escort. Nobody should linger for belongings or create an uproar. Afterwards, we recalled the sequence. Preparedness means knowing what to do first and which actions require trained personnel.","zh":"演练警报响起，情境是储物处失火，由受训者评估火焰，不要求游客临时自创灭火法。图片解释火花点燃材料、热灼伤表面，案例分别涉及打火机、雪茄烟头与坏保险丝。烟花另讨论，不放现场。重点是预防：外围畅通，跟随引导，不留恋财物、不喧哗。结束后回忆顺序，准备意味着知道先做什么和哪些行动需受训人员。","key":"Preparedness means knowing what to do first. || what to do 作 knowing 的宾语，简洁说明准备的内容。","task":"明确行动顺序能够减少混乱。 || A clear sequence of actions can reduce confusion.","q":"Who handled specialized actions? || Trained personnel. 分工是关键。","note":"","wc":106,"new":["perimeter","prevention","ignite","cigar","extinguish","blaze","scorch","uproar","siren","flame","linger","butt","lighter","firework","fuse","escort"]},{"id":"88","title":"病区志愿者的职责","en_title":"A Volunteer in the Ward","kind":"听力·服务","en":"In the ward, I helped visitors find seats. A nurse asked me to fetch a blanket, not to inject medicine or assess an injured limb. One patient wore a bandage over a scar. I could offer directions and company, not medical judgment. The coordinator said that a small errand could be vital to a busy team. I should not hover over patients or spread an unconfirmed outbreak story. If someone began to sneeze, I would follow the facility's instructions. A pregnant visitor thanked me, as did a parent holding a baby. Reliable service required understanding my role and knowing when to seek help.","zh":"病区里，我帮访客找座位。护士让我拿毯，不是注射或评估伤肢。有患者疤上缠绷带，我能指路陪伴，不能医疗判断。协调员说小跑腿对忙碌团队也重要，不应围着患者或传未核实疫情故事。有人打喷嚏就遵设施指引。孕妇与抱婴儿家长感谢我。可靠服务需要理解职责并知道何时求助。","key":"Reliable service required understanding my role and knowing when to seek help. || 并列动名词说明可靠服务的两个条件。","task":"清楚职责范围有助于提供可靠服务。 || Understanding the scope of one's role helps make service reliable.","q":"What could the volunteer offer? || Directions and company. 不能越权作医疗判断。","note":"","wc":103,"new":["inject","baby","vital","hover","pregnant","limb","sneeze","errand","ward","bandage","scar","outbreak"]},{"id":"89","title":"阅读困难的历史材料","en_title":"Reading Difficult Archives","kind":"阅读·历史","en":"An archive described a slave forced to work under a ruthless overseer. Its purpose was to document injustice, not excuse it. Some experiences remained behind a veil of official language. Another document discussed an opium trade dispute; a third recorded a torpedo attack. These subjects required context beyond a single paragraph. We compared sources rather than let one vivid account become the whole story. The class also examined language that could degrade a person. A respectable title did not make a corrupt official merciful, and a label such as coward could conceal complexity. Learning difficult vocabulary should sharpen judgment rather than normalize the harm it describes.","zh":"档案描述奴隶在残酷监工下被迫劳动，目的记录不公，不是开脱。有些经历被官方语言遮蔽。另文涉及鸦片贸易争端，还有鱼雷袭击，都需要超过一段文字的语境。我们比较来源，不让生动记载替代全部历史，也审视贬低人的措辞。体面头衔不使腐败官员仁慈，“懦夫”等标签可能掩盖复杂性。难词应提高判断，而非让人把伤害当常态。","key":"A respectable title did not make a corrupt official merciful. || make + 宾语 + 形容词，区分名号与实质。","task":"理解历史需要比较不同来源。 || Understanding history requires comparing different sources.","q":"Why were several sources compared? || One account could not explain the whole history. 单一来源有限。","note":"","wc":106,"new":["slave","torpedo","veil","opium","ruthless","degrade","merciful","coward","respectable","corrupt"]},{"id":"90","title":"展厅里的运动模型","en_title":"Motion on Display","kind":"阅读·工程","en":"A model arm could deflect an object, and a scale measured the deflection. Another display asked us to turn a handle clockwise and watch a wheel reverse direction. We compared velocity with speed. Nearby, a channel made two streams converge or diverge. A metal mesh caught particles, while a cubic container collected liquid. The guide asked us to observe rather than assume equilibrium. A machine might appear stable while material remained in constant flux. The guide described this as a dynamical system. One apparatus could eject a token after each cycle; another showed how friction might retard motion. A useful explanation connects what learners see with the conditions that produce it.","zh":"模型臂让物体偏转，刻度量偏转程度。另一展项让人顺时针转把手，看轮子反向，比较速度矢量与速率。通道使两股流汇合或分开，金属网截颗粒，立方容器收液。导游要求观察，不假定平衡。机器看似稳，物质仍流变，导游将其称为动力系统。一装置每周期弹代币，另一演示摩擦减缓运动。有用解释把所见与产生条件联系起来。","key":"A machine might appear stable while material remained in constant flux. || while 对照外表与内部状态。","task":"解释应该把现象与产生条件联系起来。 || An explanation should connect a phenomenon with the conditions that produce it.","q":"Why was direction discussed? || Direction is part of velocity, unlike speed. 区分近义术语。","note":"retard 在此是减缓的动词，不可据此当作称呼人的词。dynamic / dynamical 均保留；普通作文用 dynamic 的场景更多。","wc":111,"new":["eject","retard","velocity","mesh","equilibrium","deflection","flux","cubic","deflect","clockwise"]},{"id":"91","title":"排练室中的声音与动作","en_title":"Rehearsing a Scene","kind":"听力·舞台与动作","en":"Our energetic group prepared a circus scene for a school play. A performer would march in a parade, blow a shrill whistle, and shout \"Hurrah!\" Another would flap a cloth wing and pretend to fly. The comic hero had to hop over a box, squat behind it, then stride into view. Nobody needed a dangerous stunt.\nThe director asked us to vary the sound. A character might whisper, hiss, grunt, or give a sudden exclamation. A metallic bell would jingle; a drumbeat would follow a quick rap on the door. We practised when to clap, how to reel in surprise, and where to pause.\nThe scene ended with a hymn followed by a hush. Its effect depended on contrast and timing. Even a fantastic story requires disciplined preparation. A good performance can emerge when many small actions become a harmonious whole.","zh":"活力十足的剧团排马戏场景：演员游行、吹尖哨、喊好耶，另一人扑布翅假装飞。喜剧英雄跳过箱子、蹲下再大步入场，不做危险特技。导演要求变化声音：低语、嘶声、咕哝或突然感叹，金属铃叮当，敲门后接鼓点。大家练习鼓掌时机、惊讶踉跄和停顿。结尾是圣歌与寂静，效果依赖对比和节奏。幻想故事也需严谨准备，小动作协调成整体才能形成好表演。","key":"A good performance can emerge when many small actions become a harmonious whole. || emerge 表示形成；when 从句说明形成条件。","task":"团队成果依赖每个人对细节的关注。 || A team's success depends on each member's attention to detail.","q":"What made the final scene effective? || Contrast and timing. 不是危险特技。","note":"","wc":141,"new":["grunt","hymn","hop","hiss","rap","circus","parade","fantastic","reel","metallic","shrill","energetic","exclamation","harmonious","hurrah","emerge","fly","whisper","stride","hush","squat","jingle","flap"]},{"id":"92","title":"自然观察中的误判","en_title":"Looking without Labels","kind":"阅读·自然观察","en":"At dawn, a cock called near the fence. A tiny insect gave a child a sting, and he declared every bug vicious. The guide asked him to reconsider. An unfamiliar animal was not necessarily a hazard; a shark on a poster was neither a cartoon villain nor a creature to tease.\nWe watched birds pluck food, observed a plant repel an insect, and noticed how a leaf could taper towards its tip. The guide invited us to roam only within the marked area. We should not clutch a creature, disturb it for a photograph, or let curiosity become thoughtless intrusion.\nA nickname such as \"monster\" could obscure an animal's actual behaviour. So could the urge to adore everything that looked soft. Observation requires patience with what we do not yet understand. Respect for nature is more reliable when it rests on attention rather than fear or sentiment alone.","zh":"黎明公鸡叫，昆虫蜇了孩子，他便说所有虫都恶毒。导游让他重想：陌生动物未必有害，海报中的鲨鱼既非卡通反派，也不该逗弄。我们看鸟啄取食物、植物驱虫、叶片尖端渐细，只在标记范围走动，不抓生物或为拍照打扰。叫动物“怪物”可能掩盖真实行为，喜欢一切软萌东西也会误判。观察需耐心面对未知，对自然的尊重建立在留心之上比只靠恐惧或感情可靠。","key":"An unfamiliar animal was not necessarily a hazard. || not necessarily 表示未必，避免绝对化判断。","task":"观察应该帮助我们修正最初的印象。 || Observation should help us revise our initial impressions.","q":"Why did the guide challenge the child's statement? || One sting did not justify a judgment about every insect. 避免以偏概全。","note":"","wc":148,"new":["clutch","roam","cock","vicious","taper","hazard","shark","cartoon","sting","repel","pluck","sentiment","tease","adore","bug","nickname"]},{"id":"93","title":"冒险故事如何制造紧张","en_title":"Suspense and Action","kind":"阅读·叙事语言","en":"In a fictional adventure, a fighter tried to cross an icy pass before an enemy could seize the bridge. Ice made each step uncertain. The story did not ask readers to imitate him: its aim was to create fright. A gigantic gate guarded a vault, and a skeleton lay beneath a faded flag.\nThe hero would grope through darkness, heave a heavy door, and wield a broken pole to keep an attacker away. His companion wanted to punch and thrash their opponent, but the hero chose to subdue the conflict without further violence. A trap threatened to expel them into the snow.\nThe climax brought an unexpected ally. A fearsome appearance had concealed kindness. Readers felt astonishment because their assumptions had been overturned. Suspense can terrify or excite through selective information. To understand the story, we must examine what the narrator reveals, what remains a mystery, and when that information changes.","zh":"虚构冒险中，战士试图在敌人夺桥前穿过冰冷山口。冰使步步危险，故事意在制造恐惧，不供模仿。巨门守宝库，褪旗下躺骨架。英雄摸黑推重门、挥断杆阻攻击；同伴想拳打痛揍敌手，英雄选择缓和冲突，陷阱险把他们弹入雪中。高潮出现意外盟友，可怕外表藏善意，读者因预设被推翻而惊讶。悬念通过信息选择使人害怕或兴奋，阅读需看叙述者何时揭示什么。","key":"Readers felt astonishment because their assumptions had been overturned. || 过去完成时被动表示先前假设已被推翻。","task":"叙述者可以通过控制信息来制造悬念。 || A narrator can create suspense by controlling information.","q":"Why was the ally surprising? || A fearsome appearance had led readers to expect hostility. 外表与实际反差。","note":"动作来自虚构故事，学习重点是叙事、推断和动作动词。全文其他故事与研究项目也为教学情境。","wc":151,"new":["thrash","subdue","terrify","ice","mystery","expel","gigantic","fright","astonishment","wield","skeleton","vault","fighter","punch","icy","heave","grope"]},{"id":"94","title":"改变偏见的相处","en_title":"Beyond First Impressions","kind":"写作·人际与包容","en":"I had dismissed my new neighbour as snobbish because he rarely spoke. He was bald, wore formal clothes, and looked decidedly uneasy at our first gathering. I foolishly treated those details as evidence of his personality. That judgment now seems shameful.\nWhen a storm damaged the street, he worked tirelessly to help. He did not preach about generosity or deliver a sermon on duty. He simply offered time and tools. I felt shame at my earlier assumption and tried to make amends.\nThe experience taught me not to resent someone for failing to fit my expectations. A tolerant community must make room for different manners, including silence. A person may be reserved without being rude, just as a lively manner need not indicate goodness. We ought to replace petty labels with patient attention. The requisite first step is often to admit that our impression may be wrong.","zh":"邻居少言，我就判他势利。他秃顶、衣着正式，初聚明显不自在，我愚蠢地当作性格证据，如今想来羞愧。风暴损街时，他不辞辛苦帮忙，不宣扬慷慨或说教责任，只贡献时间工具。我为旧判断羞愧并弥补。不要因别人不符期待而怨他。包容社区容纳不同举止，也包括沉默。内敛未必无礼，活泼也未必善良。应用耐心观察替代琐碎标签，第一步常是承认印象可能错。","key":"A person may be reserved without being rude. || without + 动名词区分常被误认为相伴的两种特征。","task":"我们不应该仅凭外表判断一个人的品格。 || We should not judge a person's character solely by appearance.","q":"What changed the narrator's view? || The neighbour's practical help after a storm. 实际行为修正判断。","note":"","wc":147,"new":["requisite","petty","bald","preach","snobbish","shame","goodness","tolerant","decidedly","shameful","resent","sermon","uneasy","ought"]},{"id":"95","title":"好的结论有多大范围","en_title":"The Scope of a Conclusion","kind":"阅读·研究与表达","en":"Our research team examined a global trend over a ten-year span. An apparent similarity between two regions was notable, but the differences were equally important. We divided the data into a segment for each period and checked whether simultaneous changes had a shared explanation.\nA figure of nought did not necessarily prove absence; it might reflect the way a variable was recorded. Nor did a dramatic peak justify an indefinite forecast. The teacher asked us to qualify each inference and identify whether a result was statistically useful or merely interesting.\nWe could deem the findings suggestive without presenting them as final. The overall range remained broad, and a peripheral factor might still matter. Research should bring uncertainty to the fore rather than hide it. To pore over evidence is worthwhile when it makes a conclusion more precise. Its value lies not in sounding formidable but in saying exactly what the data can support.","zh":"团队研究十年全球趋势，两地区表面相似值得注意，差异同样重要。按时期分段数据，检查同步变化是否共同原因。零值未必证明不存在，也可能来自记录方式；明显峰值不能证明无限期预测。老师要求给推断加适用限制，区分统计价值与仅有趣。结论可算提示性却非定论，范围仍广，边缘因素也可能重要。研究应呈现不确定性，仔细审证据是为了准确。价值不在听来深奥，而在准确说数据支持什么。","key":"Its value lies not in sounding formidable but in saying exactly what the data can support. || not in ... but in ... 形成平行动名词结构。","task":"一个结论的范围不应该超出证据所能支持的范围。 || A conclusion should not extend beyond what the evidence can support.","q":"Why might a recorded zero be ambiguous? || It could reflect how a variable was recorded rather than true absence. 数据需结合测量方式。","note":"","wc":153,"new":["peripheral","notable","fore","qualify","indefinite","nought","simultaneous","deem","global","segment","range","pore","similarity","formidable","peak","span"]},{"id":"96","title":"贸易增长与公共责任","en_title":"Trade and Responsibility","kind":"写作·经济发展","en":"A commonwealth of fictional coastal states sought to expand trade. Its members wanted to combat discrimination, reduce a monopoly's influence, and prevent development from damaging a virgin forest. The plan would elevate incomes only if benefits reached ordinary households.\nThe first proposal overlooked environmental degradation. Extraction of raw materials could deprive a community of clean water, and waste might infect an already polluted stream with harmful microbes. A destructive project could bring a short boom and a disastrous decline. Growth alone was not enough.\nThe states agreed to review each proceeding before approval and publish the terms thereof in accessible language. One group threatened a boycott if consultation was ignored. The debate showed that cooperation requires more than agreeing on an attractive goal. Trade can improve lives, but its design must account for who bears the costs and who receives the gains.","zh":"虚构沿海国家联合体想扩贸易、反歧视、减垄断影响，并防开发损原始森林。收益到普通家庭才提升收入。初案忽略环境退化：开采可能剥夺社区清水，废物可把有害微生物带入已污染溪流；破坏项目或先短繁荣后灾难衰退。各国同意批准前审查程序，以易懂语言公布相关条款；团体威胁若忽略咨询就抵制。合作不止同意漂亮目标，贸易制度要问谁承担成本、谁得到收益。","key":"Its design must account for who bears the costs and who receives the gains. || account for 后两个宾语从句，完整列出分配问题。","task":"经济增长应该兼顾当地居民与环境。 || Economic growth should take local residents and the environment into account.","q":"Why was growth alone insufficient? || It could create environmental harm and unequal costs. 增长与分配、环境并非同一指标。","note":"commonwealth 在此是虚构联合体的设定，不是对现实组织的报道。","wc":142,"new":["disastrous","elevate","thereof","infect","destructive","monopoly","degradation","commonwealth","combat","deprive","virgin","extraction","proceeding","discrimination","boycott"]},{"id":"97","title":"如何坚持一个长期项目","en_title":"Staying with a Project","kind":"写作·毅力与方法","en":"A long project can overwhelm even an industrious student. My first inclination was to work excessively and disregard rest. The result was not extraordinary productivity but stiffness, fatigue, and a wish to desert the task. I nearly let one difficult week destine the whole project for failure.\nMy tutor suggested a steadier rhythm. I should adhere to a realistic schedule, strive for a clear daily objective, and persist without treating every delay as disgrace. A setback could disillusion me, but it did not have to end the endeavor.\nWe revised the plan and allowed time to elapse between demanding sessions. Ideally, work would finish early; ordinarily, it would require adjustment. I learnt to waver less when a problem appeared and to ask for help before frustration became overwhelming. Determination is not a promise never to hesitate. It is the willingness to resume thoughtfully after difficulty.","zh":"长项目连勤奋学生也会不堪重负。我起初过度工作不休息，结果不是惊人效率，而是僵硬疲劳、想放弃，险让一周困难决定项目失败。导师建议稳定节奏：遵现实计划，每天有目标，坚持但不把延误当耻辱。挫折会打破幻想，却不必终止努力。我们修计划，在高强度时段间留间隔。理想上早完成，通常仍需调整。我少些动摇，在沮丧压倒自己前求助。决心不是从不犹豫，而是困难后审慎继续。","key":"Determination is not a promise never to hesitate. || 用简短句澄清毅力的含义，再接具体解释。","task":"坚持也需要根据实际情况调整计划。 || Persistence also requires adjusting a plan to actual circumstances.","q":"What was wrong with the initial approach? || Excessive work without sufficient rest caused fatigue rather than lasting productivity. 方法与结果不匹配。","note":"","wc":145,"new":["adhere","stiffness","desert","waver","ordinarily","disgrace","inclination","industrious","strive","destine","ideally","disillusion","hesitate","excessively","persist","elapse","endeavor"]},{"id":"98","title":"礼貌拒绝与坚定边界","en_title":"Saying No Clearly","kind":"听力·人际沟通","en":"A classmate was obstinate about borrowing my equipment. He would entreat, implore, and finally plead that I make an exception. I wanted to oblige him, but the device belonged to a team and could not leave the laboratory without authorization.\nI explained the limitation without calling him selfish. He tried to defy the rule, insisting that a small exception was a trifle. I replied that the issue was shared responsibility. A device that went missing would cause more than a troublesome afternoon.\nThe discussion was tense, yet I did not need to slap the table or summon others to shame him. I could remain calm and suggest an approved alternative. A clear boundary need not be hostile. Respectful refusal can protect cooperation when a hasty favour would place other people's work at risk.","zh":"同学执意借设备，先恳求、再央求，最后请求破例。我想帮，但设备属团队，未经授权不能出实验室。我解释限制不骂自私。他想违规则，称小例外不值一提，我说问题是共同责任，丢设备可不止麻烦一下午。讨论紧张，但不用拍桌或叫别人羞辱他，我能平静提获准替代。边界不一定敌对，仓促帮忙会让他人工作冒险时，尊重的拒绝反能保护合作。","key":"A clear boundary need not be hostile. || need not 表示不必，并非 must not 的禁止。","task":"礼貌拒绝不等于不愿合作。 || A polite refusal does not imply an unwillingness to cooperate.","q":"Why could the device not be lent immediately? || It was shared equipment requiring authorization to leave the lab. 责任归属决定边界。","note":"","wc":133,"new":["summon","defy","plead","trifle","oblige","implore","troublesome","slap","obstinate","entreat"]},{"id":"99","title":"旧广告与现代读者","en_title":"Reading an Old Advertisement","kind":"阅读·语言变化","en":"A periodical from an earlier epoch advertised a classic household product. It promised everlasting softness and a solution to every cleaning problem. One page displayed a primitive tool; another claimed a modern process would make every stain disappear. The teacher asked us to distinguish persuasive language from reliable evidence.\nWe examined the word \"smart\" and compared its meanings in several contexts. A fashionable appearance and a useful technological feature were not identical. Nor did a noted inventor's endorsement guarantee a product's success. The advertisement's simplicity concealed unanswered questions.\nThe exercise was an apt introduction to critical reading. A claim may be memorable without being sound. Before deciding to subscribe to a service or buy a product, a reader should examine its specific promise, the evidence offered, and the conditions under which that promise could hold.","zh":"旧时代期刊宣传经典家用品，承诺永恒柔软、解决一切清洁问题。一页展示简陋工具，另一页称现代工艺让所有污渍消失。老师要求区分劝服语言与可靠证据。大家比较 smart 在不同语境的意义：时髦外表与有用科技功能不同，知名发明者背书也不保证成功。广告简洁却隐藏未答问题。这是批判阅读的恰当引入：主张好记未必可靠。订服务或买商品前，应看具体承诺、证据与适用条件。","key":"A claim may be memorable without being sound. || may 与 without 共同表示两种性质不必相伴。","task":"广告的吸引力不能代替产品性能的证据。 || An advertisement's appeal cannot replace evidence of a product's performance.","q":"What did the advertisement's simplicity conceal? || Unanswered questions about evidence and conditions. 简洁不代表完整。","note":"","wc":135,"new":["noted","primitive","everlasting","softness","apt","periodical","classic","subscribe","simplicity","smart","epoch"]},{"id":"100","title":"一座城市的旧照片","en_title":"A City in Photographs","kind":"翻译·城市与记忆","en":"The exhibition placed an old photograph beside a recent one. A mighty bridge now crossed the river, and new buildings seemed to spring from every vacant plot. Yet the curator did not herald every change as progress. The disappearance of a familiar lane could bring both convenience and loss.\nIn the older image, a woman stood beside a cradle while a worker pulled a cart. A narrow path led to a small house. In the newer one, a broad road occupied the same spatial position. The contrast brought changes in everyday life into focus.\nVisitors were invited to meditate on what the city should preserve. Nostalgia alone could not answer that question, but neither could an account concerned only with growth. A city is more than a collection of structures. Its evolution also involves memory, relationships, and the ways people learn to share space.","zh":"展览并列旧照新照。大桥跨河，新楼从空地涌起，策展人却没把每个变化都称进步：熟悉小巷消失可能兼有便利与失落。旧照女人站摇篮旁、工人拉车，窄道通小屋，新照同位置是宽路，对比凸显生活变化。游客被邀思考城市该保留什么，怀旧不能独自回答，但只谈增长也不够。城市不只是建筑集合，演变还涉及记忆、关系与共享空间方式。","key":"A city is more than a collection of structures. || more than 表示不只是，可引出社会与文化维度。","task":"城市的发展也应关注居民的记忆与关系。 || Urban development should also consider residents' memories and relationships.","q":"Did the curator describe every change as progress? || No. Some changes brought loss as well as convenience. 评价有两面。","note":"","wc":144,"new":["cradle","disappearance","mighty","spatial","evolution","herald","meditate"]},{"id":"101","title":"演员怎样表达情绪","en_title":"Acting without Exaggeration","kind":"听力·动作与情绪","en":"During her maiden performance, an actress had to play a frightened traveller. Her first attempt was extraordinarily loud. She would pant, stagger, and quiver, then cry, \"Alas, what awful news!\" The director asked her to reconsider. A frightened person might become mute or speak in a hoarse whisper; fear did not always require a violent outburst.\nThe next scene involved a wretched character unable to escape a memory. His torment interrupted his slumber, and he spoke of endless woe. The actor wanted to smash a prop and shatter a glass. The director substituted safe sound effects and asked him to express the conflict through posture.\nHitherto, the group had treated strong emotion as a reason to shout. Now they learnt that stillness could be equally powerful. Their muse was ordinary observation. The scene became more convincing when the actors stopped trying to display every possible feeling at once. Less movement did not mean less meaning.","zh":"首次演出中，女演员扮受惊旅人。她起初格外响亮：喘气、踉跄、发抖，再喊“唉，多可怕的消息！”导演让重想：受惊者也可能沉默或嘶哑低语，并非总猛烈爆发。下一角色被记忆折磨，睡眠受扰，倾诉无尽悲哀。演员想砸道具与玻璃，导演换安全音效，请他用姿势表达冲突。此前大家把强情绪当大喊理由，如今学会静止也有力量。灵感来自日常观察，不同时展示一切情绪反使场景可信。动作少不等于意义少。","key":"Less movement did not mean less meaning. || 平行比较形式表达数量与效果不能简单等同。","task":"强烈的情绪也可以通过安静的方式表达。 || Strong emotions can also be expressed quietly.","q":"What changed the actors' approach? || They learnt that stillness could convey emotion as powerfully as shouting. 表达手段不只有音量。","note":"maiden 表示首次的，修饰 performance；muse 表示灵感来源。","wc":155,"new":["awful","torment","slumber","maiden","mute","pant","hitherto","stagger","violent","shatter","extraordinarily","smash","muse","wretched","woe","alas","hoarse","quiver"]},{"id":"102","title":"维修日的准备与收尾","en_title":"Preparing for a Repair Day","kind":"听力·劳动与维护","en":"Before volunteers arrived, staff would erect a sign and inspect a damaged bench. A bump on its surface could catch a sleeve. An old hook needed replacing, and the printer required a new cartridge. The caretaker asked us to leave a lifting jack to trained workers and report any mechanical jam.\nWe cleaned dirt without treating every surface alike. A label warned that bleach could damage one material. Another object showed decay, not merely filth. We learnt to wipe a spill, wring a cloth, and flush a dirty channel only as instructed. Nobody should grind a sharp edge without the right training.\nOutside, a contractor examined old tar on the path. The remainder of the team sorted reusable materials. Maintenance involved knowing what to do, what to inspect, and when to seek expertise. The lesson was practical: preserving useful things requires attention both before work begins and after the tools are put away.","zh":"志愿者到前，员工立告示、查破凳。凸起可能勾袖，旧钩需换，打印机需新墨盒。管理员要求千斤顶交受训者，机械卡住就报告。清洁要区别表面：漂白剂会损某材料，另一物件是腐朽不只是脏。大家按指引擦溢出物、拧布、冲脏槽，不擅磨锐边。外面承包人查路上旧沥青，其余人分类可复用材料。维护需知道做什么、查什么、何时求专业帮助，开工前和收工具后都要用心。","key":"Maintenance involved knowing what to do, what to inspect, and when to seek expertise. || 三个疑问词加不定式并列，组织行动步骤。","task":"维护工作需要适当的知识和准备。 || Maintenance requires appropriate knowledge and preparation.","q":"Was every dirty-looking surface treated in the same way? || No. Some materials could be damaged, and some objects showed decay. 区分材质与损坏类型。","note":"","wc":153,"new":["bump","grind","hook","flush","filth","erect","decay","remainder","jack","bleach","wring","jam","cartridge","tar"]},{"id":"103","title":"运动会上的小插曲","en_title":"An Incident at Sports Day","kind":"听力·校园活动","en":"Our class was bound for the field when two pupils almost collided at a doorway. The teacher explained that people can collide even without moving quickly if everyone tries to pass at once. He asked us to form a row, keep an elbow away from others, and watch the slippery slide.\nA mischievous child tried to wink at his friend during the instructions. His playful wink was not itself a problem, but he was about to stray onto a wet area. The teacher chose to intervene calmly. Mischief did not require a dramatic punishment; safety did require attention.\nLater, we watched a horse trot in a supervised demonstration. A cold wind brought a chill, so the group moved indoors to quench its thirst. Nobody made a fuss about the change. The event was memorable because staff combined clear boundaries with kindness. They did not confuse an energetic child with a troublesome one.","zh":"去操场时两孩子险在门口相撞。老师解释，一拥而过即使不快也会碰撞，要求排队、肘别碰人、小心滑梯。淘气孩子向朋友眨眼，眨眼本身无妨，但他快误入湿地。老师平静介入：调皮不需大惩罚，安全却需注意。后来大家看受监督的马小跑演示。冷风带寒意，群体进屋解渴，没人为变化大惊小怪。活动难忘因工作人员把明确界限与善意结合，没把活泼等同麻烦。","key":"They did not confuse an energetic child with a troublesome one. || confuse A with B 表示把两者混淆。","task":"清楚的规则可以与友善的态度并存。 || Clear rules can coexist with a kind attitude.","q":"Why did the group move indoors? || A cold wind brought a chill. 天气变化引出地点调整。","note":"","wc":152,"new":["wink","elbow","bound","wind","quench","mischief","collide","stray","fuss","slide","intervene","chill","row","trot"]},{"id":"104","title":"信息传播与判断","en_title":"How a Claim Travels","kind":"阅读·研究与媒介","en":"The circulation of a striking story can outpace its verification. In our project, we examined the propagation of a claim across a cluster of accounts. Its incidence increased sharply after one popular post, but popularity did not establish truth. We had to examine the representation of events and the possibility of fabrication.\nThe analysis was subject to clear limits. A missing record could make a conclusion invalid, while an apparently uniform pattern might conceal distinct groups. We could not assume that people responded uniformly or invariably shared the same motive. Nor did a negative comment prove hostility.\nWe distinguished reach from penetration into a particular audience. A story could be seen by many people yet understood by few. The result was a useful lesson in public consciousness: exposure does not automatically produce understanding. Before deciding what a message achieves, researchers must ask who encountered it, how they interpreted it, and what evidence supports the conclusion.","zh":"醒目故事传播可能快于核实。项目考察主张跨账号群传播，热门帖后出现率升高，但流行不证明真相，需查事件呈现及编造可能。分析有限制：缺记录可能使结论无效，表面统一模式可能藏不同群体，不能假设人反应一致、动机总相同，负面评论也不证明敌意。我们区分触及人数与在特定受众中的深入程度：多人见却少人懂。公众认知提醒，接触不自动产生理解，评价信息效果要问谁接触、如何解读、证据是什么。","key":"Exposure does not automatically produce understanding. || 简洁因果否定，适合讨论信息、教育和传播。","task":"信息传播广泛，并不意味着它被准确理解。 || Wide circulation of information does not mean that it is accurately understood.","q":"Why was reach distinguished from understanding? || Many people might see a story while few understand it accurately. 接触与理解是不同指标。","note":"","wc":155,"new":["fabrication","consciousness","cluster","circulation","uniformly","subject","representation","negative","propagation","incidence","distinct","penetration","invariably","invalid"]},{"id":"105","title":"度假计划中的取舍","en_title":"Choosing a Short Break","kind":"听力·计划与偏好","en":"My friend wanted to immerse herself in a new place, whilst I preferred a quiet break. We nearly let that contrast become a clash. She proposed a strenuous tramp through hills; I feared the walk would devour our limited time and leave no room to rest.\nWe agreed not to gamble on an unrealistic timetable. A morning visit could precede an afternoon near the coast. I could indulge in reading, while she could explore nearby paths. We would not claim that one preference was more sensible in every case. Nor would we let stubborn insistence turn a holiday into strife.\nThe compromise pleased us both. I learnt that a plan can have direction without being rigid. My friend learnt that rest need not be laziness. Shared travel requires a willingness to embrace another person's priorities without abandoning one's own. A small adjustment can preserve both cooperation and enjoyment.","zh":"朋友想沉浸新地方，我想安静休息，差异险成冲突。她提议山间长途跋涉，我怕耗尽时间不能休息。双方不拿不现实日程冒险，上午参观、下午海边，我享阅读，她走附近小径。不说某偏好总更合理，也不执拗到度假变争斗。折中让两人满意：计划可有方向而不僵硬，休息不一定懒。结伴旅行需接纳他人优先事项而不放弃自身，小调整能保合作与乐趣。","key":"A plan can have direction without being rigid. || without + 动名词，表示目标与灵活性可以兼容。","task":"合作需要认真考虑不同的优先事项。 || Cooperation requires taking different priorities seriously.","q":"What compromise did the friends make? || A morning visit and an afternoon allowing different activities near the coast. 共同计划保留个人空间。","note":"","wc":148,"new":["stubborn","devour","whilst","clash","indulge","gamble","strife","immerse","embrace","tramp"]},{"id":"106","title":"讲清楚而不是说漂亮","en_title":"A Talk That Changed Direction","kind":"写作·表达与逻辑","en":"My first talk was a bore: it sounded elaborate but gave listeners little to use. I had mistaken simplicity for ignorance and filled the slides with vague claims. A peer asked what I actually meant. That commonsense question changed the presentation.\nI removed an improper comparison and explained why one inference was only tentative. Inasmuch as the evidence was incomplete, I could not claim certainty. Notwithstanding that limitation, the project still offered a useful insight. I would not say the result was incredible or doubtless correct merely to impress.\nI also replaced \"male versus female abilities\" with a more precise question about expectations. Describing a role as masculine or feminine did not prove that anyone was naturally suited to it. The improved talk avoided an empty opposition and offered a clear argument. Careful wording can help listeners think rather than simply persuade them to agree.","zh":"首次演讲枯燥：听着精巧却无实用内容。我把简单当无知，幻灯片满空话。同伴问到底什么意思，这个常识问题改变报告。我删不当比较，解释推断暂定。由于证据不全，不能称确定；尽管有限制，仍有启发。不为讨好就说结果不可思议或无疑正确。还把“男女能力对抗”改为更准确的社会期待问题：角色被称男性化或女性化，不证明谁天生适合。好措辞帮助听者思考，而非只劝同意。","key":"Inasmuch as the evidence was incomplete, I could not claim certainty. || inasmuch as 表示因为，较正式；日常作文用 because 也自然。","task":"准确表达比夸大结论更有说服力。 || Accurate expression is more persuasive than overstating a conclusion.","q":"What changed the presentation? || A peer's question about what the speaker actually meant. 清晰问题促成具体化。","note":"inasmuch as / notwithstanding 属较正式表达。清楚自然时，because / despite 往往已经足够。","wc":145,"new":["commonsense","inasmuch","ignorance","doubtless","bore","feminine","peer","incredible","masculine","notwithstanding","improper","versus"]},{"id":"107","title":"记录一个项目的变化","en_title":"Keeping a Useful Project Log","kind":"阅读·连接词与时间","en":"Our project log stated that work was currently behind schedule. Hitherto, the team had relied on informal updates. Henceforth, each member would record progress weekly. The first review identified a delay; subsequently, we revised the timetable. Thereafter, reports became more consistent.\nThe log was useful because it explained decisions, not just dates. A note might say that a change could pose a risk or that a resource was on the verge of running out. Another would explain why an apparently easy solution had proved of no avail. A summary referred to a problem and the lessons contained therein.\nFormal connectors should clarify relationships, not decorate a paragraph. Incidentally, an extra fact belongs only where it helps the reader. A record becomes confusing when every sentence sounds official but no one can tell what happened. The best account lets readers trace a decision, understand its reason, and see what followed.","zh":"项目日志写工作目前落后。此前靠非正式更新，此后每人每周记进展。首轮审查发现延误，随后改时间表，此后报告更一致。日志有用因解释决定不只记日期：变化可能带风险，资源濒临用尽，看似简单方案无效，摘要提到问题及其中教训。正式连接词应说明关系而非装饰。顺带事实只有帮助读者才值得放。每句官腔却不知发生什么只会困惑，最佳记录能追决定、明原因、见后果。","key":"Formal connectors should clarify relationships, not decorate a paragraph. || clarify relationships 可迁移到写作建议；避免堆砌连接词。","task":"好的记录应该清楚说明决定的原因。 || A good record should clearly explain the reasons behind decisions.","q":"Why was the log useful? || It explained decisions rather than merely listing dates. 信息之间有清晰关系。","note":"hitherto、henceforth、thereafter、therein 用于辨认正式文本，写作文不必成串使用。","wc":149,"new":["therein","avail","subsequently","currently","henceforth","incidentally","thereafter","verge","pose"]},{"id":"108","title":"讲述变化的科普作者","en_title":"Explaining Change to the Public","kind":"阅读·科学传播","en":"An author used an elemental example to explain a complex process. A growing plant could originate from a tiny seed, yet its development depended on many conditions. Readers should not confuse a simple starting point with a simple outcome.\nThe author compared the example with a different system, carefully noting where the analogy would deviate from reality. She refused to let a memorable image perplex readers about the underlying science. A spectacular claim might attract attention, but sheer novelty did not make it true.\nThe final chapter urged readers to remain curious. They could marvel at a discovery without attributing it to superstition. They could acknowledge a mystery without assuming that it would remain forever unexplained. Scientific communication succeeds when it preserves wonder while making the limits of knowledge visible. An explanation can be both accessible and intellectually honest.","zh":"作者用基本例子说明复杂过程：植物可来自小种子，但发展依赖多条件，不能把简单起点当简单结果。她谨慎类比另一系统，指出何处偏离现实，不让好记图像混淆科学。惊人主张吸睛，单凭新奇不真。最后鼓励好奇：可赞叹发现而不归迷信，可承认未知而不认永远无法解释。科普在保留惊奇又呈现知识边界时成功，解释能易懂又诚实。","key":"They could acknowledge a mystery without assuming that it would remain forever unexplained. || without + 动名词区分承认未知与断言不可知。","task":"通俗的解释也应该诚实呈现知识的局限。 || An accessible explanation should also present the limits of knowledge honestly.","q":"Why did the author identify limits to the analogy? || To prevent a memorable image from misleading readers. 类比有适用边界。","note":"","wc":139,"new":["marvel","superstition","perplex","elemental","originate","sheer","deviate"]},{"id":"109","title":"压力下的合作","en_title":"Cooperation under Pressure","kind":"写作·团队","en":"Our cooperative project began with vigour. Everyone wanted to move forward, but nobody could foresee every obstacle. When supplies ran short, the leader refused to make a rash promise. We had to wrestle with the schedule and choose tactics that protected quality.\nOne member wanted to head straight into production. Another preferred to wait indefinitely. We chose a middle course: preserve stability and test a small batch. A follower could contribute judgment rather than simply repeat instructions.\nThe experience was unique in its details but familiar in its lesson. Even an enthusiastic group can fall behind when responsibilities remain unclear. We should not leave a gap in planning and hope goodwill will fill the void. Nor should a slack schedule encourage careless work. We must reckon with uncertainty and turn common intentions into specific action.","zh":"合作项目起初充满活力，人人想前进，却无法预见所有困难。物资不足时负责人不轻率承诺，团队认真处理日程难题，选择保质量的策略。一人想直接生产，一人想无限等，我们取中间路：稳住局面、小批测试。跟随者也能贡献判断。细节独特，道理熟悉：职责不清，热情团队也会落后。不能留计划空白再盼善意填补，也不能因日程宽松而粗心。必须考虑不确定性并落实行动。","key":"Even an enthusiastic group can fall behind when responsibilities remain unclear. || even 引出让步，when 说明可能失败的条件。","task":"团队需要把共同目标转化为明确行动。 || A team needs to turn a shared objective into clearly defined actions.","q":"What course did the group choose? || Preserve stability and test a small batch. 在冒进与无限拖延之间取可检验路径。","note":"","wc":135,"new":["foresee","head","slack","forward","unique","reckon","wrestle","rash","follower","void","stability","vigour","cooperative","tactics","fall"]},{"id":"110","title":"从口语走向正式写作","en_title":"Choosing the Right Register","kind":"写作·语域","en":"My sales pitch was full of slang. I said a product would be a hit and invited customers to pop into the shop. Such phrases suited conversation, but a formal report needed greater precision.\nCalling a product positively perfect could conceal a gross exaggeration. A puff of promotional praise was not evidence. Nor should I call a competitor shady because its methods were unfamiliar. Frequent repetition could make a label seem credible without making it fair.\nWe also discussed literally, a word often used loosely in conversation. In formal work its meaning should be clear. An expression described as vulgar may be inappropriate for the audience. Good style means choosing language whose tone and meaning fit the purpose.","zh":"推销话术满俚语，说产品会大受欢迎，邀顾客顺便进店；聊天可用，正式报告需更精确。称产品绝对完美可能严重夸大，宣传吹捧不是证据，不能因陌生就说竞争者可疑。重复使标签似可信，却不使其公平。literally 闲谈常宽泛用，正式写作要清楚；粗俗表达可能不适合读者。好风格意味着语气和意义符合目的。","key":"Frequent repetition could make a label seem credible without making it fair. || make + 宾语 + 动词原形，区分外观可信与公平。","task":"语言风格应该符合目的和读者需要。 || Style should suit the purpose and the needs of its audience.","q":"Why revise casual expressions? || A formal report requires precision and a suitable tone. 表达需适合场景。","note":"puff 指宣传性吹捧。slang、gross、literally 的具体含义需结合语境。","wc":118,"new":["literally","pitch","positively","slang","shady","hit","vulgar","puff","frequent","gross","pop"]},{"id":"111","title":"海边村庄的一天","en_title":"A Day in a Coastal Village","kind":"阅读·场景","en":"A multitude of visitors gathered on the fringe of the village as milky light spread across the bay. Boats moved to and fro, and a path along the hill's flank led to the shore. The morning seemed pacific, yet a notice warned us to beware of changing weather.\nAt noon, a swell appeared offshore. Guides asked people to disperse, except for a group waiting under shelter. One visitor called the precaution senseless. Presumably, he expected calm weather to last; on the contrary, the guide had received an updated forecast.\nWe went indoors to hear local history. Our host used plague to mean a recurring problem, not a current illness. The story helped kindle curiosity. A frightful event showed how people could perish without community support. Responsible travel begins with listening to people who know a place.","zh":"乳白晨光铺海湾，村边聚满游客。船来回行，小径沿山侧通岸。晨间平静，告示却提醒天气变化。中午外海涌浪，导游让人散开，棚下等候组除外。游客称预防无意义，大概以为平静会持续；实际上导游已收新预报。大家进屋听历史，主人用 plague 指反复难题而非现有疾病。故事点燃好奇，其中可怕事件显示缺支持时人们可能丧生。负责旅行始于倾听当地人。","key":"Presumably, he expected calm weather to last. || presumably 标明推测，不能将推测当已证实事实。","task":"游客应该认真对待当地人的提醒。 || Visitors should take local people's advice seriously.","q":"Did plague mean a current illness? || No. It meant a recurring problem. 根据语境识别比喻义。","note":"pacific 在这里取较少见的平静义，普通作文优先用 calm / peaceful；perish 指死亡。","wc":136,"new":["senseless","pacific","plague","fro","presumably","fringe","perish","milky","flank","frightful","contrary","kindle","multitude","except","disperse","swell","beware"]}];